Vegetables,Ash Gourd,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME ASH GOURD FIELD PREPARATION?,"To bring soil to fine tilth, carryout ploughing operation for three-fourth time. Before last ploughing add, well decomposed cowdung@20kg along with neem cake@40kg/acre.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Ash Gourd,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME ASH GOURD SPACING?,"Sow two seeds per hill on one side of bed which is 3 m wide and use spacing of 75-90 cm.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Ash Gourd,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME ASH GOURD SOWING DEPTH?,Sowing Depth: Seeds are sown at depth of 1-2 cm.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Ash Gourd,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME ASH GOURD SOWING METHOD?,"In ash guard, Seeds are directly sown on bed.

","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Ash Gourd,Seeds,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME ASH GOURD SEEDS MANAGEMENT?,"Seed rate of 2 kg is sufficient for one acre land.
To protect seeds from soil borne fungus, treat seeds with Carbendazim@2gm/kg of seeds. After chemical treatment, treat seeds with Trichoderma Viride@4gm/kg of seeds or Pseudomonas fluroscens@10gm/kg of seeds.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Ash Gourd,Seeds,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME ASH GOURD SEEDS TREATMENT?,"To protect seeds from soil borne fungus, treat seeds with Carbendazim@2gm/kg of seeds. After chemical treatment, treat seeds with Trichoderma Viride@4gm/kg of seeds or Pseudomonas fluroscens@10gm/kg of seeds.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Ash Gourd,Fertilizer Uses,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME ASH GOURD BETTER/GOOD/FERTILIZER USE?,"It required Nitrogen@40kg in form of Urea@90kg/acre, Phosphorus@20kg in form of SSP@125kg/acre and Potash@20kg in form of MOP@35kg/acre. Apply half dose of Nitrogen and full dose of Phosphorus and Potash at time of bed preparation. Apply remaining dose of Nitrogen when crop is at flowering stage","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Ash Gourd,Weed Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME ASH GOURD WEED MANAGEMENT?,"Depending upon weed intensity, carry out hand or hoe weeding operation. Mulching is best way to keep check on weed growth along with water saving","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Ash Gourd,Water Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME ASH GOURD WATER MANAGEMENT?,"Depending upon climate, soil type, in summer season provide irrigation with interval of 7-10 days. In rainy season provide irrigation depending upon rainfall frequency.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Ash Gourd,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME LEEF BEETLES CONTROL IN ASH GOURD?,"Leef beetles: If infestation is observed, to controlled take spray of Malathion 50EC@1ml/ltr or Dimethoate 30EC@2ml/lit of water.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Ash Gourd,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME APHID CONTROL IN ASH GOURD?,"Aphid: If infestation is observed, take spray of Imidacloprid@0.5ml/ltr of water.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Ash Gourd,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME POWDERY MILDEW CONTROL IN ASH GOURD?,"Patchy, white powdery growth appear on upper surface of leaves also on main stem of infected plant. It parasitizes the plant using it as a food source. In severe infestation it causes defoliation and premature fruit ripening.
If infestation is observed take spray of Dinocap@1ml/lit or Carbendazim@0.5gm/lit of water.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Ash Gourd,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME DOWNY MILDEW CONTROL IN ASH GOURD?,"Downy mildew: If infestation is observed, take spray of Mancozeb or Chlorothalonil@2gm/ltr of water, two times with 10 days interval.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Ash Gourd,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME ASH GOURD HARVESTING?,"Depending upon variety, crop is ready for harvesting in 90-100 days. Depending upon market requirement, fruits can be harvested at immature or mature stage. Mature fruits are mostly stored for seed production purpose. Cut the fruits from vines with help of sharp knife.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Ash Gourd,Seeds,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME ASH SEEDS PRODUCTION?,"For seed production purpose, sow seeds in February-March month. Disease or unwanted crops are remove at time of flowering, fruiting and maturity stage. When fruits and stem surface give white waxy appearance, fruits are ready for harvesting. Seeds are separated and then wash with water. Wash seeds are dry and then clean before storing. Seeds are store in low temperature and low humidity conditions.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Ash Gourd,Nutrient Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME ASH GOURD FOLIAR APPLICATIONINFORMATION?,5g of Porus mix with water anf apply in the plant.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Ash Gourd,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SUITABLE SOIL FOR ASH GOURD CULTIVATION?,"Ash gourd thrives on all types of soil. But loam, sandy loam and clay loam are best suited for its cultivation. The optimum pH is 6.5-7.5. The land is prepared by ploughing the soil for 3 to 4 times.","[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Ash Gourd,Plant Protection,"INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME APHID , WHITE FLY AND LEAF CATERPILLAR CONTROL MANAGEMENT IN ASH GOURD?",Spray 1.5 ml of water in Cibron with a liter of water.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Ash Gourd,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME ASH GOURD MATURITY INDEX DETAIL?,"The fruit of the skin and the flesh will change, the pale yellow color will change and the stem will be contraction, and the fruit will be a normal sound.","[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Ash Gourd,Nutrient Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME NECESSARY NUTRITION OF ASH GOURD?,"NITROGEN--40kg/acre, PHOSPHORUS --20kg/acre, POTASH--20 kg/acre
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Ash Gourd,Fertilizer Uses,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FERTILIZER REQUIREMENT IN ASH GOURD?,"UREA--90kg/acre, SSP--135kg/acre,MURIATE OF POTASH--35 kg/acre
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME TOMATO CROP?,"Tomato is originated in Peru of South America. It is important commercial vegetable crop of India. It is the second most important crop of world after potato. Fruits are eaten raw or in cooked form. It is rich source of vitamin A, C, potassium and minerals. It is used in soup, juice and ketch up, powder. The major tomato producing states are Bihar, Karnataka, Uttar Pradesh, Orissa, Maharashtra, Andhra Pradesh, Madhya Pradesh and West Bengal. In Punjab state, Amritsar, Ropar, Jalandhar, Hoshiarpur are tomato growing districts.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME TOMATO SOWING TIME?,"For northern state, tomato cultivation for spring season is done in late November and transplanted in second fortnight of January. For autumn crop, sowing is done in July - August and transplanted in August - September. In hilly areas sowing is done in March- April and transplantation is done in April -May.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME TOMATO SUITABLE TIME?,"For northern state, tomato cultivation for spring season is done in late November and transplanted in second fortnight of January. For autumn crop, sowing is done in July - August and transplanted in August - September. In hilly areas sowing is done in March- April and transplantation is done in April -May.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
