Vegetables,Tomato,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME TOMATO VARIETIEY PUNJAB NR -7?,Dwarf variety having medium size juicy fruits. It is highly resistant to fusarium wilt and root knot nematodes. Gives average yield of 175-180qtl/acre.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME TOMATO VARIETIEY PUNJAB RED CHERRY?,"Developed by Punjab Agricultural University. These cherry tomatoes are used in salads. These are of deep red color and in future it will be available in yellow, orange and pink color. Sowing is done in August or September and plant is ready to harvest in February and gives yield up to July. Its early yield is 150 qtl/acre and total yield is 430-440 qtl per acre.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME TOMATO VARIETIEY PUNJAB VARKHA BAHAR 2?,"Ready to harvest in 100days after transplanting. It is resistant to leaf curl virus. Gives average yield of 215 qtl/acre.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME TOMATO VARIETIEY PUNJAB VARKHA BAHAR 1?,"After transplanting, ready to harvest in 90days. It is suitable for sowing in rainy season. It gives resistance to leaf curl virus. Gives average yield of 215qtl/acre.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME TOMATO VARIETIEY PUNJAB SONA CHERRY?,Released in 2016. It gives an average yield of 425qtl/acre. The fruits are yellow in color and bears in bunches. The average weight of the fruit is approximately 11gm. It contains 7.5% sucrose content.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME TOMATO VARIETIEY PUNJAB KESARI CHERRY?,"Released in 2016. It gives an average yield of 405qtl/acre. The average weight of the fruit is approximately 11gm. It contains 7.6% sucrose content.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME TOMATO VARIETIEY PUNJAB KESAR CHERRY?,"Released in 2016. It gives an average yield of 405qtl/acre. The average weight of the fruit is approximately 11gm. It contains 7.6% sucrose content.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME TOMATO VARIETIEY PUNJAB VARKHA BAHAR-4?,Released in 2015. It gives an average yield of 245qtl/acre. It contains 3.8% sucrose content.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME TOMATO VARIETIEY PUNJAB GAURAV?,"Released in 2015. It gives an average yield of 934qtl/acre. It contains 5.5% sucrose content.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME TOMATO VARIETIEY TH-1?,"Released in 2003. The fruits are dark red in color, round hard and approximately 85gm weight. It gives an average yield of 245qtl/acre.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME TOMATO VARIETIEY PUNJAB SWARNA?,Released in 2018. It has dark green color foliage. It has oval shaped fruits which is orange in color and medium in size. First picking should be done after 120 days of transplanting. It gives an average yield of 166qtl/acre till end-March and gives total yield of 1087qtl/acre. The variety is suitable for table purpose.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME TOMATO VARIETIEY HS 101?,Suitable for growing in north India during winter condition. Plants are dwarf. Fruits are round and medium size and juicy. Fruits are borne in cluster. It is resistant to Tomato Leaf Curl Virus.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME TOMATO VARIETIEY HS 102?,"Early maturing variety. Fruits are small to medium in size, round and juicy.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME TOMATO VARIETIEY SWARNA BAIBHAV HYBRID?,"Recommended for cultivation in Punjab, Uttarakhand, Jharkhand, Bihar and Uttar Pradesh. It is sown in September- October. Fruits keeping quality is good so suitable for long distance transport and processing. Gives yield of 360-400qtl/acre.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME TOMATO VARIETIEY SWARNA SAMPADA HYBRID?,"Recommended for cultivation in Punjab, Uttarakhand, Jharkhand, Bihar and Uttar Pradesh. Suitable timing for sowing is August - September and February-May. It is resistant to bacterial wilt and early blight. It gives yield of 400-420qtl/acre.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME TOMATO VARIETIEY KEEKRUTH?,"Plant height is about 100cm. Ready to harvest in 136days. Fruits are medium to large size, round shape, deep red color.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME TOMATO VARIETIEY KEEKRUTH AGETI?,"Plant height is about 100cm. Fruits are medium to large size, round shape having green shoulder which disappears on ripening.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME TOMATO VARIETIEY PUNJAB SARTAJ?,"Released in 209. It has round shape fruit, moderate and hard. Suitable for rainy season. It gives an average yield of 898qtl/acre. 
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME TOMATO FIELD PREPARATION?,"For tomato plantation, it required well pulverise and levelled soil. To bring soil to fine tilth, plough land for 4-5times, then planking is done to make soil level. At time of last ploughing add well decomposed cow dung and Carbofuron@5kg or Neem cake@8kg per acre should be applied. Transplantation of tomato is done on raised bed. For that prepared raised bed of 80-90cm width. To destroy harmful soil borne pathogen, pest and organism, soil solarization is carried out. It can be done by using transparent plastic film as mulch. This sheet absorb radiation and thus increases soil temperature and kill pathogen.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME TOMATO NURSERY MANAGEMENT AND TRANSPLANTING?,"Do solarization for one month before sowing. Sow tomato seeds on raised beds of 80-90cm width and of convenient length. After sowing covered bed with mulch and irrigate bed with Rose-Can daily in morning. To protect crop from virus attack cover nursery bed with fine nylon net.

10-15days after transplanting sprayed 19:19:19 along with micronutrients@2.5 to 3gm/Ltr of water. To make plants healthier and stronger and to harden seedling against transplanting sock take spray of Lihocin@1ml/Ltr water at 20days after sowing. Damping Off damages crop to great extent, to prevent crop from it avoid overcrowding of seedlings and keep soil wet. If wilting is observed, do drenching of Metalaxyl@2.5gm/Ltr water, 2-3 times till plants are ready for transplantation.

Seedling is ready for transplantation 25 to 30days after sowing with 3-4leaves. In case if seedlings age is more than 30days transplant it after de-toping. Water seedling beds 24hours before transplanting so that seedlings can be easily uprooted and be turgid at transplanting time.

To protect crop from bacterial wilt, dip seedlings in 100ppm Streptocycline solution for 5 minutes before transplanting.

","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME TOMATO SPACING?,"Spacing: Depending upon variety use and its growth habit, use spacing of 60x30cm or 75x60cm or 75x75cm. In Punjab, for dwarf variety use spacing of 75cm x 30cm and for rainy season use spacing of 120-150 x 30cm.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME TOMATO SOWING DEPTH?,"Sowing Depth: In nursery sow seeds at depth of 4cm and then covered with soil. 
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME TOMATO SOWING METHOD?,Method of sowing: Transplanting of seedling in main field.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Seeds,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME TOMATO SEEDS MANAGEMENT?,"Seed Rate:
Use seed rate of 100gm for preparing seedling for sowing in one acre land.
Seed Treatment:
To protect crop from soil borne disease and pest, before sowing do seed treatment with Thiram@3gm or Carbendazim @ 3gm of seeds. After chemical treatment, treat seed with Trichoderma@5gm/kg of seeds. keep it in shade. And use it for sowing.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Seeds,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME TOMATO SEEDS TREATMENT?,"To protect crop from soil borne disease and pest, before sowing do seed treatment with Thiram@3gm or Carbendazim @ 3gm of seeds. After chemical treatment, treat seed with Trichoderma@5gm/kg of seeds. keep it in shade. And use it for sowing.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Fertilizer Uses,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME TOMATO BETTER/GOOD/FERTILIZER USE?,"At the time of land preparation, apply well rotten cow dung@10ton/acre and mix well in the soil. Apply fertilizer dose of N:P:K @60:25:25kg/acre in form of Urea@130kg/acre, Single Super Phosphate@155kg/acre and MOP@45kg/acre. Apply half dose of Nitrogen, full dose of Phosphorus and Potash applied as basal dose, apply it before transplanting. 20 to 30days after transplantation apply remaining 1/4th dose of nitrogen. Two month after transplantation, apply remaining dose of Urea.

WSF: 10-15days after transplanting, take spray of 19:19:19 along with micronutrient@2.5 to 3gm/ltr of water. Due to low temperature, plant absorbs fewer nutrients and growth get affected. In such cases foliar spray helps in growth of plants. In vegetative growth stage take spray of 19:19:19 or 12:61:00 @ 4-5 gm/Ltr. For better growth and more yield, spray with 50ml Brassinolide per acre in 150ltr of water at 40-50 days after transplanting for two times at 10days intervals.

Obtain good fruit quality along with good yield, take spray of 12:61:00 (Mono Ammonium Phosphate)@10 gm/Ltr before flowering. When flowering starts in initial days, take spray of Boron@25gm/10litre of water. It will help to control flower and fruit dropping. Sometime black spots are observed on fruits, these are due to calcium deficiency. Take spray of calcium nitrate@2gm/ltr of water. In high temperature flower drop is seen, spray with NAA@50 ppm (50ml/10L water) when crop is in flowering stage. Give one spray of sulphate of potash (00:00:50+18S) during fruit development stage@3-5 gm/ltr of water. It will give good fruit development and colour. Fruit cracking reduces fruit quality and lowers prices up to 20%. Take spray of chelated boron (Solubor)@200gm/acre/200Ltr water at fruit ripening stage. To improve plant growth, flowering and fruit set, spray with sea weed extract (Biozyme/Dhanzyme)@3-4 ml/Ltr water twice a month. Maintain good soil moisture.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Weed Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME TOMATO WEED MANAGEMENT?,"Do frequent weeding, hoeing and earthing up and keep field weed free till 45 days. If weed left uncontrolled then it will reduce crop yield upto 70-90%. Two to three days of after transplantation take spray of Fluchloralin (Basalin) @800ml/200Ltr water as pre-emergence weedicide. If weed intensity is high, take post emergence spray of Sencor@300g/acre. Mulching is also an effective way to reduce soil temperature along with weed control.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Water Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME TOMATO WATER MANAGEMENT?,"In winter, apply irrigation with interval of 6 to 7days and in summer month, apply with interval of 10-15days depending upon soil moisture. Period of drought follow by heavy watering leads to cracking of fruits. Flowering stage is critical for irrigation, water stress during this stage can leads to flower drop and adversely affecting fruiting and productivity. According to various researches, it is found that, half inch irrigation at every fortnight causes maximum penetration of roots and thus gives high yield.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME LEAF MINER CONTROL IN TOMATO?,"Maggots of leaf miner feed on leaf and make serpentine mines into leaf. It affects the photosynthesis and fruit formation.
At initial stage, take spray of Neem Seed Kernel Extract@5%, 50gm/Ltr of water. To control leaf miner, spray with Dimethoate 30EC@250ml or Spinosad@80ml in 200Ltr of water or Triazophos@200ml/200Ltr of water.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WHITE FLY CONTROL IN TOMATO?,"The nymphs and adults of white fly suck the cell sap from the leaves and weaken the plants. They secrete honey dew on which black sooty mould develops on leaves. They also transmit leaf curl diseases.
After sowing of seeds in nursery, cover bed with 400mesh nylon net or thin white cloth. It helps to protect seedlings from pest-disease attack. To check infestation use yellow sticky traps coated with grease and sticky oils. To control spread of whiteflies, uproot and destroy affected plants. In case of severe infestation, take spray of Acetamiprid 20SP@80gm/200Ltr of water or Triazophos@250ml/200litre or Profenophos@200ml/200litre of water. Repeat the spray after 15 days.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME THRIPS CONTROL IN TOMATO?,"Commonly observed pest. Mostly observed in dry weather. They suck sap from the foliage and results in curling of leaves, leaves become cup shaped or curved upward. Also causes flower drop.
To check severity of thrips incidence, keep blue sticky traps @6-8 per acre. Also to reduce the incidence of this disease, spray Verticillium lecani@5gm/Ltr water. If incidence of thrips is more, then take spray of Imidacloprid 17.8SL @60ml or Fipronil@200ml/200Ltr of water or Acephate 75% WP@600 gm/200Ltr or Spinosad@80ml/acre in 200Ltr water.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME GRAM POD BORER OR HELIOTHIS ARMIGERA CONTROL IN TOMATO?,"It is a major pest of tomato. Crop loss due to Helicoverpa is about 22-37% if not controlled at proper stage. It feeds on leaves also on flower and fruits. On fruits they make circular holes and feed on flesh.
In case of initial infestation, handpicked grown up larvae. At early stage use HNPV or Neem extract@50gm/Litre of water. To control fruit borer, put 16 pheromone traps/acre at equal distance after 20 days of transplanting. Change lure in every 20 days interval. Destroy infested parts. If pest population is high, spray Spinosad@80ml+sticker@400ml/200Ltr of water. To control shoot and fruit borer, spray Rynaxypyr(Coragen)@60ml/200Ltr water.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME MITE CONTROL IN TOMATO?,"Mite is a serious pest and it may cause yield loss up to 80%. These are widely distributed pest observed throughout the world. It attacks on several crops like potato, chilli, beans, cotton, tobacco, curcurbit, castor, jute, coffee, lemon, citrus, blackgram, cowpea, pepper, tomato, sweet potato, mango, papaya, brinjal, guava. Nymphs and adults feed exclusively on the lower surface of the leaves. Infected leaves give cup shape appearance. Heavy infestation results in defoliation bud shedding and drying of leaves.
If Infestation of yellow mite & thrips is observed in field, spray of Chlorfenapyr@15ml/10Ltr, Abamectin@15ml/10Ltr or Fenazaquin @100ml/100Ltr are found effective. For effective control spray Spiromesifen 22.9SC(Oberon)@200ml/acre/180Ltr of water.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FRUIT ROT CONTROL IN TOMATO?,"Major disease of tomato and observed due to changing weather. Water soaked lesions are appeared on fruits. Afterwards they turn into black or brown color and causing rotting of fruits.
Before sowing, do seed treatment with Tricoderma@5-10gm or Carbendazim@2gm or Thiram@3 gm/Kg of seeds. If infection observed in field collect and destroy infected fruit and leaves which lies on ground. Fruit rot and anthracnose attacked mostly observed in cloudy weather, to control take spray of Mancozeb@400gm or Copper Oxychloride@300gm or Chlorothalonil@250gm/200Ltr water. Repeat spray with 15 days interval.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME ANTHRACNOSE CONTROL IN TOMATO?,"Warm temperatures, high moisture are ideal condition for spread of this disease. It is characterized by black spots that are formed on infected parts. Spots are usually circular, water-soaked and sunken with black margins. The fruits with many spots drop off prematurely resulting in heavy loss of yield.
If Infestation of Anthracnose is observed. To control this disease, spraying of Propiconazole or Hexaconazole@200ml/200Ltr of water should be done.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME EARLY BLIGHT CONTROL IN TOMATO?,"Common and major disease of tomato. Initially small, brown isolated spots are observed on leaf. Later spots are seen on stem and also on fruits. Fully developed spots become irregular, dark brown color with concentric ring inside spots. In severe condition, defoliation occurred.
If infestation of early blight is observed, take spray of Mancozeb@400gm or Tabuconazol@200ml/200Ltr. Repeat spray 10-15 days after first spray. In cloudy weather, chances of incidence of early and late blight increases. As a preventive measure, spray with Chlorothalonil@250gm/100Ltr of water. Also sudden rain pattern aggravate blight and other diseases take spray of Copper based fungicides@300gm/Ltr+Streptocycline@6gm/200Ltr water to control blight disease.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WILT AND DAMPING OFF CONTROL IN TOMATO?,"Moist and poorly drain soil causes damping off disease. It is soil borne disease. Water soaking and shriveling of stem occurs. Seedlings killed before emergence. If it appears in nursery the entire lot of seedling may get destroyed.
To prevent root rot, drench soil with 1% Urea@100gm/10Ltr and Copper oxychloride @250gm/200Ltr water. To control wilt, drench nearby soil with Copper oxychloride@250gm or Carbendazim@400gm/200Ltr of water. Increased temperature and humidity due to watering facilitate fungal growth at roots, to overcome it, apply Trichoderma 2 kg/acre along with cow dung near roots of plants. To control soil born disease, drench soil with Carbendazim@1gm/Ltr or Bordo mix@10gm/ltr, 1 month after that apply 2 kg Trichoderma /acre, mixed with 100kg cow dung.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME POWDERY MILDEW CONTROL IN TOMATO?,"Patchy, white powdery growth appears on lower side of leaves. It parasitizes the plant using it as a food source. It commonly occurs on older leaves just before or at fruit set. But it can develop at any stage of crop development. In severe infestation it causes defoliation.
Avoid water lodging in field. Keep field clean. To control this disease, spraying with Hexaconazole along with sticker @1ml/Ltr of water should be done. In case of sudden rain, chances of powdery mildew is more. Mild infestation takes spray of water soluble sulphur@ 20gm/10Ltr of water 2-3 times with interval of 10 days.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME HARVESTING IN TOMATO?,"Plant starts yielding by 70days after transplantation. Harvesting is done depending upon purpose like for fresh market, long distance transport etc. Mature green tomatoes, 1/4th fruits portion gives pink color are harvested for long distance markets. Almost all fruits turn into pink or red color but having firm flesh are harvested for local markets. For processing and seed extraction purpose, fully ripe fruits with soft flesh are used.After harvesting, grading is done. Then fruits are packed in bamboo baskets or crates or wooden boxes. To increase self-life of tomato during long distance transport pre-cooling is carried out. From ripen tomatoes several products like Puree, syrup, juice and ketch up are made after processing.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF VIRUS IN TOMATO?,Remove diseased tomato plants from the field and spray 400 ml of Melathion (to control whitefly) in 100 liters of water per acre to prevent disease spread.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF INSECT PEST IN CUCURBITS IN KITCHEN GARDEN?,Spray 10 ml nimbecidine per liters of water to control sucking pest in bottle gourd or kitchen garden.," [Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF APHIDS IN TOMATO?,"For aphids control in tomato crop, spray 400 ml of Melathion (to control oil and whitefly) or 300 ml of Roger 30 EC (dimethoate) mixed with 100 liters of water for one acre."," [Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FROST DAMAGE CONTROL OF TOMATO CROP?,"To protect the tomato crop from blight, cover the soil and apply light water.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FLOWER DROP CONTROL IN TOMATO?,Apply plano fix 4 ml / 15 liters of water should be sprayed,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME YELLOWING CONTROL IN TOMATO?,Spray Roco 15 g/15 liter of water (Thiophinate Methyl 70 % WDG)," [Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME LEAF EATING CATTERPILLAR CONTROL IN TOMATO?,Spray Nuvan 20 ml/15 liters of water (Dichlorvos 76% EC),"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FRUIT BORER CONTROL IN TOMATO CROP?,For control of fruit borer in tomato crop - Spray with Corazan 5 ml/15 liters of water.(Chloranthraniliprol 15.8% EC) DuPont.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SUCKING PEST ATTACK CONTROL IN TOMATO CROP?,For control of sap-sucking insects on tomato crop - Actra (Thiomithosome 25%) should be sprayed with 5 gm/15 liter of water.," [Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CUTWORM ATTACK CONTROL IN TOMATO CROP?,For cutworm control in tomato crop - Deltamethrin 100 EC (11% w/w) 200-250 ml + Chlorpyrifos 50% + Cypermethrin 5% EC. 500 ml per acre should be released by drip.Also Chlorpyrifos 50% + Cypermethrin 5% EC. Spray with 30 ml / 15 liters of water.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FUNGUS CONTROL IN TOMATO CROP?,"Add a heaping tablespoon of baking soda, a teaspoon of vegetable oil, and a small amount of mild soap to a gallon of water and spray the tomato plants with this solution. This needs to be reapplied regularly to maintain its efficiency.","[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME DELEGATE PROPORTION FOR TOMATO?,Delegate spray should be done at the rate of 5 ml,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CATERPILLER TOMATO?,Prophex 30 ml + thiomethozone-5g/15 liters of water should be taken and sprayed. (Profenofos 40 %) should be mixed with 10 liters of water and sprayed.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME YELLOWING OF TOMATO?,Mikrolla should be sprayed at 30 ml /15 liters of water.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME PREVENT SOIL BORN PATHOGEN IN TOMATO CROP?,"1 kg of pseudomonas, 1 kg trigoderma, 1 kg of cow dung fertilizer, 25 kg per acre.","[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Nutrient Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME TOP DRESSING FERTILIZER (HYBRID) MANAGEMENT?,Urea 42 kg + potash 33 kg / acre.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FLOWER SHED MANAGEMENT IN TOMATO?,Spray 2 ml of plynofix with 10 liters of water.," [Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Nutrient Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME NECESSARY NUTRITION OF TOMATO?,"NITROGEN--60kg/acre, PHOSPHORUS --25kg/acre, POTASH--25 kg/acre
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Tomato,Fertilizer Uses,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FERTILIZER REQUIREMENT IN TOMATO?,"UREA--130kg/acre, SSP--155kg/acre,MURIATE OF POTASH--45 kg/acre
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sweet Potato,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SWEET POTATO CROP?,"The botanical name of Sweet potato is Ipomoea batatas. This crop is mainly grown because of its sweet taste and starchy roots. The tubers are rich source of beta-carotene and are used as anti-oxidants. It is an herbaceous perennial vine having lobed or heart shaped leaves. Its tubers are edible, smooth skin, tapered and long. It has wide color range of tuber skin i.e. purple, brown, white and purple which contains wide range of flesh i.e. yellow, orange, white and purple. In India about 2 lakh of land is under cultivation of sweet potatoes. In Bihar, West Bengal, Uttar Pradesh and Orissa are the major growing states in India.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sweet Potato,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SWEET POTATO SOWING TIME?,"For optimum yield, tubers should be sown in nursery beds in the month of January to February and the optimum time for planting vines in the field is in the month of April to July.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sweet Potato,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SWEET POTATO SUITABLE TIME?,"For optimum yield, tubers should be sown in nursery beds in the month of January to February and the optimum time for planting vines in the field is in the month of April to July.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sweet Potato,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SWEET POTATO SUITABLE TEMPARATURE?,"The suitable temparature: Sowing Temparature- 12-15 degree, Normal Temperature- 26-30 degree,Harvesting Temperature- 15-20 degree,Rainfall- 300-600cm","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sweet Potato,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SWEET POTATO SOWING TEMPARATURE?,Sowing Temparature- 12-15 degree,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sweet Potato,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SWEET POTATO NORMAL TEMPARATURE?,Normal Temperature- 26-30 degree,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sweet Potato,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SWEET POTATO HARVESTING TEMPARATURE?,Harvesting Temperature- 15-20 degree,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sweet Potato,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SWEET POTATO RAINFALL?,Rainfall- 300-600cm,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sweet Potato,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SWEET POTATO SOIL MANAGEMENT?,"It is grown in variety of soil types ranging from sandy to loamy soil, but it gives best result when grown under sandy loam soil having high fertility and good drainage system. Avoid cultivation of sweet potato in very light sandy and heavy clayey soil as it is not good for tuber development. It requires pH ranging from 5.8-6.7 is best for sweet potato cultivation.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sweet Potato,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SWEET POTATO VARIETIES?,"Punjab Sweet Potato-21: The vines of this variety are medium long in length. It has broad shape and dark green color leaves, long and thick stem, 4.5cm inter nodal length and has 9cm petiole length. It contains deep red color tubers having white flesh which is 20cm long and 4cm wide. The variety gets mature within 145 days. The average weight of tuber is 75g. The tuber contains 35% of dry matter and 81mg/g of starch. It gives an average yield of 75 qtl/acre.
Varsha: It is recommended to grown in Maharashtra. It is suitable to grown in rainy season. It gives an average yield of 62.5 qtl/acre.

Konkan Ashwini: This variety is developed to be cultivated in Maharashtra. It is short duration crop and gives high yield.

Sree Arun: It is an early maturing variety having pink color skin and cream color flesh. The variety is developed by Central Tuber Crop Research Institute (CTCRI), Sreekariyam. It gives an average yield of 83-116 qtl/acre.

Sree Kanaka: The variety is developed by Central Tuber Crop Research Institute (CTCRI), Sreekariyam. It has cream color skin tuber which has dark orange color inner flesh. It gives an average yield of 41-62.5 qtl/acre.

Sree Varun: The variety is developed by Central Tuber Crop Research Institute (CTCRI), Sreekariyam. It contains cream color skin of the tuber. It is an early maturing variety which gets mature within 90-100 days. It gives an average yield of 80-110 qtl/acre.

Improved varieties:

H-41, H-42, Co 3, Co CIP 1, Sree Vardhini, Sree Rethna, Sree Bhadra, Sree Nandini, Kanjanghad, Gouri, Sankar and Kiran.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sweet Potato,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SWEET POTATO VARIETIEY PUNJAB SWEET POTATO-21?,"The vines of this variety are medium long in length. It has broad shape and dark green color leaves, long and thick stem, 4.5cm inter nodal length and has 9cm petiole length. It contains deep red color tubers having white flesh which is 20cm long and 4cm wide. The variety gets mature within 145 days. The average weight of tuber is 75g. The tuber contains 35% of dry matter and 81mg/g of starch. It gives an average yield of 75 qtl/acre.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sweet Potato,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SWEET POTATO VARIETIEY VARSHA?,"It is recommended to grown in Maharashtra. It is suitable to grown in rainy season. It gives an average yield of 62.5 qtl/acre.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sweet Potato,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SWEET POTATO VARIETIEY KONKAN ASHWINI?,This variety is developed to be cultivated in Maharashtra. It is short duration crop and gives high yield.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sweet Potato,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SWEET POTATO VARIETIEY SREE ARUN?,"It is an early maturing variety having pink color skin and cream color flesh. The variety is developed by Central Tuber Crop Research Institute (CTCRI), Sreekariyam. It gives an average yield of 83-116 qtl/acre.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sweet Potato,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SWEET POTATO VARIETIEY SREE KANAKA?,"The variety is developed by Central Tuber Crop Research Institute (CTCRI), Sreekariyam. It has cream color skin tuber which has dark orange color inner flesh. It gives an average yield of 41-62.5 qtl/acre.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sweet Potato,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SWEET POTATO VARIETIEY SREE VARUN?,"The variety is developed by Central Tuber Crop Research Institute (CTCRI), Sreekariyam. It contains cream color skin of the tuber. It is an early maturing variety which gets mature within 90-100 days. It gives an average yield of 80-110 qtl/acre.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sweet Potato,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SWEET POTATO IMPROVED VARIETIES?,"H-41, H-42, Co 3, Co CIP 1, Sree Vardhini, Sree Rethna, Sree Bhadra, Sree Nandini, Kanjanghad, Gouri, Sankar and Kiran.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sweet Potato,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SWEET POTATO FIELD PREPARATION?,"For sweet potato plantation, the land should be well prepared. To bring the soil to the fine tilth, before sowing land must be ploughed 3-4 times followed by planking. The field should be weed-free.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sweet Potato,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SWEET POTATO SOWING METHOD?,"Mainly propagation is done by tubers or vine cuttings. In vine cutting method (commonly used), the tubers are taken from the old vines and planted on prepared nursery beds. Mainly vines are planted in ridges or on prepared flat beds. It is seen that terminal cuttings gives better result. The host plant must have at least 4 nodes. Row spacing of 60cm and within row spacing of 30cm is used. Before planting it is better to treat the cuttings with DDT 50% solution for 8-10 minutes.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sweet Potato,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SWEET POTATO SOWING DEPTH?,Sowing depth:Use depth of 20-25cm for tuber planting.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sweet Potato,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SWEET POTATO SPACING?,"Spacing: Use row to row spacing of 60cm and plant to plant spacing of 30cm.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sweet Potato,Seeds,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SWEET POTATO SEEDS MANAGEMENT?,"Seed rate:
Use 25,000-30,000 of vines cutting in per acre land. Sowing of 35-40kg tubers in half a kanal land is done for raising vines in February to March month. Vines are then planted in the main fields in one acre land.

Seed treatment:
Place the tubers in plastic bag and then soak them in concentrated sulphuric acid for 10-40 minutes.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sweet Potato,Seeds,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SWEET POTATO SEEDS TREATMENT?,Seed treatment:Place the tubers in plastic bag and then soak them in concentrated sulphuric acid for 10-40 minutes.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sweet Potato,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SWEET POTATO ROTATION?,Sweet potato + Rice crop rotation can be taken up successfully under irrigated conditions. Sweet potato can be planted in the month of December-January after second harvesting of rice.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sweet Potato,Fertilizer Uses,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SWEET POTATO BETTER/GOOD/FERTILIZER USE S?,"Apply FYM (Farm Yard Manure) @100 qtl/acre. Along with FYM apply fertilizer dose in terms of CAN @125 kg/acre, SSP @155 kg/acre and MOP @35 kg/acre.Full dose of K2O and P2O5 is applied at the time of planting. Nitrogen dose is applied in 2 splits i.e. first at the time of planting and secondly should be applied after 5 weeks of planting.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sweet Potato,Weed Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SWEET POTATO WEED MANAGEMENT?,Apply Metribuzine 70WP@200gm per acre or Alachlor@2Ltr per acre before sprouts emergence. On 5-10% sprout emergence and ridge are infested with weeds then only apply Paraquat@500-750ml per acre.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sweet Potato,Water Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SWEET POTATO WATER MANAGEMENT?,"After planting, irrigation is given once in 2 days for period of 10 days and thereafter irrigation is given once in 7-10 days. Irrigation must be stopped before 3 weeks of harvesting. But before 2 days of harvesting one irrigation is necessary.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sweet Potato,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME BLACK SCURF CONTROL IN SWEET POTATO?,"Black speck observed on tubers. Affected plant show drying up. In infected tubers, at time of sprouting, black, brown color appear on eyes.
For planting use diseased free tubers. Before sowing, seed treatment with Mercury is essential. Avoid mono-cropping and follow crop rotation. If land kept fallow for two years then severity of disease is reduced.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sweet Potato,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME EARLY BLIGHT CONTROL IN SWEET POTATO?,"Necrotic spots observed on lower leaves. The fungus due which infestation occurred lies in soil. It rapidly spread in high moisture and low temperature.
Avoid mono-cropping of crop and follow crop rotation. If infestation is observed, take spray of Mancozeb@30gm or Copper oxychloride@30gm/10Ltr water at 45 days 2-3 times at 10 days interval.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sweet Potato,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME COMMON SCAB CONTROL IN SWEET POTATO?,"It survives in field as well as in storage. Disease is spread rapidly in low moisture condition. Light brown to dark brown lesion are appeared on infected tubers.
Use only well rotten cow dung for application in field. Use diseased free seeds for planting. Avoid deep planting of tubers. Follow crop rotation and avoid mono cropping in same field. Before sowing, treat seeds with Emisan 6@0.25% (2.5gm/Ltr of water) for five minutes.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sweet Potato,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SWEET POTATO WEEVILS CONTROL?,"
They damage the plant by feeding themselves on the epidermis of vines and leaves.
Treatment: To control weevils spray of 200 ml Rogor @150 ltr water per acre.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sweet Potato,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME APHID CONTROL IN SWEET POTATO?,"Adult and nymphs, both suck the sap thus weaken the plant. In severe infestation, they cause curling and deformation of young leaves. They secrete honey dew like substance and Sooty, black mould is developed on affected parts.
Cut the foliage according region timing, to check infestation of Aphid. If Infestation of Aphid and Jassid observed take spray of Imidacloprid@50ml or Thiamethoxam@40gm/acre/150Ltr water.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sweet Potato,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME TUBER MOTH CONTROL IN SWEET POTATO?,"It is major pest in field as well as in storage. It make tunnel in potato and feeds on flesh. Use healthy and diseased free seeds for sowing. Use only well decomposed cow dung.
If infestation is observed take spray of Carbaryl@400gm/100ltr of water.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sweet Potato,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME HARVESTING IN SWEET POTATO?,The crops get mature after 120 days of planting. Harvesting is mainly done when tubers get mature and the leaves turn yellow. Harvesting is done by digging tubers. It gives an average yield of 100 qtl/acre. Freshly harvested tubers are ready for market purposes.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sweet Potato,Nutrient Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME NECESSARY NUTRITION OF SWEET POTATO?,"NITROGEN--30kg/acre, k2o --20kg/acre, p2o5--25 kg/acre
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sweet Potato,Fertilizer Uses,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FERTILIZER REQUIREMENT IN SWEET POTATO?,"UREA--125kg/acre, SSP--155kg/acre,MURIATE OF POTASH--35 kg/acre
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sponge Gourd,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SPONGE GOURD CROP?,"It is also known as uffasponge gourd. The vines of sponge gourd attain the height of 30 feet or more. The fruits of sponge gourd are cylindrical in shape and outer skin is smooth green. The fruit contains white inner flesh which is fibrous and have similar flavor to bitter melon. The fruit attains the height of 1-2 feet. Fully ripened sponge gourd contains high fiber content which is used as cleansing agent and for making table mats, shoe-soles etc. It is a good source of Vitamin A and C. It is used to cure jaundice, diabetes, to purify blood, and is used to cure skin diseases. In India it is grown in Punjab, Bihar, U.P., Delhi, Gujarat, Haryana, Rajasthan and Jharkhand.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sponge Gourd,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOWING TIME OF SPONGE GOURD CROP?,The seeds are sown twice in the year. The ideal time for sowing is in the month of mid-February to March and second time in the month of mid-May to July.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sponge Gourd,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SUITABLE TIME OF SPONGE GOURD CROP?,The seeds are sown twice in the year. The ideal time for sowing is in the month of mid-February to March and second time in the month of mid-May to July.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sponge Gourd,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SUITABLE TEMPARATURE OF SPONGE GOURD CROP?,The suitable temparature: 25-28 degree,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sponge Gourd,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOIL MANAGEMENT OF SPONGE GOURD CROP?,It is grown in variety of soil types. It gives best result when grown in sandy loam soil. The pH value of soil ranges from 6.5-7.0 or neutral to slightly alkaline soil is good for plantation.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sponge Gourd,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FIELD PREPARATION OF SPONGE GOURD CROP?,"To bring the soil to the fine tilth and to make the field weed free, ploughings are required. At the time of ploughing add Farm Yard Manure (FYM) in the field for the good yield. FYM @84qtl in per acre of land is added for quality crop production.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sponge Gourd,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SPACING OF SPONGE GOURD CROP?,"Spacing: Sow two seeds per hill which is 3m wide and use spacing of 75-90cm between seeds.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sponge Gourd,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOWING DEPTH OF SPONGE GOURD CROP?,Sowing depth: Seeds are sown at the depth of 2.5-3cm.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sponge Gourd,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME METHOD OF SOWING OF SPONGE GOURD CROP?,Method of sowing: Dibbling method is used.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sponge Gourd,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME HARVESTING OF SPONGE GOURD CROP?,Crops are ready for harvesting after 70-80 days of sowing. Carry out picking at the interval of 3-4 days. Harvesting of tender and medium sized fruits should be done. It gives an average yield of 66-83 qtl per acre.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sponge Gourd,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME NURSERY MANAGEMENT AND TRANSPLANTING OF SPONGE GOURD CROP?,"Seeds are sown on prepared nursery beds. Avoid seedbeds to touch the ground to protect them from soil-borne diseases. Transplanting is mainly done after 25-30 days of sowing having 4-5 leaves on the seedling.
Seedlings are planted at the distance of 2.5 x 1.2m between rows and plants. Fertilizer application of NPK is applied after 7-10 days of transplanting, then at the time of starting of lateral vine development, then at the flowering period.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sponge Gourd,Fertilizer Uses,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME BETTER/GOOD/FERTILIZER USE S OF SPONGE GOURD CROP?,"At the time of land preparation apply fertilizer dose of Nitrogen @40kg (Urea@90kg), phosphorus @20kg (Single super phosphate @125kg) and potassium@20kg (Muriate of potash @35kg) as a basal dose. At the time of sowing, apply one third of the Nitrogen dose along with Phosphorus and potash. At the early stage of vine production i.e. one month of sowing apply rest of the dose.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sponge Gourd,Water Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WATER MANAGEMENT OF SPONGE GOURD CROP?,"In summer or dry condition, apply irrigation with the interval of 7-10 days and in rainy season, it requires limited irrigation. First irrigation must be done immediately after seed sowing. In total crop requires 7-8 numbers of irrigations.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sponge Gourd,Weed Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WEED MANAGEMENT OF SPONGE GOURD CROP?,To make the field weed free mulching and then weedicides are necessary. Apply Pendimethalin @1 ltr/acre or Fluchloralin @800ml/acre as pre-emergence herbicide.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sponge Gourd,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME VARIETIES OF SPONGE GOURD CROP?,"PSG-9: The variety is developed in 2005. The variety contains dark green color leaves with medium-long vines. The fruits of this variety are smooth, tender, dark green in color and are long in shape. Harvesting is mainly done after 60days of transplanting. It gives an average yield of 65qtl/acre. The average fruit size is 65g.

Pusa Chikni: This variety contains dark green color leaves, medium height plant and medium sized fruit. The fruits are smooth, tender and 2.5-3.5cm in thickness. It gives an average yield of 35-40qtl/acre.

Azad Toria-2: It is recommended to grow in Punjab, Uttarakhand, Jharkhand, Bihar, and Tarai region of U.P.

Pusa Supriya: It is recommended to grow in Punjab, Jharkhand, Bihar, U.P., Gujarat, Haryana, Delhi and Rajasthan regions.

Punjab Kaali Tori-9: Released in 2005. It gives an average yield of 65qtl/acre. It has long, soft and dark green color fruits. The first harvesting is done after 60 days of sowing. 

Other state varieties:

Pusa Sneha: The variety is developed in 2004 by Indian Agriculture Research Institute (IARI). It contains medium long size fruit which is smooth and is dark green in color having blackish green color strips on it. The variety is resistant to high temperature. Spring and rainy seasons are best for crop production. Harvesting is mainly after 45-50 days of sowing.

Azad Toria-1: It is recommended to grown in Uttar Pradesh regions.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sponge Gourd,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SPONGE GOURD  VARIETIEY PSG-9?,"The variety is developed in 2005. The variety contains dark green color leaves with medium-long vines. The fruits of this variety are smooth, tender, dark green in color and are long in shape. Harvesting is mainly done after 60days of transplanting. It gives an average yield of 65qtl/acre. The average fruit size is 65g.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sponge Gourd,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SPONGE GOURD  VARIETIEY PUSA CHIKNI?,"This variety contains dark green color leaves, medium height plant and medium sized fruit. The fruits are smooth, tender and 2.5-3.5cm in thickness. It gives an average yield of 35-40qtl/acre.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sponge Gourd,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SPONGE GOURD  VARIETIEY AZAD TORIA-2?,"It is recommended to grow in Punjab, Uttarakhand, Jharkhand, Bihar, and Tarai region of U.P","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sponge Gourd,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SPONGE GOURD  VARIETIEY PUSA SUPRIYA?,"It is recommended to grow in Punjab, Jharkhand, Bihar, U.P., Gujarat, Haryana, Delhi and Rajasthan regions.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sponge Gourd,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SPONGE GOURD  VARIETIEY PUNJAB KAALI TORI-9?,"Released in 2005. It gives an average yield of 65qtl/acre. It has long, soft and dark green color fruits. The first harvesting is done after 60 days of sowing.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sponge Gourd,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SPONGE GOURD  VARIETIEY PUSA SNEHA?,The variety is developed in 2004 by Indian Agriculture Research Institute (IARI). It contains medium long size fruit which is smooth and is dark green in color having blackish green color strips on it. The variety is resistant to high temperature. Spring and rainy seasons are best for crop production. Harvesting is mainly after 45-50 days of sowing.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sponge Gourd,Seeds,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SEED MANAGEMENT OF SPONGE GOURD CROP?,"Seed rate:Use seed rate of 2.0 kg/acre.
Seed treatment:With the help of filer firstly scrap the seed coat of the seed and then soak the seeds in the water for 24 hours for better viability and higher germination percentage.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sponge Gourd,Seeds,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SEED TREATMENT OF SPONGE GOURD CROP?,"With the help of filer firstly scrap the seed coat of the seed and then soak the seeds in the water for 24 hours for better viability and higher germination percentage.

","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sponge Gourd,Seeds,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SEED PRODUCTION OF SPONGE GOURD CROP?,"Keep isolation distance of 1000m from other varieties of sponge gourd. Remove diseased plants from the field. The ideal time for growing the seed crop is in the month of February-March because harvesting of seeds will be easier during dry month. For seed production, the fruits are harvested when they get physiologically mature. After harvesting seeds are taken out form pulp, then they are packed and are stored.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sponge Gourd,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF POWDERY MILDEW  IN SPONGE GOURD CROP?,"The symptoms are appearance of white powdery spots on upper surface of leaves which causes leaf withering.
Treatment: Treatment must be given in start of hot and humid summer season. Application of M-45@2gm in 1ltr of water will help to cure powdery mildew. It can also be controlled by fungicidal sprays of Chlorothalonil, benomyl or dinocap.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sponge Gourd,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF BEETLES  IN SPONGE GOURD CROP?,"The symptoms are damage to flowers, leaves and stems.
Treatment: Appropriate insecticidal spray will help to cure pests.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sponge Gourd,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF APHID AND THRIPS  IN SPONGE GOURD CROP?,"They suck the sap from the leaves resulting in yellowing and drooping of leaves. Thrips results in curling of leaves, leaves become cup shaped or curved upward.If infestation is observed in field, To control spray the crop with Thiamethoxam@5gm/15Ltr of water.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sponge Gourd,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF BLIGHT IN SPONGE GOURD CROP?,"Copper oxychloride should be sprayed at the rate of 30 grams per 15 liters of water. 
","[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Sponge Gourd,Nutrient Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME NECESSARY NUTRITION OF SPONGE GOURD?,"NITROGEN--40kg/acre, k2o --20kg/acre, p2o5--20 kg/acre
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Sponge Gourd,Fertilizer Uses,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FERTILIZER REQUIREMENT IN SPONGE GOURD?,"UREA--90kg/acre, SSP--125kg/acre,MURIATE OF POTASH--35 kg/acre
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Radish,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME RADISH CROP?,"Radish, edible root vegetable belongs to family of ""Cruciferae"" and its origin is in Mediterranean. It is crop of tropical and temperate region. It is a quick growing annual or biannual herb. Its edible roots are having different color from white to red. West Bengal, Bihar, Uttar Pradesh, Karnataka, Punjab and Assam are major radish growing states. Radish is good source of vitamin B8, Calcium, copper, magnesium and riboflavin. Also it is rich in ascorbic acid, folic acid and potassium.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Radish,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME PUSA HIMANI SOWING TIME OF  RADISH CROP?,Pusa Himani: Optimum time for sowing is January-February.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Radish,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME PUNJAB PASAND SOWING TIME OF  RADISH CROP?,Punjab Pasand: Optimum time for sowing is from second fortnight of March where as for Pusa chetki optimum time for sowing is from April-August.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Radish,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME JAPANESE WHITE SOWING TIME OF  RADISH CROP?,Japanese white: Optimum time for sowing is from November-December.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Radish,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOIL MANAGEMENT OF  RADISH CROP?,"It can be grown on all type of soils but give best result when grown on light friable, sandy loam soil. Avoid heavy or compact soils as it produce rough, malformed roots. Ideal pH of soil for good growth is 5.5 to 6.8","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Radish,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME RADISH SUITABLE TEMPARATURE?,"The suitable temparature: Sowing Temparature- 20-25 degree, 
Normal Temperature- 18-25 degree,Harvesting Temperature- 18-20 degree,Rainfall- 100-225cm","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Radish,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME RADISH SOWING TEMPARATURE?,Sowing Temparature- 20-25 degree,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Radish,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME RADISH NORMAL TEMPARATURE?,Normal Temperature- 18-25 degree,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Radish,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME RADISH HARVESTING TEMPARATURE?,Harvesting Temperature- 18-20 degree,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Radish,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME RADISH RAINFALL?,Rainfall- 100-225cm,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Radish,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FIELD PREPARATION OF  RADISH CROP?,Plough land thoroughly and make land weed and clods free. Add well decomposed cow dung of 5-10ton/acre and mix well in soils at time of land preparation. Avoid use of undecomposed or free cowdung as it will leads to forking of fleshy roots.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Radish,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SPACING OF  RADISH CROP?,"Spacing: Use row to row spacing of 45 cm and plant to plant spacing of 7.5cm.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Radish,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOWING DEPTH OF  RADISH CROP?,"Sowing Depth: For good growth, sow seeds at depth of 1.5cm
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Radish,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME METHOD OF SOWING OF  RADISH CROP?,Method of Sowing: Sowing can be done by Line Sowing and Broadcasting method.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Radish,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME HARVESTING OF  RADISH CROP?,"Depending upon variety, radish is ready for harvesting in 25-60days after sowing. Harvesting is done manually by uprooting plants. Harvested roots are washed and then graded upon size.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Radish,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME POST-HARVESTING OF  RADISH CROP?,After harvesting grading of radish depending upon size is carried out. The product is marketed loose to sometime they are packed in gunny bags or basket.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Radish,Water Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WATER MANAGEMENT OF  RADISH CROP?,"After sowing, apply first irrigation, it will help in good germination. Depending upon soil type and climate, apply remaining irrigations at interval of 6-7days in summer and 10-12 days interval in winter month. Overall radish required five to six irrigations. Avoid excessive irrigation as it will leads misshape of roots and numerous hair growth. In summer season, provide pre-harvest light irrigation. It will keep root fresh and reduce pungency.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Radish,Weed Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WEED MANAGEMENT OF  RADISH CROP?,"Take interculture operation like weeding and hoeing to keep check on weed growth also to provide soil aeration. Take one weeding operation, two to three weeks after sowing. After weeding, carryout earthing operation.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Radish,Fertilizer Uses,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME BETTER/GOOD/FERTILIZER USE S OF  RADISH CROP?,"Along with well decomposed cowdung, apply Nitrogen@25kg (in form of Urea@55kg), Phosphorus@12kg (in form of SSP@ 75kg/acre) per acre in soil at time of sowing.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Radish,Seeds,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SEED MANAGEMENT OF  RADISH CROP?,"Seed Rate: For sowing of one acre land seed rate of 4-5kg is sufficient. It is sown on ridge for proper root development.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Radish,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME VARIETIES OF  RADISH CROP?,"Japanese white: Optimum time for sowing is from November-December. It is introduced in India from Japan. In northern plains it is recommended for late sowing and in hilly areas recommended for cultivation in July-September. Roots are cylindrical and having pure white color. Gives average yield of 160qtl/acre. 

Pusa chetki: Optimum time for sowing is from April-August. Early maturing variety suitable for seed production for Punjab region. Its roots are smooth, snow white color and medium long. It gives average yield of 105qtl/acre and seed yield of 4.5qtl/acre.

Pusa Himani: Suitable for sowing in fortnight of January-February. Its root are white with green shoulders. Ready to harvest in 60-65days after sowing. Gives average yield of 160qtl/acre.

Punjab Pasand: Optimum time for sowing is from second fortnight of March. It is early maturing variety, ready to harvest in 45days after sowing. Roots are long, white and free from hair. Suitable for sowing in main season as well as for off season. In main season, gives average yield of 215qtl/acre where as in off season gives average yield of 140qtl/acre.

Punjab Safed Mooli-2: The variety matures in 60days and gives an average yield of 236qtl/acre. 

Other state varieties---

Pusa Deshi: Suitable for sowing in northern plains. Roots are of pure white color. Ready to harvest in 50-55days after sowing.

Pusa Reshmi: Variety is suitable for early sowing. Ready to harvest in 50 to 60days. 

Arka Nishant: Long and pink root variety. Ready to harvest in 50-55days.

Rapid Red White Tipped: Very early maturing European table type variety. Ready to harvest in 25-30days. Roots are small and bright red colored with pure white flesh color.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
