Vegetables,Radish,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME RADISH VARIETIEY  PUSA RESHMI?,Variety is suitable for early sowing. Ready to harvest in 50 to 60days.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Radish,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME RADISH VARIETIEY  ARKA NISHANT?,"Long and pink root variety. Ready to harvest in 50-55days.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Radish,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF APHID IN RADISH CROP?,"Aphid: Serious pest of Radish, attacked at seedling as well as at maturity stage. If infestation is observed, spraying of Malathion 50EC@1ml/Litre of water should be done. Repeat spray for two-three times at interval of 10days.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Radish,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF ALTERNARIA BLIGHT IN RADISH CROP?,"Alternaria blight: Slightly raised, yellow spots are observed on leaves. Infection is rapidly spread in rainy season. Fungus spread on pods and seeds loose viability.If infestation is observed, spraying of Mancozeb@2gm/lit of water or Carbendazim@1gm/lit of water should be done to control this disease.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Radish,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF FLEA BEETLES AND MUSTARD SAW FLY IN RADISH CROP?,"Flea beetles and mustard saw fly: If infestation is observed in field, to control take spray of Malathion 50EC@1ml/Litre of water. Repeat spray for two-three times at interval of 10days.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Radish,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF TOBACCO CATERPILLAR IN RADISH?,"For control of tobacco borer in radish, spray 150 ml Rimon (Novaluron) 10 EC or 70 gm Proclam 5 SG (Emamectin Benzoate) dissolved in 80-100 liters of water (per acre).","[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Radish,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF ROOT ROT IN RADISH?,"For control of root rot diseases in radish, spray 150 ml Rimon (Novaluron) 10 EC or 70 gm Proclam 5 SG (Emamectin Benzoate) dissolved in 80-101 liters of water (per acre).","[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Radish,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF DOWNY MILDEW AND ALTERNARIA BLIGHT IN RADISH?,"For the prevention of downy mildew and alternaria blight disease in radish, dissolve 500 g of Indofil M-45 in 200 liters of water and spray per acre at an interval of 7 days.","[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Radish,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME EXCESS USE OF FERTILIZER DOSE?,"In case of heavy use of fertilizers in the crop, give light sprinkle irrigation.","[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Radish,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF TERMITE IN RADISH?,Apply 1 liter of Chlorpyrifos 20 EC mixed with 15-20 kg of soil for one acre.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Radish,Nutrient Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME THE BETTER GROWTH AND CONTROL NITROGEN DEFICIENCY IN RADISH?,Spray 1 kg of NPK 19:19:19 in 100 liters of water per acre to compensate for radish growth and nitrogen deficiency.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Radish,Nutrient Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME NECESSARY NUTRITION OF RADISH?,"NITROGEN--30kg/acre, PHOSPHORUS --8kg/acre, POTASH--12 kg/acre
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Radish,Fertilizer Uses,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FERTILIZER REQUIREMENT IN RADISH?,"UREA--65kg/acre, SSP--50kg/acre,MURIATE OF POTASH--20 kg/acre
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Rabi Onion,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME ONION CROP?,"Onion is most widely cultivated popular vegetable species. It is used for culinary purpose also it has several non-culinary use like it is used as Moth repellent because of its pungent juice, it is used to polish glass and copperware, onion concentrated water can be spray on plants to increased plants pest resistance. India ranks first in term of area and second in production after China.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Rabi Onion,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOWING TIME OF  ONION CROP?,"Optimum time for raising nursery is middle of October to middle of November month. Seedlings are ready for transplantation in middle of December to Middle of January month. For transplanting, select 10-15 cm heighted healthy seedlings.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Rabi Onion,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SUITABLE TIME OF  ONION CROP?,"Optimum time for raising nursery is middle of October to middle of November month. Seedlings are ready for transplantation in middle of December to Middle of January month. For transplanting, select 10-16 cm heighted healthy seedlings.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Rabi Onion,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOIL MANAGEMENT OF  ONION CROP?,"It can be cultivated on various soil types such as sandy loam, clay loam silt loam and heavy soils. It gives best result when grown in deep loam and alluvial soils with good drainage, moisture holding capacity and sufficient organic matter. Loose and sandy soils are not suitable for cultivation as bulb produce in such soil are deformed with less keeping quality. pH of soil should be 6 to 7.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Rabi Onion,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FIELD PREPARATION OF  ONION CROP?,Give three to four deep ploughing and bring soil to fine tilth. Add well decomposed cow dung to increase organic content of soil. Then levelled the soil and divide into small plots and channels.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Rabi Onion,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SPACING OF  ONION CROP?,"Spacing:To get higher yield, while transplanting, use spacing of 15 cm between rows and 7.5 cm between plants.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Rabi Onion,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOWING DEPTH OF  ONION CROP?,"Sowing Depth:In nursery, sow seeds at depth of 1-2 cm.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Rabi Onion,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME HARVESTING OF  ONION CROP?,"Harvesting at proper time is necessary. It depend upon variety, season, market price etc. 50% neck falls is sign indicating crop is ready for harvesting. Harvesting is done manually by uprooting bulbs. After harvesting they are kept in field for 2-3 days to remove excessive moisture from bulb.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Rabi Onion,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME POST-HARVESTING OF  ONION CROP?,"After harvesting and proper drying, bulbs are sorted and graded according to size.

","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Rabi Onion,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME METHOD OF SOWING OF  ONION CROP?,Method of sowing: For sowing use transplanting method.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Rabi Onion,Water Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WATER MANAGEMENT OF  ONION CROP?,Depending upon climatic conditions and soil type decide irrigation amount and frequency. Apply first irrigation immediately after sowing then depending upon need apply irrigation with interval of 10-15 days.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Rabi Onion,Weed Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WEED MANAGEMENT OF  ONION CROP?,Initially onion seedlings grow slowly. So it is better to use chemical herbicides than hand weeding to avoid injury. To control weeds take spray of Pendimethalin(Stomp)@1 ltr/200 ltr water/acre within 72 hours of sowing. Apply Oxyfluorfen @425 ml/200 ltr of water per acre as post emergence herbicide 7 days after planting. Two to three weeding are recommended for weed control. First hand weeding should be done one month after sowing and second hand weeding to be done one month after first hand weeding.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Rabi Onion,Fertilizer Uses,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME BETTER/GOOD/FERTILIZER USE S OF  ONION CROP?,"Apply 20 tonnes of Farm Yard Manure or well decomposed cow dung 10 days before sowing. Apply Nitrogen@40 kg, Phophorus@20 kg and Potash@20 kg in form of Urea@90 kg, Single Super Phosphate@125 kg per acre and MOP@35 kg/acre. Apply whole quantity of Phosphorus, Potash and half dose of Nitrogen at time of transplanting. Apply remaining amount of nitrogen as top dressing, four weeks after transplantation.
WSF: 10-15 days after transplanting, sprayed 19:19:19 along with micronutrients@2.5 to 3 gm/Ltr of water.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Rabi Onion,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME VARIETIES OF  ONION CROP?,"PRO 6: Medium heighted variety with deep red, medium-large and round bulb. Ready to harvest in 120 days after transplanting. Gives average yield of 175 qtl/acre. Bulbs have good keeping quality.

Punjab Naroya: Medium heighted variety with deep red, medium-large and round bulb. Ready to harvest in 145 days after transplanting. Gives average yield of 150 qtl/acre. It is tolerant to purple blotch disease.

Punjab White: Medium large, round and white variety. Gives average yield of 135 qtl/acre.

Other state varieties:

Bhima Kiran: Suitable for growing in rabi season. Bulbs are of light red color and having round to oval shapes. Ready to harvest in 130 days. Bulbs having good keeping quality in storage. Gives average yield of 165 qtl/acre.

Bhima Shakti: Suitable for growing in kharif and rabi season. Ready to harvest in 130 days after transplanting, gives average yield of 170 qtl/acre.

Bhima Shweta: Suitable for rabi season. Bulbs are of white color and round in shape. Ready to harvest in 110-115 days after transplanting. Gives average yield of 160 qtl/acre. 

Early Grano: Developed by IARI, New Delhi. Bulbs are of yellow color. Suitable for cultivation in kharif as well as rabi season. Gives average yield of 200 qtl/acre.

","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Rabi Onion,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME ONION VARIETIEY  PRO 6?,"Medium heighted variety with deep red, medium-large and round bulb. Ready to harvest in 120 days after transplanting. Gives average yield of 175 qtl/acre. Bulbs have good keeping quality.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
