","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Rabi Onion,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME ONION VARIETIEY  BHIMA SHWETA?,Suitable for rabi season. Bulbs are of white color and round in shape. Ready to harvest in 110-115 days after transplanting. Gives average yield of 160 qtl/acre.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Rabi Onion,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME ONION VARIETIEY  EARLY GRANO?,"Developed by IARI, New Delhi. Bulbs are of yellow color. Suitable for cultivation in kharif as well as rabi season. Gives average yield of 200 qtl/acre.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Rabi Onion,Seeds,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SEED MANAGEMENT OF  RABI ONION CROP?,"Seed Rate-
Seed rate of 4-5 kg is sufficient for raising seedling required for one acre land.

Seed Treatment-
Seed treatment with Thiram@2 gm/kg of seed + Benomyl 50WP@1 gm/liter water effectively controls damping off and smut diseases. After chemical treatment, seed treatment with bio agent Trichoderma viride@2 gm/kg of seed is recommended, it help in reducing early seedling diseases and soil borne inoculum.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Rabi Onion,Seeds,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SEED TREATMENT OF  RABI ONION CROP?,"Seed treatment with Thiram@2 gm/kg of seed + Benomyl 50WP@1 gm/liter water effectively controls damping off and smut diseases. After chemical treatment, seed treatment with bio agent Trichoderma viride@2 gm/kg of seed is recommended, it help in reducing early seedling diseases and soil borne inoculum.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Rabi Onion,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF THRIPS IN RABI ONION CROP?,"Thrips: If not controlled properly can cause yield loss up to 50%. Mostly observed in dry weather. They suck sap from the foliage and results in curling of leaves, leaves become cup shaped or curved upward.

To check severity of thrips incidence, keep blue sticky traps @6-8 per acre. If infestation observed in field take spray of Fipronil (Regenta)@30 ml/15 ltr water. Or Prophenophos@10ml /10 ltr water by 8-10 days interval.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Rabi Onion,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF MAGGOTS   IN  RABI ONION CROP?,"Maggots: Infestation observed in January-February Month. They feed on roots causes browning of leaves. Base of plant become watery.

If infestation is observed, apply Carbaryl@1 ltr or Phorate@4 kg to the soil and give light irrigation. Or Apply Chlorpyriphos @2 ltr/acre alongwith irrigation water or sand.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Rabi Onion,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF WILT   IN  RABI ONION CROP?,19:19:19 60 g + Microla 40 ml + Clear 30 g / 15 liters of water should be sprayed,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Rabi Onion,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF BLIGHT ATTACK   IN  RABI ONION CROP?,Mancozeb 400 g/200 liters of water should be sprayed for 1 acre,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Rabi Onion,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF SUCKING PEST   IN  RABI ONION CROP?,For control of sap-sucking pest in onion crop - Bavistein Carbendazim 50% WP 30 gm/15 liter of water should be sprayed.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Rabi Onion,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF FUNGAL ATTACK   IN  RABI ONION CROP?,Clear (Carbendazim 12% + Mancozeb 63%).- Take 30 g/15 liters of water and spray.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Rabi Onion,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF YELLOWING LEAVES   IN  RABI ONION CROP?,19:19:19 - Take 60 grams + micronutrients in 30 ml / 15 liters of water and spray.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Rabi Onion,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF CATTERPILLER  IN  RABI ONION CROP?,Imamectin benzoate 5% - 8 gm in 15 liters of water should be sprayed.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Rabi Onion,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF LEAF BLIGHT  IN  RABI ONION CROP?,You should spray Pseudomonas Bluesons at 5 ml per liter of water,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Rabi Onion,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF PURPLE BLOTCH AND STEMPHYLIUM BLIGHT  IN  RABI ONION CROP?,"Purple blotch and stemphylium blight: In severe infestation may cause yield loss up to 70%. Deep purple lesions are observed on leaves. Yellow streaks get turn brown and extend along the blade.

Take spray of Propineb 70%WP@350 gm/acre/150 ltr of water, twice at 10 days interval.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Rabi Onion,Nutrient Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME BETTER GROWTH OF RABI ONION?,00:52:34 60 gm+ Micro in 30/15 liter of water should be sprayed for better growth.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Rabi Onion,Nutrient Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME NECESSARY NUTRITION OF RABI ONION?,"NITROGEN--40kg/acre, PHOSPHORUS --20kg/acre, POTASH--20 kg/acre
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Rabi Onion,Fertilizer Uses,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FERTILIZER REQUIREMENT IN RABI ONION?,"UREA--90kg/acre, SSP--125kg/acre,MURIATE OF POTASH--35 kg/acre
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Rabi Onion,Fertilizer Uses,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME BIO BETTER/GOOD/FERTILIZER USE D IN RABI ONION CROP?,Apply 4 kg of Consortium mixed with 15-20 kg of soil (per acre) and as soon as the onion crop is planted in the field.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Rabi Onion,Nutrient Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME THE BETTER GROWTH OF RABI ONION NURSERY?,Spray 10 grams of NPK 19:19:19 per liter of water for growth of onion.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Pumpkin,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME PUMPKIN CROP?,"It is a popular vegetable crop in India which is grown in rainy season. It is also known as ""HalwaKadduor adduin hindi and it belongs to cucurbitaceae family. India is the second largest producer of pumpkin. It is used for cooking purpose and is used to make sweets. It is good source of Vitamin A and potassium. Pumpkin helps to boost eye vision, lowers blood pressure and has antioxidant properties. Its leaves, young stems, fruit juice and flowers contain medicinal properties.

","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Pumpkin,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOWING TIME OF  PUMPKIN CROP?,Time of sowing:February-March and June-July is an optimum time for seed sowing.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Pumpkin,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SUITABLE TIME OF  PUMPKIN CROP?,Time of sowing:February-March and June-July is an optimum time for seed sowing.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Pumpkin,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOIL MANAGEMENT OF  PUMPKIN CROP?,It requires loamy soil having good drainage system and is rich in organic matter. Soil pH of 6-7 is optimum for pumpkin cultivation.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Pumpkin,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FIELD PREPARATION OF  PUMPKIN CROP?,"Well prepared land is required for pumpkin farming. To bring the soil to fine tilth, ploughings with local tractor is required.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Pumpkin,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SPACING OF  PUMPKIN CROP?,"Spacing:Sow two seeds on per hill and use spacing of 60cm. For hybrid varieties, sow seeds on both side of bed and use spacing of 45cm.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Pumpkin,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOWING DEPTH OF  PUMPKIN CROP?,"Sowing Depth:Seeds are sown 1 inch deep in the soil.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Pumpkin,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME HARVESTING OF  PUMPKIN CROP?,Harvesting is mainly done when skin of the fruits turns pale brown in color and the inner flesh becomes golden yellow in color. Mature fruits having good storage capacity therefore they can be used for long distance transportation. Harvesting of immature fruits is also done for sale purpose.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Pumpkin,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME METHOD OF SOWING OF  PUMPKIN CROP?,Method of sowing: Direct sowing,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Pumpkin,Water Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WATER MANAGEMENT OF  PUMPKIN CROP?,"Proper irrigation at proper intervals of time is required. Immediate irrigation is required after seed sowing. Depending upon the season, subsequent irrigations at the interval of 6-7 days is required. In total 8-10 irrigation are required.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Pumpkin,Weed Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WEED MANAGEMENT OF  PUMPKIN CROP?,"To control the weeds, frequent weeding or earthing up operation is required. Weeding is done with the help of hoe or by hands. First weeding is done after 2-3 weeks of seed sowing. In total 3-4 weedings are required to make the field weed free.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Pumpkin,Fertilizer Uses,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME BETTER/GOOD/FERTILIZER USE S OF  PUMPKIN CROP?,"Application of well rotten FYM@8-10tonnes/acre is used before preparation of beds. Fertilizer dose of Nitrogen @40kg/acre in the form of urea @90kg/acre, Phosphorus @20kg/acre in the form of SSP@125kg/acre and Potassium @20kg/acre in the form of MOP@35kg/acre is added. Nitrogen dose is applied in 2 equal splits. First half dose is applied before sowing and then remaining dose of nitrogen is applied as top dressing within one month.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Pumpkin,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME VARIETIES OF  PUMPKIN CROP?,"Hybrid varieties:

PAU Magaz Kaddoo-1: Released in 2018. The variety is also used for making Magaz and snacks. It has hull-less seeds, dwarf vines and dark green color leaves. It has medium sized fruits which is round and turns golden yellow at maturity. The seed contains 32% omega-6, 3% protein and 27% oil content. It gives an average yield of 2.9qtl/acre of seeds.

PPH-1: Released in 2016. Extra early maturing variety. They have dwarf vines, short internodal length and dark green color leaves. It contains small fruits which are round in shape. The fruit is mottled green in color when immature and at maturity stage it becomes mottled brown in color. Fruit contains golden yellow color flesh. It gives an average yield of 206qtl/acre.

PPH-2: Released in 2016. Extra early maturing variety. They have dwarf vines, short internodal length and green color leaves. It contains small fruits which are round in shape. The fruit is light green in color when immature and at maturity stage it becomes smooth brown in color. Fruit contains golden yellow color flesh. It gives an average yield of 222qtl/acre.

Punjab Samrat (Released in 2008): They have medium long vines, angular stem and dark green color leaves. It contains small fruits which are round in shape. The fruit is mottled green in color when immature and at maturity stage it becomes pale brown in color. Fruit contains golden yellow color flesh. It gives an average yield of 165qtl/acre.

Other state varieties:

CO 2: Released in 1974. The average weight of each fruit is 1.5-2kg. The fruit contains orange color flesh. It gives an average yield of 100qtl/acre. The variety gets mature in 135 days.

CO1, ArkaSuryamukhi, PusaViswesh, TCR 011, Ambilli and ArkaChandan are the important varieties of Pumpkin.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
