","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Potato,Seeds,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SEED MANAGEMENT OF  POTATO CROP?,"Seed rate:
Seed rate of 1kg seed is sufficient for one acre land.

Seed treatment:
Treatment with Benlate or Bavistin @2.5 gm/kg of seed is used to cure from soil borne diseases.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Potato,Seeds,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SEED PRODUCTION OF  POTATO CROP?,Keep isolation distance of 1000m for foundation and 500m for certified seed production from other varieties of Potato. Remove diseased plants from field. When fruits are mature i.e. they changes their color into dull. Then they are crushed with hands in fresh water and then separate seeds from pulp. Seeds which are settled in bottom are collected for seed purpose.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Potato,Seeds,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SEED TREATMENT OF  POTATO CROP?,"Treatment with Benlate or Bavistin @2.5 gm/kg of seed is used to cure from soil borne diseases.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Potato,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF MOSAIC  IN  POTATO CROP?,"Mosaic: Mosaic affected plants give faint yellow appearance along with stunted growth. Size and number of tuber get reduced.

For sowing use healthy and diseased free seeds. Inspect field regularly and destroyed infected plant and parts immediately. Take spray of Metasystox or Rogor@300ml in 200 litres of water per acre.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Potato,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF BACTERIAL SOFT ROT  IN  POTATO CROP?,"Bacterial soft rot: At base of plant black leg appears along with browning of infected tubers also plant give yellow appearance. In severe condition plant wilt and get died. On infected tubers soft, reddish spot appear on infected tubers.

For sowing, use healthy and disease free tubers. Before sowing treat seed with Boric Acid@3% (300gm/10Ltr of water) for 30minutes and then dried in shades. Before storage of tubers repeat the treatment with Boric Acid. In plains areas, treat seed with Carbendazim@1% (100gm/10Ltr of water) for 15minutes for effective control of disease.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Potato,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF COMMON SCAB  IN  POTATO CROP?,"Common scab: It survives in field as well as in storage. Disease is spread rapidly in low moisture condition. Light brown to dark brown lesion are appeared on infected tubers.

Use only well rotten cow dung for application in field. Use diseased free seeds for planting. Avoid deep planting of tubers. Follow crop rotation and avoid mono cropping in same field. Before sowing, treat seeds with Emisan 6@0.25% (2.5gm/ltr of water) for five minutes.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Potato,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF LATE BLIGHT IN  POTATO CROP?,"Late Blight: Infestation is observed on lower part of leaves and tip of leaves. Irregular water spots are seen on infected leaves. Around the spot white powdery growth is observed. In severe condition, white powdery growth is seen on nearby soil surface of infected plants. This disease is rapidly spread in cloudy weather and after rains. If not controlled, it can cause loss up to 50%.

For sowing, use healthy and disease free seeds. If infestation is observed, take spray of Propineb@40gm/15Ltr of water.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Potato,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF BLACK SCURF  IN  POTATO CROP?,"Black scurf: Black speck observed on tubers. Affected plants show drying up. In infected tubers, at time of sprouting, black, brown color appear on eyes.

For planting use diseased free tubers. Before sowing, seed treatment with Mercury is essential. Avoid mono cropping and follow crop rotation. If land kept fallow for two years then severity of disease is reduced.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Potato,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF EARLY BLIGHT  IN  POTATO CROP?,"Early blight: Necrotic spots observed on lower leaves. The fungus due which infestation occurred lies in soil. It rapidly spread in high moisture and low temperature.

Avoid mono cropping of crop and follow crop rotation. If infestation is observed, spraying of Mancozeb@30gm or Copper oxychloride@30gm/10ltr water at 45 days 2-3 times at 10 days interval should be done.

","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Potato,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF POTATO TUBER MOTH  IN  POTATO CROP?,"Potato Tuber Moth: It is major pest in field as well as in storage. It make tunnel in potato and feeds on flesh.

Use healthy and diseased free seeds for sowing. Use only well decomposed cow dung. If infestation is observed take spray of Carbaryl@1gm per Ltr of water.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Potato,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF WHITE GRUB  IN  POTATO CROP?,"White Grub: They remain in soil and damage crop by feeding on roots, stem and tubers. Infected plants show drying up. Grubs make holes in tubers.

As preventive measures, broadcasting with Carbofuran 3G@12kg or Thimet 10G@7kg/acre should be done at the time of sowing.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Potato,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF EPILANCHNA BEETLE  IN  POTATO CROP?,"Epilanchna Beetle: Larva and adults damages crop by feeding on leaves.

In initial phase of infestation, collect egg of beetle manually and then destroyed it away from the field. Take spray of Carbaryl@1gm per ltr of water.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Potato,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF LEAF EATING CATERPILLAR  IN  POTATO CROP?,"Leaf eating Caterpillar: They feed on potato leaves and thus damage the crop.

If infestation observed in field, spray crop with Chlorpyrifos or Profenofos@2ml or Lambda Cyhalothrin@1ml/Ltr of water.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Potato,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF CUT WORMS  IN  POTATO CROP?,"Cut worms: They damage crop by cutting sprout at ground level. They feed at night so control becomes difficult.
As a preventive measure, use only well rotten cow dung. If infestation is observed, spray crop with Chlorpyrifos 20% EC@ 2.5ml per ltr of water. Apply Phorate 10G@4 kg/acre around plants and they cover with soil.
If infestation of tobacco caterpillar is observed then spraying with Quinalphos 25EC@ 20ml/10Ltr of water is done to control cut worms.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Potato,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF APHID  IN  POTATO CROP?,"Aphid: Adult and nymphs, both suck the sap thus weaken the plant. In severe infestation, they cause curling and deformation of young leaves. They secrete honey dew like substance and sooty, black mould is developed on affected parts.
Cut the foliage according region timing, to check infestation of aphid. If infestation of aphid and jassid observed take spray of Imidacloprid@50ml or Thiamethoxam@40 gm/acre/150ltr water.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Potato,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF BLIGHT  IN  POTATO CROP?,In control of blight on potato crop - Fungicide containing Propaneb 70% WP - 30 gm / 15 liters of water should be sprayed.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Potato,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF ROOT ROT  IN  POTATO CROP?,Sprayed 500g SAAF (12% carbendazim 63% WP mancozeb) with sand.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Potato,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF EALRY BLIGHT AND LATE BLIGHT  IN  POTATO CROP?,"To prevent root rot in garlic, sprinkle 500 grams of clear (Carbendazim 12% + Mancozeb 63%) mixed with 15 kg of sand per acre or drench at the rate of 3 grams of Bavistin per liter of water.","[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Potato,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SUCKING PEST CONTROL IN POTATO?,Lambda psilothrin 10 ml solution in 15 liters of water should be sprayed.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Potato,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF EARLY BLIGHT AND LATE BLIGHT  IN POTATO?,"For the prevention of early and late blight in potato, spray 500-700 grams of Indofil M45 or 750-1000 grams of copper oxychloride in 250-350 liters of water per acre. 3rd and 4th spraying Spray 700 g Ridomil Gold in 250 liters of water per acre.","[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Potato,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF JASSID AND APHID IN POTATO CROP?,Spray 300 ml of Rogor (diamethoate 30 EC) or 300 ml of malathion mixed with 80-100 liters of water.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Potato,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF POTATO SCAB?,"The following control measures have all been proven effective against scab in potatoes. However, in most cases a combination of these techniques will be required.
1. Plant-certifiedant certified, disease-free seed potatoes and resistant varieties whenever possible. We suggest using the russet-skinned varieties since they have more resistance to the disease.
2. Rotate root crops by planting in alternate locations to limit the disease.
3. Potato scab is most prevalent in dry, alkaline soils. Decrease soil pH by adding elemental sulfur. The disease is controlled or greatly suppressed at soil pH levels of 5.2 or lower. Simple and affordable soil test kits are available to check pH often.
4. Tilling in a cover crop mustard, canola, alfalfa prior to planting potatoes will help reduce infection.
5. Some growers report success spreading agricultural gypsum prior to planting at a rate of 25 lbs per 2,000 sq ft. This will raise the calcium content of your soil and help build strong cell walls in plants. (Note: S. scabies disrupts the development of cell walls resulting in lesions.)
6. Adequate irrigation during early tuber development may have a dramatic effect on common scab infection, but you will need to keep the soil damp for 2-6 weeks. This technique is effective because high soil moisture promotes growth of a bacteria that can crowd out S. scabies on the potato surface.
7. Do NOT overwater.",[Reference: www.planetnatural.com/pest-problem-solver/plant-disease/potato-scab/]
Vegetables,Potato,Fertilizer Uses,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME APPLICATION OF BIOZYME IN POTATO?,"For better yield in potato crop, apply Biozyme 8 kg granular at sowing and tilling or spray 200 ml of liquid Biozyme.","[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Potato,Fertilizer Uses,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME APPLICATION OF BIO-FERTILIZER USE IN POTATO?,"At the time of potato planting, adding 4 kg of Consortium organic fertilizer to the soil per acre increases the yield.","[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Potato,Nutrient Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME DOSE OF GIBBERALLIC ACID  IN POTATO?,Spray gibberellic acid at the rate of 2 milliliters per liter in potatoes,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Potato,Nutrient Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME POTATO CROP GROWTH?,12.61.00 1-1.5 kg + Microla 300 ml + humic acid 500 ml / 200-250 L of water should be applied by drip per acre for more shoots and balanced growth in potato crop.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Potato,Nutrient Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME NUTRIENT SPRAY FOR POTATO CROP?,Sprayed NPK 13:00:45 dose in rice crop 1.5% (1.5 kg) per 200 liter water.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Potato,Nutrient Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME THE BETTER QUALITY OF POTATO?,"For best yield of potato, spray 2 kg NPK per acre at 13:00:45 in 100 liters of water.","[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Potato,Nutrient Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CALCIUM NITRATE OF POTATO?,The dose of calcium nitrate in potatoes is 500 grams per 200 liters of water.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Potato,Nutrient Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME BURSTING OF POTATOS IN THE FIELD?,Spray 200 grams of boron per 100 liters of water per acre in the potato crop,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Potato,Nutrient Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME THE DOSE OF GIBBERALLIC ACID IN POTATO?,Spray gibberellic acid at the rate of 2 milliliters per liter in potatos.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Potato,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME EARLY SOWN VARIETIES OF POTATO?,"Early varieties of potato- Kufri Suraya (Average yield: 100-125 quintal), Kufri Chandramukhi (Average yield: 100 quintal), Kufri Ashoka (Average yield: 110 quintal) and Kufri Pukhraj (Average yield: 130 quintal)","[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Potato,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME LATE SOWN VARIETIES OF POTATO?,"Later varieties of potato - Kufri Sandhuri, Kufri Badshah","[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Potato,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME MID SOWN VARIETIES OF POTATO?,"Medium season varieties of potato - Kufri Pushkar, Kufri Jyoti and Kufri Bahar.","[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Potato,Fertilizer Uses,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME APPLICATION OF SULFUR IN POTATO FOR DRAINAGE PURPOSE?,There is no recommendation to add sulfur to water in potatos.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Potato,Nutrient Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME NECESSARY NUTRITION OF POTATO?,"NITROGEN--75kg/acre, PHOSPHORUS --25kg/acre, POTASH--25 kg/acre
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
