","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Garlic,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME GARLIC VARIETIEY VL GARLIC 1?,"VL Garlic 1: Bulbs are of whitish color. Ready to harvest in 180-190days. Gives average yield of 56-60 qtl/acre in hills and 36-40 qtl/acre in plains.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Garlic,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME GARLIC VARIETIEY YAMUNA SAFED 5?,Yamuna Safed 5: Ready to harvest in 150-160 days. Gives average yield of 68-72 qtl/acre.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Garlic,Seeds,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SEED MANAGEMENT OF  GARLIC CROP?,"Seed Rate
Use seed rate of 225-250 kg per acre.

Seed Treatment
Seed treatment with Thiram@2 gm/kg of seed + Benomyl 50WP@1 gm/liter water effectively controls damping off and smut diseases. After chemical treatment, seed treatment with bio agent Trichoderma viride@2 gm/kg of seed is recommended, it help in reducing early seedling diseases and soil borne inoculum.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Garlic,Seeds,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SEED TREATMENT OF  GARLIC CROP?,"Seed Treatment:
Seed treatment with Thiram@2 gm/kg of seed + Benomyl 50WP@1 gm/liter water effectively controls damping off and smut diseases. After chemical treatment, seed treatment with bio agent Trichoderma viride@2 gm/kg of seed is recommended, it help in reducing early seedling diseases and soil borne inoculum.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Garlic,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF THRIPS   IN  GARLIC CROP?,"Thrips: If it is not controlled properly, can cause yield loss up to 50%. Mostly observed in dry weather. They suck sap from the foliage and results in curling of leaves, leaves become cup shaped or curved upward.


To check severity of thrips incidence, keep blue sticky traps @6-8 per acre. If infestation observed in field take spray of Fipronil@30 ml/15 Ltr water or Profenophos@10 ml or Carbosulfan@10 ml+ Mancozeb@25 gm/10 Ltr water by 8-10 days interval.

","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Garlic,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF MAGGOTS  IN  GARLIC CROP?,"Maggots: Infestation observed in January-February Month. They feed on roots cause browning of leaves. Base of plant become watery.


If infestation is observed, apply Carbaryl@4 kg or Phorate@4 kg to the soil and give light irrigation. Apply Chlorpyriphos @1 Ltr/acre alongwith irrigation water or sand.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Garlic,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF PURPLE BLOTCH AND STEM PHYLIUM BLIGHT  IN  GARLIC CROP?,Purple blotch and stem phylium blight: In severe infestation may cause yield loss up to 70%. Deep purple lesions are observed on leaves. Yellow streaks get turn brown and extend along the blade.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Garlic,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME THE CONTROL OF ROOT ROT IN  GARLIC?,"To prevent root rot in garlic, sprinkle 500 grams of clear (Carbendazim 12% + Mancozeb 63%) mixed with 15 kg of sand per acre or drench at the rate of 3 grams of Bavistin per liter of water.","[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Garlic,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME THE CONTROL OF WHITE GRUB IN GARLIC?,"To control white grub in garlic, mix 1 liter of Chlorpyrifos 20 EC with 15-20 kg of sand, sprinkle diyo or 1 kg of white leaf per acre at the time of irrigation.","[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Garlic,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME  ADVANCE SPRAY TO STOP THE ATTACK OF INSECT IN GARLIC CROP?,"If the garlic is not attacked by any insects, then there is no need to do any pesticides","[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Garlic,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL MECONTROL OF FUNGAL DISEASE IN GARLIC?,Indifil M-45 can be sprayed at the rate of 3 gm per liter to prevent fungal disease in garlic crop.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Garlic,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME  IMPROVED VARIETIES OF GARLIC?,"Improved recommended types of garlic - PG-18, PG-17","[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Garlic,Water Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME IRRIGATION SCHEDULE IN GARLIC?,First irrigation in garlic should be done immediately after sowing and subsequent irrigations at 10-15 days interval depending on soil type and weather. Total 10-12 waterings are required.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Garlic,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME YIELD OF GARLIC VARIETIES?,Garlic crop takes 165-170 days to mature.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Garlic,Water Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FUNGAL ATTACK ON GARLIC?,Bavistein (Carbendazim 50% WP)-30 g/15 liters of water should be sprayed.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Garlic,Fertilizer Uses,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FERTILIZER DOSE FOR GARLIC?,Fertilizer spraying in garlic crop - 19:19:19 - 60 grams + Microla - 30 ml/ 15 liters of water should be sprayed.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Garlic,Nutrient Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME NECESSARY NUTRITION OF GARLIC?,"NITROGEN--50kg/acre, PHOSPHORUS --25kg/acre, POTASH --20kg/acre
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Garlic,Fertilizer Uses,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FERTILIZER REQUIREMENT IN GARLIC?,"UREA--110kg/acre, SSP--155kg/acre,MURIATE OF POTASH--As per soil test
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cucumber,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CUCUMBER CROP?,"The botanical name of cucumber is Cucumis sativus. Cucumbers are originated in India. It is a climbing plant which is used as summer vegetable throughout in India. The cucumber fruit is eaten raw or is served as a salad or cooked as a vegetable. The seeds of cucumber are used for oil extraction which is good for body and brain. Cucumbers contain 96% water which is good in summer season. The plants are large sized, leaves are hairy and are triangular in shape and flowers are yellow in color. Cucumber is an excellent source of Mb (Molybdenum) and Vitamin K. Cucumber is used to cure skin problems, kidney and heart problems and is used as alkalizer.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cucumber,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOWING TIME OF  CUCUMBER CROP?,It is sown in the month of February-March.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cucumber,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SUITABLE TEMPARARTURE OF CUCUMBER CROPS?,"The suitable temparature: Sowing Temparature- 22-30 degree, 
Normal Temperature- 25-35 degree,Harvesting Temperature- 30-35 degree,Rainfall- 120-150 mm
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cucumber,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOWING TEMPARARTURE OF CUCUMBER CROPS?,Sowing Temparature- 22-30 degree,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cucumber,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME NORMAL TEMPARARTURE OF CUCUMBER CROPS?,Normal Temperature- 25-35 degree,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cucumber,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME HARVESTING TEMPARARTURE OF CUCUMBER CROPS?,Harvesting Temperature- 30-35 degree,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cucumber,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME RAINFALL OF CUCUMBER CROPS?,Rainfall- 120-150 mm,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cucumber,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SUITABLE TIME OF  CUCUMBER CROP?,It is sown in the month of February-March.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cucumber,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOIL MANAGEMENT OF  CUCUMBER CROP?,It can be sown in variety of soils ranging from sandy loam to heavy soil. But a loamy soil which is rich in organic matter and has well drainage system is best for the cucumber farming. The pH ranging from 6-7 is suited best for cucumber farming.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cucumber,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FIELD PREPARATION OF  CUCUMBER CROP?,"For cucumber plantation, it requires well prepared and weed free field. To bring soil to fine tilth, 3-4 ploughings must be done before planting. FYM such as cow dung is mixed with soil to enrich the field. Then nursery beds are prepared having width of 2.5m and at the distance of 60cm.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cucumber,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SPACING OF  CUCUMBER CROP?,Spacing:Sow two seeds per place of bed which is 2.5m wide and use spacing of 60cm between seeds.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cucumber,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOWING DEPTH OF  CUCUMBER CROP?,"Sowing Depth:Seeds are sown at the depth of 2-3cm.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cucumber,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME HARVESTING OF  CUCUMBER CROP?,Plants start yielding in about 45-50 days after sowing. Mainly 10-12 harvestings can be done. Harvesting is mainly done when the seed of cucumber are soft and the fruits are green and young. Harvesting is done with the help of sharp knife or any sharp object. It gives an average of 33-42qtl/acre of yield.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cucumber,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME POST HARVESTING OF  CUCUMBER CROP?,"After harvesting and proper drying, bulbs are sorted and graded according to size.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cucumber,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME METHOD OF SOWING OF  CUCUMBER CROP?,"Method of sowing: 1.Low tunnel technology: This technology is used to produce early yield of cucumber in early summer. It helps to protect the crop from cold season i.e. in the month of December and January. Beds of 2.5m width are sown in the month of December. Seeds are sown both sides of the bed at the distance of 45cm. Before sowing supportive rods of 45-60cm length are fixed in the soil. Cover the field with plastic sheet (100 gauge thickness) with the help of support rods. Plastic sheet should be removed mainly in the month of February when temperature is suitable outside.
2. Dibbling method
3.Basing method
4.Layout in ring method","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cucumber,Water Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WATER MANAGEMENT OF  CUCUMBER CROP?,"In summer season it requires frequent irrigation and in rainy season it does not require any irrigation. In total it requires 10-12 irrigations. Pre-irrigation is required before sowing then subsequent irrigation is required after 2-3 days of sowing. After second sowing, the crops are then irrigated at the interval of 4-5 days. Drip irrigation is very useful for this crop.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cucumber,Weed Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WEED MANAGEMENT OF  CUCUMBER CROP?,"Weed can be controlled by hand-hoeing and also controlled by chemically, use glyphosate@1.6litre per 150 litre of water. Use glyphosate only on weeds not on crop plants.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cucumber,Fertilizer Uses,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME BETTER/GOOD/FERTILIZER USE S OF  CUCUMBER CROP?,"At the time of land preparation apply fertilizer dose of Nitrogen @40kg (Urea@90kg), phosphorus @20kg (Single phosphate @125kg) and potassium@20kg (Muriate of potash@35kg) as a basal dose. At the time of sowing, apply one third of the Nitrogen dose along with Potassium and Single superphosphate. At the early stage of veins production i.e. one month of sowing apply rest of the dose.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cucumber,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME VARIETIES OF  CUCUMBER CROP?,"Punjab Kheera - 1 (2018): It is only recommended for poly-net houses. The plant is vigorous, producing 1-2 fruits per node. Flowers are parthenocarpic, and the fruits are dark green, seedless, bitter-free, medium in size (125 g), 13-15 cm long, and do not need to be peeled. The first fruit can be picked 45 and 60 days after sowing for September and January crops, respectively. Its average yield is 304 q/acre for September sown crop and 370 q/acre for January sown crop, respectively.

Punjab Naveen (2008): The plants have dark green leaves as having a rough surface. At edible maturity, the fruits are cylinderical with a smooth surface, light green in colour, bitter free, and very crispy, with a single seed. It is of higher quality due to its high dry matter and vitamin C content. From planting to harvesting, it takes 68 days.Taste, appearance, colour, size, and texture are all excellent. It has an average yield of 70 q/acre.

Other state varieties

Pusa Uday: The Indian Agricultural Research Institute created the variety (IARI). This varietys fruits are light green in colour, medium in size, and 15cm long. Per acre of land, use 1.45 kg of seed. The variety matures in 50-55 days. It has a yield of 65 qtl/acre on average.

Pusa Barkha: This variety was created for the Kharif season. It is extremely resistant to humidity, temperature, and downy mildew disease. It has a yield of 78 qtl/acre on average.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cucumber,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CUCUMBER VARIETIEY  PUNJAB KHEERA - 1 (2018)?,"Punjab Kheera - 1 (2018): It is only recommended for poly-net houses. The plant is vigorous, producing 1-2 fruits per node. Flowers are parthenocarpic, and the fruits are dark green, seedless, bitter-free, medium in size (125 g), 13-15 cm long, and do not need to be peeled. The first fruit can be picked 45 and 60 days after sowing for September and January crops, respectively. Its average yield is 304 q/acre for September sown crop and 370 q/acre for January sown crop, respectively.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cucumber,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CUCUMBER VARIETIEY  PUNJAB NAVEEN (2008)?,"Punjab Naveen (2008): The plants have dark green leaves as having a rough surface. At edible maturity, the fruits are cylinderical with a smooth surface, light green in colour, bitter free, and very crispy, with a single seed. It is of higher quality due to its high dry matter and vitamin C content. From planting to harvesting, it takes 68 days.Taste, appearance, colour, size, and texture are all excellent. It has an average yield of 70 q/acre.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cucumber,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CUCUMBER VARIETIEY  PUSA UDAY?,"
Pusa Uday: The Indian Agricultural Research Institute created the variety (IARI). This varietys fruits are light green in colour, medium in size, and 15cm long. Per acre of land, use 1.45 kg of seed. The variety matures in 50-55 days. It has a yield of 65 qtl/acre on average.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cucumber,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CUCUMBER VARIETIEY  PUSA BARKHA?,"Pusa Barkha: This variety was created for the Kharif season. It is extremely resistant to humidity, temperature, and downy mildew disease. It has a yield of 78 qtl/acre on average.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cucumber,Seeds,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SEED MANAGEMENT OF  CUCUMBER CROP?,"Seed rate:

Seed rate of 1.0 kg is sufficient for one acre of land.
 
Seed treatment:
Before sowing seeds, treat them with the suitable chemical to protect them from disease and pests and to increase viability. Seeds are treated with Captan@2gm before sowing.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cucumber,Seeds,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SEED TREATMENT OF  CUCUMBER CROP?,"Seed Treatment:
Before sowing seeds, treat them with the suitable chemical to protect them from disease and pests and to increase viability. Seeds are treated with Captan@2gm before sowing.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cucumber,Seeds,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SEED PRODUCTION OF  CUCUMBER CROP?,"Keep isolation distance of 1000m from other varieties of wild melon, muskmelon, snap melon and Cucumber. Remove disease infected plants from field. When fruits are mature i.e. they changes their color into dull. Then they are crushed with hands in fresh water and then separate seeds from pulp. Seeds which are settled in bottom are collected for seed purpose.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cucumber,Seeds,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FUNGICIDES OF CUCUMBER CROP?,"(Dosage per kg seed)
Carbendazim 2gm
Imidacloprid 5gm","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cucumber,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF ANTHRACNOSE   IN  CUCUMBER CROP?,"Anthracnose: It attacks almost all parts of the cucumber which are above the ground. The symptoms are yellowish color circular spots are seen on the older leaves and the circular and sunken spots are seen on the fruit.
Treatment: Fungicidal application of Chlorothalonil and benomyl is given to protect the crop from disease.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cucumber,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF BACTERIAL WILT  IN  CUCUMBER CROP?,"Bacterial wilt: It is caused by Erwinia tracheiphila. It affects the vascular tissues of the plant which result in immediate wilting.
Treatment: Spraying of foliar insecticides is done to cure the bacterial wilt.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cucumber,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF POWDERY MILDEW  IN  CUCUMBER CROP?,"Powdery mildew: The symptoms are appearance of white powdery spots on upper surface of leaves which causes leaf withering.
Treatment: Application of carbendazim@2gm in 1ltr of water will help to cure powdery mildew. It can also be controlled by fungicidal sprays of Chlorothalonil, benomyl or dinocap.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cucumber,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF MOSAIC  IN  CUCUMBER CROP?,"Mosaic: The symptoms are stunted growth of plant, leaves turn down and fruit knobs become light yellow in color.
Treatment: Application of Diazinon is done to cure mosaic disease. Use of Immidachloprid-17.8%SL @7ml in 10ltr of water is done to cure disease.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cucumber,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF FRUIT FLY  IN  CUCUMBER CROP?,"Fruit fly: It is serious pest found in cucumber. Females fly lay eggs below epidermis of young fruits. Later on maggots feed on pulp afterward fruits starts rotting and get drop.
Treatment: Foliar application of Neem oil @3.0%is given to cure the crop from fruit fly pest.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cucumber,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF FUNGAL DISEASES  IN  CUCUMBER CROP?,Spray 3 grams of Indofil M45 per liter of water to prevent fungal disease in cucumber.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Cucumber,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF APHIDS OR OTHER SUCKING PEST  IN  CUCUMBER CROP?,Spray 250 ml of malathionon or 200 ml of Rogor mixed with 100 liters of water for one acre to control sap-sucking insects in cucumber.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Cucumber,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF ROOT ROT  IN  CUCUMBER CROP?,"To prevent root rot in cucumber crop, mix 500 grams of clear (Carbendazim + Mancozeb) with 15-20 kg of sand and spread it per acre.","[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Cucumber,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF DUMPING DISEASES  IN  CUCUMBER CROP?,"Spray of 500 g Indofil Z-78, 75 WP in 200 liter water or Bavistin (carbendazim 50% wp) 3 gm/ liter water.","[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Cucumber,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF YELLOWNESS  IN  CUCUMBER CROP AFTER RAIN?,You can spray 500 gm M-45 in 200 liters of water to prevent leaf yellowing in cucumber.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Cucumber,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF LEAF MINER  IN  CUCUMBER CROP?,Spray Cucumber-Nagali-Nimboli extract 1500 ppm 2 ml/1 liter of water.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Cucumber,Plant Protection,"INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF THRIPS, APHIDS, JASSIDS  IN  CUCUMBER CROP?","Actra (Thiomithosome 25%) 5 gm/15 liter of water should be sprayed and after this spraying cucumber should not be taken to market for 8-10 days, thanks.","[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Cucumber,Fertilizer Uses,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SPRAY FOR FLOWERING IN  CUCUMBER CROP?,To increase the number of flowers - Boomflower should be sprayed with 30 ml / 15 liters of water.(Nitrobenzene 20%),"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Cucumber,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF BITTER  CUCUMBER CROP?,"Keep your cucumbers well watered to offset the tendency for them to turn bitter. Give them a deep soaking of at least an inch of water per week, more during extreme dry spells. Consider adding drip irrigation to ensure the plants receive adequate, consistent moisture.","[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Cucumber,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF VIRUS  IN  CUCUMBER CROP?,Remove the diseased plants from the cucumber crop and spray 400 ml of Melathion (oil to control whitefly) in 100 liters of water for one acre to prevent,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Cucumber,Nutrient Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FLOWERING ON CUCUMBER?,Boomflower should be taken in 30 ml / 15 liters of water and sprayed (Nitrobenzene 20%).,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Cucumber,Nutrient Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME NECESSARY NUTRITION OF CUCUMBER?,"NITROGEN--40kg/acre, PHOSPHORUS --20kg/acre, POTASH --20kg/acre
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cucumber,Nutrient Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CUCUMBER TOP DRESSING FERTILIZER MANAGEMENT?,Use urea 28 kg per acre,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Cucumber,Fertilizer Uses,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FERTILIZER REQUIREMENT IN CUCUMBER?,"UREA--90kg/acre, SSP--125kg/acre,MURIATE OF POTASH--35kg/acre
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Chilli,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CHILLI CROP?,"It is known as the most valuable crop of India. It is used as a principle ingredient of various curries and chutneys, also used in vegetables, spices, condiments, sauces and pickles. Pungency in chillies is due to the active constituent ""Capsaicin"", an alkaloid. The native home of chilli is considered to be Mexico with secondary origin of Guatemala. Chilli was introduced in India by the Portuguese in Goa in the middle of 17th century and since then it had rapidly spread throughout the country. Capsaicin has many medicinal properties, especially as an anti-cancerous agent and instant pain reliever. It also prevents heart diseases by dilating blood vessels. Major chilli growing countries are India, China, Pakistan, Indonesia, Korea, Turkey and Sri Lanka in Asia; Nigeria, Ghana, Tunisia and Egypt in Africa; Mexico, United States of America in North & Central America; Yugoslavia, Spain, Romania, Bulgaria, Italy and Hungary in Europe and Argentina, Peru and Brazil in South America. India is the world leader in chilli production followed by China & Pakistan. Andhra Pradesh, Maharashtra, Karnataka, Orissa, Tamil Nadu, Bihar, UP and Rajasthan are the main chilly growing states.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Chilli,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOWING TIME OF  CHILLI CROP?,The ideal time for raising nursery is from October end to mid of November. Cover the nursery area with 50 % shade net and cover the sides using 40 / 50 mesh insect proof nylon net. Seedlings are ready for transplantation in 30-40 days (Usually in February - March).,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Chilli,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SUITABLE TEMPARARTURE OF CHILLI CROPS?,"The suitable temparature: Sowing Temparature- 35-40 degree, 
Normal Temperature- 18-40 degree,Harvesting Temperature- 35-40 degree,Rainfall- 625-1500 mm
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
