Vegetables,Chilli,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CHILLI VARIETIEY BYADGI (KADDI):?,"Byadgi (Kaddi): Mild flavour, long and bright red color variety.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Chilli,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CHILLI VARIETIEY DABBI?,"Dabbi: Mild flavour, long and thick blackish variety.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Chilli,Seeds,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SEED MANAGEMENT OF  CHILLI CROP?,"Seed rate:

Seed rate of 1.0 kg is sufficient for one acre of land.
 
Seed treatment:
Before sowing seeds, treat them with the suitable chemical to protect them from disease and pests and to increase viability. Seeds are treated with Captan@2gm before sowing.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Chilli,Seeds,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SEED TREATMENT OF  CHILLI CROP?,"Seed Treatment:
Before sowing seeds, treat them with the suitable chemical to protect them from disease and pests and to increase viability. Seeds are treated with Captan@2gm before sowing.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Chilli,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF ANTHRACNOSE   IN  CHILLI CROP?,"Anthracnose: It is caused by the fungi Colletotrichum piperatum and C.capsici and is promoted by warm temperatures, high moisture. It is characterised by black spots that are formed on infected parts. Spots are usually circular, water-soaked and sunken with black margins. The fruits with many spots drop off prematurely resulting in heavy loss of yield.

If infestation of Anthracnose is observed then spraying with Propiconazole or Hexaconazole @1ml/Ltr of water should be done.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Chilli,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF BACTERIAL LEAF SPOT  IN  CHILLI CROP?,"Bacterial Leaf Spot: It is observed mostly in rainy season. On young leaves the spots are yellowish green, on older leaves they are dark and water soaked. Severely affected leaves become chlorotic and defoliation occurs. It observed on stem also. Stem infection leads to formation of cankerous growth and wilting of branches. On fruit round water soaked spots with pale yellow border is observed. 

To control various leaf spot and yellowing diseases, spray Propiconazole 25%EC@ 200ml or Chlorothalonil 75%WP @400-600gm per 150-200Ltr of water. If bacterial leaf spot infestation is observed, to control spray with Streptocycline@1gm +Copper oxychloride@400gm/200Ltr of water.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Chilli,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF POWDERY MILDEW  IN  CHILLI CROP?,"Powdery Mildew: Patchy, White powdery growth appears on lower side of leaves. It parasitizes the plant using it as a food source. It commonly occurs on older leaves just before or at fruit set. But it can develop at any stage of crop development. In severe infestation it causes defoliation.

Avoid water lodging in field. Keep field clean. To control spray with Hexaconazole(Contaf, Sitara) along with sticker @1 ml/Ltr of water. In case of sudden rain, chances of powdery mildew are more. Mild infestation take spray of water soluble Sulphur @ 20 gm/10 Ltr of water 2-3 times with interval of 10 days.

Phytophthora blight: It is caused by the fungus Phytophthora capsici. It is soil borne and commonly observed on soil with low drainage capacity and areas where proper Cultural Practices have not been maintained. Also cloudy weather is favourable for spread of this disease.
 
Avoid crop rotation with brinjal, tomato, cucumber, pumpkin for atleast three years. Spray with Copper oxychloride@250gm/150Ltr of water.

","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Chilli,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF YELLOW MOSAIC  IN  CHILLI CROP?,"Light and green patches observed on leaves. In early stage plant growth get stops. Yellowing, chlorotic ring spots on leaves and fruits. Select healthy and disease free seeds for cultivation. Avoid monocropping in chilly crop. Raise two rows of maize or sorghum for every five rows of chilly against wind direction. Uproot and destroyed infected plant away from field.

Recommendations given for aphids may be adopted (take spray of Acephate 75SP@1gm/Ltr or Methyl demeton 25EC@2ml/Ltr of water. Soil application of granular insecticides viz Carbofuran, Phorate@4-8kg/acre should be done on 15 and 60 days after transplanting.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Chilli,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF FRUIT BORER  IN  CHILLI CROP?,"Fruit borer: Caterpillar eat leaves of crop afterward they enter into fruit and caused heavy loss in yield management. Collect and destroyed damaged fruits and grown up caterpillars. Set up pheromone traps for Helicoverpa armigera or Spodoptera litura at 5 Nos./acre.

To control pod borers apply poison bait balls made up of bran-5 kg, Carbaryl-500 gm, Jaggery-500 gm and sufficient amount of water. If infestation of fruit borers is observed. spray Chlorpyrifos + Cypermethrin (Nurel-D/Amla) @30 ml+Teepol@0.5 ml in 12 Ltr of water with power sprayer. Spray with Emamectin benzoate 5% SG @4 gm/10 Ltr of water or Flubendiamide 20 WDG@6 gm/10 litre of water.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Chilli,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF MITE IN  CHILLI CROP?,"Mite: These are widely distributed pest observed throughout the world. It attacks on several crops like potato, chilli, beans, cotton, tobacco, curcurbit, castor, jute, coffee, lemon, citrus, blackgram, cowpea, pepper, tomato, sweet potato, mango, papaya, brinjal, guava. Nymphs and adults feed exclusively on the lower surface of the leaves. Infected leaves give cup shape appearance. Heavy infestation results in defoliation, bud shedding and drying of leaves.
 

If Infestation of yellow mite & thrips is observed in field, spray of Chlorfenapyr@1.5ml/Ltr, Abamectin@1.5ml/Ltr are found effective. Mite is a serious pest and it may cause yield loss up to 80%. For effective control spray Spiromesifen 22.9SC@200ml/acre/180Ltr of water.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Chilli,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF APHID IN CHILLI?,"Aphid: They attack mostly in winter month and later stage of crop. They suck sap from the leaf. They excrete honey like substance and developed sooty mold i.e blackish colour fungus on the calyx and pods thus deteriorate quality of product. Aphids also work as important insect vectors for chilli mosaic. Mosaic disease transmitted by aphids cause 20-30 percent loss in yield.

To control, take spray of Acephate 75SP@5gm/Ltr or Methyl demeton 25EC@2ml/Ltr of water. Soil application of granular insecticides viz Carbofuran, Phorate@4-8kg/acre on 15 and 60 days after transplanting were also effective.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Chilli,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF WHITE FLY IN CHILLI?,"White fly: The nymphs and adults of White fly suck the cell sap from the leaves and weaken the plants. They secrete honey dew on which black sooty mould develops on leaves. They also transmit leaf curl diseases. To check infestation use yellow sticky traps coated with grease and sticky oils.

In case of severe infestation to control take spray of Acetamiprid 20SP (@4gm/10Ltr of water or Triazophos@2.5ml/litre or Profenophos@2ml/litre of water. Repeat the spray after 15 days.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Chilli,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF THRIPS IN CHILLI?,"Thrips: Commonly observed pest. Mostly observed in dry weather. They suck sap from the foliage and results in curling of leaves. Also causes flower drop.
To check severity of thrips incidence, keep blue sticky traps @6-8 per acre. Also to reduce the incidence spray Verticillium lecani@5gm/Ltr water
If incidence of thrips is more, then take spray of Imidacloprid 17.8SL or Fipronil@1ml/Ltr water or Fipronil 80%WP@2.5ml/Ltr of water or Acephate 75% WP@1.0gm/Ltr or do drenching of Thiamethoxam 25% WG@1.0gm/Ltr of water.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Chilli,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF DIE BACK AND FRUIT ROT IN CHILLI?,"Die back and fruit rot: The branches and leaves get dried and black spots are formed on infected parts. Spots are usually circular, water-soaked and sunken with black margins. The fruits with many spots drop off prematurely resulting in heavy loss of yield. The disease spreads rapidly with blowing wind, rains during rainy season. Partially affected plants bear fruits which are few and of low quality.
Use disease free seeds. Before sowing seed treatment with Thiram or Captan@4gm/kg of seeds is effective in eliminating the seed borne inoculum. To control die back and fruit rot diseases spray with Mancozeb@2.5gm or Copper oxychloride@3gm per Ltr of water. Give first spray just before flowering and second at the time of fruit formation.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Chilli,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF CATERPILLER IN CHILLI?,Spray 400 ml of Acalx mixed with 100 liters of water for prevention of caterpiller in chilies.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Chilli,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL LEAF CURL VIRUS IN CHILI?,Remove the diseased plants from the field and spray 400 ml of Malathion (to control whitefly) or 250 ml of Roger 30 EC (Dimethoate) in 100 liters of water per acre to prevent the spread of the disease.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Chilli,Plant Protection,"INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF  JASSID, APHIDS AND WHITEFLY IN CHILI CROP?",Mix 400 ml of Melathion (to control oil and whitefly) in 100 liters of water and spray one acre.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Chilli,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME GROWTH OF CHILLIES?,"You can spray NPK 19:19:19, 1 kg in 100 liters of water.","[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Chilli,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FRUIT ROT IN CHILLIES?,pray 250 ml Folikar or 750 g Indofil M45 or Blytox in 250 liters of water per acre for fruit and branch rot in chillies.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Chilli,Nutrient Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME  GROWTH REGULATOR USED IN CHILLI CROP?,Growth Regulator used in Chilli crop spray in May-June of Napthalene acetic acid (NAA) 4g in 10-15ml ethyl alcohol per liter or Planofix 1ml in 4.5lt water at 10 days interval.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Chilli,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME  INCREASING FLOWERING IN CHILLIES?,To increase the quantity of flowers in chilli crop :-Bumflower should be taken in 30 ml/15 liters of water and sprayed. (Nitrobenzene 20 %),"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Chilli,Nutrient Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FOLIAR SPRAY IN CHILLI?,Mix a liter of water 19: 19: 19 fertilizer 2g and spray it.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Chilli,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME DAMPING OFF DISEASE MANAGEMENT IN CHILLI NURSERY?,"Damping-off is controlled primarily through good sanitation, high quality planting material, and proper cultural and environmental controls. Damping-off is worse when soil is wet or compacted. Prepare planting beds so that the soil has good drainage.","[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Chilli,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME  BLIGHT ATTACK ON CHILLI?,Carbendazim 12% + Mancozeb 63% 30 gms / 15 liters of water should be sprayed,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Chilli,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME ATTACK OF WHITE FLY ON CHILLI CROP?,Spray Flonicamid 100 gm/200 liters of water.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Chilli,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CHILLI HYBRID VARIETY SEED RATE?,80 - 100 g / acre,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Chilli,Nutrient Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CHILLI BASAL FERTILIZER MANAGEMENT?,Use urea 4 kg + dap 50 kg + potash 20 kg per acre.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Chilli,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF DIE BACK AND ALSO FRUIT ROT IN CHILLI?,Spray Lambda Psylothrene (Karate) 20 ml /15 liters of water,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Chilli,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF WHITE GRAB IN CHILLI?,Chlorpyrifos 2ml/1 liter of water should be sprayed.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Chilli,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF SUCKING PEST IN CHILLI?,Ullala (Flonikamid 50 WG ) 8 gm/15 liter of water should be sprayed.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Chilli,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF WILT AND DAMPING OFF IN CHILLI?,"Wilt and damping off: Moist and poorly drain soil causes damping off disease. It is soil borne disease. Water soaking and shrivelling of stem occurs. Seedlings killed before emergence. If it appears in nursery the entire lot of seedling may get destroyed.

To control wilt, drench nearby soil with Copper oxychloride@250gm or Carbendazim@200gm/150Ltr of water. To control wilting of plants due to root rot do drenching with Trichoderma bio fungus@2.5kg/500Ltr water, near to roots of plants.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Chilli,Nutrient Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME NECESSARY NUTRITION OF CHILLI?,"NITROGEN--25kg/acre, PHOSPHORUS --12kg/acre, POTASH --12kg/acre
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Chilli,Fertilizer Uses,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FERTILIZER REQUIREMENT IN CHILLI?,"UREA--55kg/acre, SSP--75kg/acre,MURIATE OF POTASH--20kg/acre
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cauliflower,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CAULIFLOWER CROP?,"Cauliflower is popular vegetable and this belongs to family Cruciferous. It work as anti-cancer agent. It promotes heart health, lower cholesterol levels. The major cauliflower producing states are Bihar, Uttar Pradesh, Orissa, West Bengal, Assam, Haryana and Maharashtra.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cauliflower,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOWING TIME OF  CAULIFLOWER CROP?,"For early season variety June-July is best transplanting time, For main season variety August to mid-September and October to first week of November is best transplanting for late varieties.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cauliflower,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SUITABLE TEMPARARTURE OF CAULIFLOWER CROPS?,"The suitable temparature: Sowing Temparature- 25-30 degree, 
Normal Temperature- 12-30 degree,Harvesting Temperature- 12-18 degree,Rainfall- 120-125mm
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cauliflower,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOWING TEMPARARTURE OF CAULIFLOWER CROPS?,Sowing Temparature- 25-30 degree,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cauliflower,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME NORMAL TEMPARARTURE OF CAULIFLOWER CROPS?,Normal Temperature- 12-30 degree,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cauliflower,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME HARVESTING TEMPARARTURE OF CAULIFLOWER CROPS?,Harvesting Temperature- 12-18 degree,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cauliflower,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME RAINFALL OF CAULIFLOWER CROPS?,Rainfall- 120-125mm,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cauliflower,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOIL MANAGEMENT OF  CAULIFLOWER CROP?,"It can grow well in wide range of soil from sandy loam to clay. For late sown variety, clay loam soils are preferred and for early maturing varieties sandy loam soil is recommended. pH of soil should be in range of 6 to 7. Add lime in case of low pH soil.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cauliflower,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FIELD PREPARATION OF  CAULIFLOWER CROP?,Bring soil to fine tilth by ploughing land thoroughly. Add well decomposed cow dung and mixed well in soil at time of last ploughing.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cauliflower,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SPACING OF  CAULIFLOWER CROP?,"Spacing:Use spacing of 45x45 cm for main season crop whereas for early and late maturing crop use spacing of 45x30 cm.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cauliflower,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOWING DEPTH OF  CAULIFLOWER CROP?,"Sowing Depth:Sow seeds at depth of 1-2 cm.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cauliflower,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME HARVESTING OF  CAULIFLOWER CROP?,After developing proper head harvesting can be done. Carry out harvesting in morning or evening time. After harvesting keep product in cool place.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cauliflower,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME POST HARVESTING OF  CAULIFLOWER CROP?,"After harvesting, do sorting and grading depending upon curd size.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cauliflower,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME METHOD OF SOWING OF  CAULIFLOWER CROP?,"Method of sowing: For Sowing dibbling method and transplanting methods can be used.
Sow seeds in nursery and apply irrigation, fertilizer dose as per requirement. Seedlings are ready to transplant within 25-30 days after sowing. For transplantation use three to four weeks old seedlings.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cauliflower,Water Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WATER MANAGEMENT OF  CAULIFLOWER CROP?,"Immediately after transplanting, give first irrigation. Depending upon soil, climatic condition, apply irrigation at interval of 7-8 days in summer season and 10-15 days during winter season.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cauliflower,Weed Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WEED MANAGEMENT OF  CAULIFLOWER CROP?,To check weed control apply Fluchloralin (Basalin)800ml/150-200 Ltr water before transplantation followed by hand weeding 30 to 40 days after transplanting. Apply Pendimethalin@1 Ltr/acre one day before transplanting of seedlings.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cauliflower,Fertilizer Uses,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME BETTER/GOOD/FERTILIZER USE S OF  CAULIFLOWER CROP?,"Apply well decomposed cow dung@40 tonnes per acre in soil along with Nitrogen@50 kg, Phophorus@25 kg and Potash@25 kg in form of Urea@110 kg, Single Superphosphate@155 kg and Muriate of Potash@40 kg. Apply whole quantity of cowdung, SSP and MOP and half quantity of Urea before transplanting. Apply remaining quantity of Urea four week after transplanting as top dressing. 

To get better flower (Curd) set and to obtain good yield, spray Water Soluble Fertilizer (19:19:19)@5-7 gm/Ltr water during the early plant growth. 40 days after transplanting take spray of 12:61:00@4-5 gram + microneutrients@2.5 to 3 gram + Boron@1 gm per Ltr water. To improve curd quality, apply Water Soluble Fertilizer 13:00:45@8-10 gm/Ltr of water at the time of curd development.

Do soil testing and if Magnesium deficiency is observed to overcome Mg deficiency apply Magnesium sulphate@5 gm/Ltr, 30-35 days after transplantation and for Calcium deficiency apply Calcium Nitrate@5 gm/Ltr, 30-35 days after transplanting.

If Hollow and sometimes discolored stems are observed, Also curds become brown and leaves may get roll and curl it is due to Boron deficiency, apply Borax@250 gm-400 gm/acre.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cauliflower,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME VARIETIES OF  CAULIFLOWER CROP?,"Pusa Snowball 1: Crop get ready to harvest in 100 days after transplanting. Outer leaves are upright and curd is compact, of medium size. Color of curd is snow white. It produces yield of 90 qtl per acre. 

Pusa Snowball K-1: Crop get mature late compared to Pusa snowball 1. Outer leaves are upright and curd is compact. Curd is of snow white color. It gives yield of 90 qtl/acre.

Other state varieties:

Snowball 16: Late maturing variety. Curds are compact having attractive white color. Gives average yield of 100-125 qtl/acre.

Pant Shubhra: Early maturing variety, suitable for cultivation in Northern India. Curds are of creamy white color. Gives average yield of 80 qtl/acre.

Early Kunwari: Early maturing variety, suitable for cultivation in Haryana, Punjab and Delhi. Gives average yield of 32 qtl/acre.

Pusa Deepali: Developed by IARI, early maturing variety, suitable for cultivation in Northern India. Medium size curd having white color. Gives average yield of 48 qtl/acre.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cauliflower,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CAULIFLOWER VARIETIEY  PUSA SNOWBALL 1?,"Pusa Snowball 1: Crop get ready to harvest in 100 days after transplanting. Outer leaves are upright and curd is compact, of medium size. Color of curd is snow white. It produces yield of 90 qtl per acre.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cauliflower,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CAULIFLOWER VARIETIEY  PUSA SNOWBALL K-1?,"Pusa Snowball K-1: Crop get mature late compared to Pusa snowball 1. Outer leaves are upright and curd is compact. Curd is of snow white color. It gives yield of 90 qtl/acre.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cauliflower,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CAULIFLOWER VARIETIEY  SNOWBALL 16?,Snowball 16: Late maturing variety. Curds are compact having attractive white color. Gives average yield of 100-125 qtl/acre.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cauliflower,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CAULIFLOWER VARIETIEY  PANT SHUBHRA?,"Pant Shubhra: Early maturing variety, suitable for cultivation in Northern India. Curds are of creamy white color. Gives average yield of 80 qtl/acre.: Early maturing variety, suitable for cultivation in Northern India. Curds are of creamy white color. Gives average yield of 80 qtl/acre.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cauliflower,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CAULIFLOWER VARIETIEY  EARLY KUNWARI?,"Early Kunwari: Early maturing variety, suitable for cultivation in Haryana, Punjab and Delhi. Gives average yield of 32 qtl/acre.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cauliflower,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CAULIFLOWER VARIETIEY  PUSA DEEPALI?,"Pusa Deepali: Developed by IARI, early maturing variety, suitable for cultivation in Northern India. Medium size curd having white color. Gives average yield of 48 qtl/acre.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cauliflower,Seeds,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SEED MANAGEMENT OF  CAULIFLOWER CROP?,"Seeds Rate
For early season variety seed rate of 500 gm is required whereas for late and main season variety seed rate of 250 gm per acre is required.

Seed Treatment
Before sowing dip seeds in hot water (50 for 30 min) or streptocycline@0.01 gm/Ltr for two hours. After treatment dry them in shade and then sow on bed. Blackrot mostly observed in Rabi. As a preventive measure seed treatment with mercury chloride is essential. For that dip seeds in Mercury chloride@1 gm/Ltr solution for 30 min after that dry them in shed. Crop grown in sandy soils are more prone to stem rot. To prevent it do seed treatment with Carbendazim 50%WP@3 gm/kg of seeds.

","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cauliflower,Seeds,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SEED TREATMENT OF  CAULIFLOWER CROP?,"Seed Treatment:
Before sowing dip seeds in hot water (50 for 30 min) or streptocycline@0.01 gm/Ltr for two hours. After treatment dry them in shade and then sow on bed. Blackrot mostly observed in Rabi. As a preventive measure seed treatment with mercury chloride is essential. For that dip seeds in Mercury chloride@1 gm/Ltr solution for 30 min after that dry them in shed. Crop grown in sandy soils are more prone to stem rot. To prevent it do seed treatment with Carbendazim 50%WP@3 gm/kg of seeds.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cauliflower,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF SUCKING PEST   IN  CAULIFLOWER CROP?,"Sucking pest: They suck the sap from the leaves resulting in yellowing and drooping of leaves. Thrips results in curling of leaves, leaves become cup shaped or curved upward.

If incidence of sucking pest like Aphid and Jassid is observed take spray of Imidacloprid 17.8SL@60ml/acre using 150 Ltr water. If infestation of Thrips is observed take Spray of Triazophos + Deltamethrin@20 ml or 25% Cypermethrin @5 ml/10 Ltr of water.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cauliflower,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF DIAMOND BACK MOTH  IN  CAULIFLOWER CROP?,"Diamond back moth: Serious pest of cauliflower. They lay eggs under surface leaves. larva of greenish color with hair on body feed on leaves and make hole. In case of lack of proper control measures, it causes loss upto 80-90%.

At initial stage take spray of Neem Seed Kernel Extract@40 gm/Ltr of water at head initiation stage. Repeat this spray with interval of 10-15 days. Avoid spraying at curd formation. Take spray of Bt formulations@200 gm/acre at 35 and 50 days after planting. In severe infestation take spray of Spinosad 2.5%SC@80ml/150Ltr of water.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cauliflower,Plant Protection,"INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF 
CATERPILLAR  IN  CAULIFLOWER CROP?","Caterpillar: They feed on leaves and damage crop. 

Spodoptera infestation mostly observed after rains. If per crop two caterpillars are observed then spray with B.T@10 gm/10 Ltr water in evening time. After that take neem ark@40 gm/Ltr spray. In case of high infestation take spray of Thiodicarb 75WP@40 gm/15 Ltr water. If infestation of leaf eating caterpillars is observed take spray of 60 ml Spinosad 2.5%EC or 100 gm Emamectin Benzoate 5SG/acre/150 Ltr","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cauliflower,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF WILT  IN  CAULIFLOWER CROP?,"Wilt: Dropping of entire leaves along with yellowing of crops. Wilting or drying of entire plant is seen. It may be due to root rot. To control wilt cause due to root rot, drench Trichoderma bio fungus@2.5 kg/500 Ltr water, near to roots of plants. Keeping checking crop losses due to fungal diseases. Drench root zone with Ridomil gold@2.5 gm/Ltr water. Give need based irrigation. Avoid flood irrigation.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cauliflower,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF DOWNY MILDEW  IN  CAULIFLOWER CROP?,"Downy Mildew. Appearance of purplish-brown spots observed on lower side of leaves along with greyish white mold on leafs underside. Sanitation and crop rotation help in reducing infection. If infestation of downy is observed, it can be controlled by combined spraying of (Metalaxyl + Mancozeb)@2gm per litre. Take three sprays with 10 days interval.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cauliflower,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF LEAF SPOT AND BLIGHT IN CAULIFLOWER?,Leaf spot and Blight: If infestation of blight is observed to control take spray of Mancozeb or Copper oxychloride @300gm/150 Ltr along with 20 ml sticker.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cauliflower,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF CATERPILLER IN CAULIFLOWER?,Spray 70 g of Proclam or Success (Spinosed 2.5 SC) 100 ml of Sumicidin 20 EC (Fenvalerate) or 200 ml of Avat (Indoxacarb 15.8 EC) or Corazine 50 ml in 100 liters of water to prevent caterpiller in cauliflower.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Cauliflower,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF ALTERNARIA LEAF SPOT IN CAULIFLOWER?,Alternaria leaf spot: Remove and burn lower leaves in morning subsequent take spray of tebuconazole 50%+ Trifloxystrobin 25%@120 gm/acre or Mancozeb@2gm/lit or Carbendazim@1gm/lit of water.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cauliflower,Nutrient Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME THE BETTER YIELD OF CAULIFLOWER?,For good yield of cauliflower you can spray 10 grams of NPK 13:00:45 per liter of water.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Cauliflower,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME IMPROVED VARIETIES OF CAULIFLOWER?,The advanced varieties of cauliflower are Pusa Snowball 1 and Pusa Snowball K1.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Cauliflower,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL MEMATURITY TIME OF CAULIFLOWER?,Cauliflower Pusa Snowball-1 variety is ready 100 days after transplanting and Pusa Snowball K-1 variety is ready after one week.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Cauliflower,Nutrient Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF  DEFICIENCY IN CAULIFLOWER?,"If boron is deficient in cabbage crop, add 200 grams of boron in 100 liters of water and spray per acre.","[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Cauliflower,Nutrient Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME NECESSARY NUTRITION OF CAULIFLOWER?,"NITROGEN--50kg/acre, PHOSPHORUS --25kg/acre, POTASH --25 kg/acre
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cauliflower,Fertilizer Uses,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FERTILIZER REQUIREMENT IN CAULIFLOWER?,"UREA--110kg/acre, SSP--155kg/acre,MURIATE OF POTASH--40 kg/acre
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Carrot,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CARROT CROP?,"Carrot ""annual"" or ""biannual"" herb belongs to family of Umbelliferae and it is native of ""Europe"". It is a great source of Vitamin A. Carrot is major vegetable crop of India. Haryana, Andhra Pradesh, Karnataka, Punjab and Uttar Pradesh are major carrot growing states.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Carrot,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOWING TIME OF  CARROT CROP?,August-September is best time for sowing local (desi) varieties of carrots whereas October-November month is ideal for European varieties.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Carrot,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SUITABLE TEMPARARTURE OF CARROT CROPS?,"The suitable temparature: Sowing Temparature- 18-23 degree, 
Normal Temperature- 7-23 degree,Harvesting Temperature- 20-25 degree,Rainfall- 75-100cm
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Carrot,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOWING TEMPARARTURE OF CARROT CROPS?,Sowing Temparature- 18-23 degree,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Carrot,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME NORMAL TEMPARARTURE OF CARROT CROPS?,Normal Temperature- 7-23 degree,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Carrot,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME HARVESTING TEMPARARTURE OF CARROT CROPS?,Harvesting Temperature- 20-25 degree,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Carrot,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME RAINFALL OF CARROT CROPS?,Rainfall- 75-100cm,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Carrot,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SUITABLE TIME OF  CARROT CROP?,August-September is best time for sowing local (desi) varieties of carrots whereas October-November month is ideal for European varieties.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Carrot,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOIL MANAGEMENT OF  CARROT CROP?,"For good root development carrot required deep, loose loamy soils. Heavy soils as well as very loose soils are not suitable for carrot cultivation. For optimum yield pH of soil should be in range of 5.5 to 7 (pH of 6.5 is ideal for good yield).","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Carrot,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FIELD PREPARATION OF  CARROT CROP?,Plough land thoroughly and make land weed and clods free. Add well decomposed cow dung of 10 ton/acre and mix well in soils at time of land preparation. Avoid use of undecomposed or free cow dung as it will leads to forking of fleshy roots.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Carrot,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SPACING OF  CARROT CROP?,"Spacing:Use row to row spacing of 45 cm and plant to plant spacing of 7.5 cm.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Carrot,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOWING DEPTH OF  CARROT CROP?,"Sowing Depth:For good growth, sow seeds at depth of 1.5 cm
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Carrot,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME HARVESTING OF  CARROT CROP?,"Depending upon variety, carrots are ready for harvesting in 90-100 days after sowing. Harvesting is done manually by uprooting plants. After harvesting remove green tops from carrots and then they are washed with water.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Carrot,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME POST HARVESTING OF  CARROT CROP?,After harvesting grading of carrot depending upon size is carried out. Then they are packed in gunny bags or basket.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Carrot,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME METHOD OF SOWING OF  CARROT CROP?,Method of sowing: For sowing use dibbling method and also use broadcasting method.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Carrot,Water Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WATER MANAGEMENT OF  CARROT CROP?,"After sowing, apply first irrigation, it will help in good germination. Depending upon soil type and climate, apply remaining irrigations at interval of 6-7 days in summer and 10-12 days interval in winter month. Overall carrot required three to four irrigations. Avoid excessive irrigation as it will leads misshape of roots and numerous hair growth. Stop irrigation two to three weeks before harvesting, It will help in increase in sweetness and taste of carrot.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Carrot,Weed Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WEED MANAGEMENT OF  CARROT CROP?,Take interculture operation like weeding and hoeing to keep check on weed growth also to provide soil aeration.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Carrot,Fertilizer Uses,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME BETTER/GOOD/FERTILIZER USE S OF  CARROT CROP?,"Along with well decomposed cowdung, apply Nitrogen@25kg (in form of Urea@55kg), Phosphorus@12kg (in form of SSP@ 75kg/acre) and Potash@30kg (in form of MOP@50kg) per acre in soil at time of sowing. Potash is required for good development of roots.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Carrot,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME VARIETIES OF  CARROT CROP?,"PC 34: Red color variety having dark green leaves. Length of root is about 25 cm and root diameter is about 3.15 cm.TSS content is 8.8%. It is ready for harvesting in 90 days after sowing. Gives average yield of 204 qtl/acre.

Punjab Black beauty: Roots are purple black with dark green leaves. It is a rich source of anthocyanins and phenols which protect from cancer. TSS content is about 7.5%. It is ready for harvesting in 93 days after sowing. Gives average yield of 196 qtl/acre. Fresh carrots are used for salad, juice, pickle and Kanji.

Punjab Carrot Red: It gives an average yield of 230qtl/acre. 

Other state varieties:

Exotic Varieties: 1) USA - Red cored chantenay, Danvers half long, Imperator. 2) New Zealand: Akaroa long red, spring market improved, Wanganui giant. 3)Japan: Suko 4)Belgium : Belgium white 5)Netherlands: Early Horn 6) Australia: Red elephant, western red, yellow 7) France: Chantenay, Nantes, oxheart

Pusa Kesar: Red colored carrot variety, developed at IARI, New Delhi. Ready to harvest in 90-110 days and gives average yield of 120 qtl/acre.

Pusa Meghali: Orange colored carrot variety, developed at IARI, New Delhi. Gives average yield of 100-120 qtl/acre.

New Kuroda: Hybrid suitable for plain as well as hilly areas.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Carrot,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CARROT VARIETIEY  PC 34?,"PC 34: Red color variety having dark green leaves. Length of root is about 25 cm and root diameter is about 3.15 cm.TSS content is 8.8%. It is ready for harvesting in 90 days after sowing. Gives average yield of 204 qtl/acre.

