Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Capsicum,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CAPSICUM VARIETIEY INDRA?,Indra: The fruits are dark green in color. It gives an average yield of 110qtl/acre. The average weight of fruit id 80gm.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Capsicum,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CAPSICUM IMPROVED VARIETIES?,"California Wonder, Chinese Giant, World Beater, Yolo Wonder Bharat, ArkaMohini, ArkaGaurav, ArkaBasant, Early Giant. Bullnose, King of North, Ruby King, etc. are the important varieties of capsicum grown in India.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Capsicum,Seeds,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SEED MANAGEMENT OF  CAPSICUM CROP?,"Seed rate:
Use seed rate of 200-300 gm for one acre of land.

Seed treatment:
Soak the seeds in Thiram or Captan, Ceresan etc. @2gm/kg of seeds before sowing to prevent the crops from seed borne diseases.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Capsicum,Seeds,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SEED TREATMENT OF  CAPSICUM CROP?,"Seed Treatment:
Soak the seeds in Thiram or Captan, Ceresan etc. @2gm/kg of seeds before sowing to prevent the crops from seed borne diseases.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Capsicum,Seeds,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME NURSERY MANAGEMENT AND TRANPLANTING OF CAPSICUM CROP?,"For capsicum farming, nursery beds are raised firstly. Seed beds of 300 x 60 x 15cm are prepared to raise seedlings. Seeds are sown in raised nursery beds and after sowing cover the nursery beds with thin layer of soil manure. Light irrigation is necessary after sowing the seeds in raising beds for optimum germination of seeds.

Transplanting is done when seedlings attain 4-5 leaves. Transplanting is done in prepared fields. Transplanting is mainly done in evening during cloudy weather. Mainly 50-60 old seedlings are used for transplanting.

Apply water to the nursery beds before transplanting so that seedling can be easily uprooted.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Capsicum,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF DAMPING OFF   IN  CAPSICUM CROP?,"Damping off: It is a fungal disease which affects the young seedlings. The symptoms are patches shown on the stem which ultimately shrivel and then die. They affect the whole crop within 4-5 days. The diseases mainly occur when crop is grown in poor drained soils.
Treatment: Spraying of Bordeaux mixture @0.5-1.0% or any copper oxychloride mixture such as Blitox or Fytolan will help to get rid of damping off.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Capsicum,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF ANTHRACNOSE  IN  CAPSICUM CROP?,"Anthracnose: It is a fungal disease which affects the stem, leaves and fruits of the crop. The symptoms are dark and round spots on fruits and black color minute spots are seen on the seeds. After some time the infected fruits will drop prematurely. The disease is mostly infected in high humidity.
Treatment: Seed treatment is must before sowing the seeds. Seeds are treated with Thiram @0.2% or Brassico @0.2% to prevent from anthracnose disease. If disease occurs then spray of Dithane(M-45) or Blitox @0.4% or Difoltan @0.2% is done at the interval of 15 days.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Capsicum,Plant Protection,"INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF 
POWDERY MILDEW  IN  CAPSICUM CROP?","Powdery mildew: The disease mainly occurs in summers. The symptoms are white talcum powder like growth is seen on the leaf, stunted growth and leaves get shed.
Treatment: Spraying of Sulfex @0.2% or Tridemorph@0.2% is done at the interval of 15 days is done to get rid of powdery mildew.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Capsicum,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF BACTERIAL WILT  IN  CAPSICUM CROP?,"Bacterial wilt: The symptoms are rapid growth of wilting on leaves as well as on fruits.
Treatment: Application of bleaching powder @15kg before will help to prevent bacterial wilt. Use of resistant varieties such as rka Gauravwill help to prevent disease.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Capsicum,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF LEAF CURL DISEASE  IN  CAPSICUM CROP?,"Leaf curl disease: The symptoms are leaf curling, blistering of interveinal areas and thickening of mid vein of leaves.
Treatment: The plants showing this should be uprooted to prevent further infection.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Capsicum,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF THRIPS IN CAPSICUM?,"Thrips: The symptoms are white blotches seen on leaves and stunted growth.
Treatment: Spraying of Malathion(Cythion 50 EC @1.5ml/ltr of water) or Dimethoate (Rogor 30 EC @ 2ml/ltr of water). The pest can also be controlled by spraying of Nicotine sulphate @0.25%.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Capsicum,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF APHIDS IN CAPSICUM?,"Aphids: They destroy the plant by feeding themselves on cell sap of leaves.
Treatment: Application of Monocrotophos @0.05-0.01% or Demeton methyl @0.05-0.02% will help to get rid from aphids.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Capsicum,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF MITES IN CAPSICUM?,"Mites: They are tiny spider like creatures which feed in leaves of capsicum.
Treatment: Spraying of cypermethrin 5 EC @3ml/ltr will help to control mites. Spraying of Dimethoate (Rogor @2ml/ltr) or Dicofol (Kelthane @1.5ml/ltr of water) is also effective to control mites.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Capsicum,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF BLIGHT ATTACK IN CAPSICUM?,Blue Copper (copper oxychloride 50% WP) - 40 g/15 liters of water should be sprayed.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Capsicum,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF FRUIT ROT ATTACK IN CAPSICUM?,Spray 250 ml Folikar or 750 g Indofil M45 or Blytox in 250 liters of water per acre for fruit and branch rot in pepper.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Capsicum,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FERTILIZER USED IN CAPSICUM?,"For capsicum crop, apply 37 kg urea, 175 kg superphosphate and 20 kg potash at sowing and 73 kg urea divided into two equal parts and applied in the field one and two months after planting.","[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Capsicum,Nutrient Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME NECESSARY NUTRITION OF CAPSICUM?,"NITROGEN--50kg/acre, p2o5 --25kg/acre, k2o--12 kg/acre
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Capsicum,Nutrient Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FOR BETTER GROWTH OF CAPSICUM?,"For good growth of capsicum, you can spray one kg of NPK 19:19:19 by mixing it in liter of water.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Capsicum,Fertilizer Uses,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FERTILIZER REQUIREMENT IN CAPSICUM?,"UREA--110kg/acre, SSP--175kg/acre,MURIATE OF POTASH--20 kg/acre
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cabbage,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CABBAGE CROP?,"It is leafy green or purple plant grown as annual vegetable crop. These are rich source of vitamin A and C also it contains minerals like phosphorus, potassium, calcium, sodium and iron. Cabbage can be eaten as raw as well as in cook form. In India, cabbage is grown mainly in winter in the plains region.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cabbage,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOWING TIME OF  CABBAGE CROP?,"September to October is ideal planting time in plain areas.

","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cabbage,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SUITABLE TEMPARARTURE OF CABBAGE CROPS?,"The suitable temparature: Sowing Temparature- 25-30 degree, 
Normal Temperature- 12-30 degree,Harvesting Temperature- 10-15 degree (summer),21-26 degree (winter),Rainfall- 300-600mm
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cabbage,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOWING TEMPARARTURE OF CABBAGE CROPS?,Sowing Temparature- 25-30 degree,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cabbage,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME NORMAL TEMPARARTURE OF CABBAGE CROPS?,Normal Temperature- 12-30 degree,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cabbage,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME HARVESTING TEMPARARTURE OF CABBAGE CROPS?,"Harvesting Temperature- 10-15 degree (summer),21-26 degree (winter)","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cabbage,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME RAINFALL OF CABBAGE CROPS?,Rainfall- 300-600mm,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cabbage,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SUITABLE TIME OF  CABBAGE CROP?,"September to October is ideal planting time in plain areas.


","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cabbage,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOIL MANAGEMENT OF  CABBAGE CROP?,"It can be grown on wide range of soil, but gives best result when grown on well drained loamy soil having good moisture holding capacity. pH of soil should be in range of 5.5 to 6.5. It cannot thrives well in highly acidic soils.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cabbage,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FIELD PREPARATION OF  CABBAGE CROP?,Bring soil to fine tilth by ploughing land thoroughly. Give ploughing for 3-4times then do levelling of soil. Add well decomposed cow dung and mixed well in soil at time of last ploughing.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cabbage,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SPACING OF  CABBAGE CROP?,"Spacing:Use spacing of 45 x 45 cm for early season crop whereas for late maturing crop use spacing of 60 x 45 cm.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cabbage,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOWING DEPTH OF  CABBAGE CROP?,Sowing Depth:Sow seeds at depth of 1-2 cm.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cabbage,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME HARVESTING OF  CABBAGE CROP?,When head reach to full size and having firm texture. Harvesting can be done on basis of market need. In case of high demand and offers high price the crop is harvested early. Harvesting is done with help of knife.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cabbage,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME POST HARVESTING OF  CABBAGE CROP?,"After harvesting, do sorting and grading depending upon head size.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cabbage,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME METHOD OF SOWING OF  CABBAGE CROP?,"Method of sowing: For Sowing dibbling method and transplanting methods can be used.
Sow seeds in nursery and apply irrigation, fertilizer dose as per requirement. Seedlings are ready to transplant within 25-30 days after sowing. For transplantation use three to four weeks old seedlings.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cabbage,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME TRANSPLANTING TIME OF CABBAGE?,Season of transplanting- October-November.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cabbage,Water Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WATER MANAGEMENT OF  CABBAGE CROP?,"Immediately after transplanting, give first irrigation. Depending upon soil, climatic condition, apply irrigation at interval of 10-15 days during winter season. Give adequate quantity of water to young seedling in vegetative stage. Heavy watering after head formation cause cracking of heads.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cabbage,Weed Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WEED MANAGEMENT OF  CABBAGE CROP?,Apply Pendimethalin@1Ltr/acre four day before transplanting of seedlings followed one hand weeding after herbicide application.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cabbage,Fertilizer Uses,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME BETTER/GOOD/FERTILIZER USE S OF  CABBAGE CROP?,"Apply well decomposed cow dung@40 tonnes per acre in soil along with Nitrogen@50kg, Phophorus@25kg and Potash@25kg in form of Urea@110kg, Single Superphosphate@155kg and Muriate of Potash@40kg. Apply whole quantity of cowdung, SSP and MOP and half quantity of Urea before transplanting. Apply remaining quantity of Urea four week after transplanting as top dressing. 

To get better flower (Curd) set and to obtain good yield, spray Water Soluble Fertilizer (19:19:19)@5-7gm/Ltr water during the early plant growth. 40days after transplanting take spray of 12:61:00@4-5gram + micronutrients@2.5 to 3 gram + Boron@1gm per Ltr water. To improve curd quality, apply Water Soluble Fertilizer 13:00:45@8-10gm/Ltr of water at the time of curd development.

Do soil testing and if Magnesium deficiency is observed to overcome Mg deficiency apply Magnesium sulphate@5gm/Ltr, 30-35 days after transplantation and for Calcium deficiency apply Calcium Nitrate@5gm/Ltr, 30-35 days after transplanting.

If Hollow and sometimes discolored stems are observed, Also curds become brown and leaves may get roll and curl it is due to Boron deficiency, apply Borax@250gm-400gm/acre.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cabbage,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CABBAGE VARIETIES?,"Popular varieties of Cabbage: Golden Acre, Pusa Mukta, Pusa Drumhead, K-1, Pride of India, Kopan hagen, Ganga, Pusa Synthetic, Shriganesh Gol, Hariana, Kaveri, Bajrang.

Midseason Market, September Early, Early Drum head, Late large drum head, K1.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cabbage,Seeds,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SEED MANAGEMENT OF  CABBAGE CROP?,"Seed Rate
For sowing use seed rate of 200-250 gm per acre is required.

Seed Treatment
Before sowing dip seeds in hot water (50 for 30 min) or streptocycline@0.01gm/Ltr for two hours. After treatment dry them in shade and then sow on bed. Blackrot mostly observed in Rabi. As a preventive measure seed treatment with Mercury chloride is essential. For that dip seeds in Mercury chloride@1gm/Ltr solution for 30 min after that dry them in shed. Crop grown in sandy soils are more prone to stem rot. To prevent it do seed treatment with Carbendazim 50%WP@3gm/kg seed.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cabbage,Seeds,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SEED TREATMENT OF  CABBAGE CROP?,"Seed Treatment:
Before sowing dip seeds in hot water (50 for 30 min) or streptocycline@0.01gm/Ltr for two hours. After treatment dry them in shade and then sow on bed. Blackrot mostly observed in Rabi. As a preventive measure seed treatment with Mercury chloride is essential. For that dip seeds in Mercury chloride@1gm/Ltr solution for 30 min after that dry them in shed. Crop grown in sandy soils are more prone to stem rot. To prevent it do seed treatment with Carbendazim 50%WP@3gm/kg seed.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cabbage,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF CUTWORM   IN  CABBAGE CROP?,Cutworm: As a preventive measure apply Methyl Parathion or Malathion (5% dust)@10kg/acre in soil before sowing.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cabbage,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF LEAF EATING CATERPILLAR  IN  CABBAGE CROP?,Leaf Eating Caterpillar: They feed on leaves. If infestation is observed in field to control of leaf eating caterpillars take spray of Dichlorvos@200ml/150Ltr water or Flubendiamide 48%S.C@0.5ml/3Ltr of water.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cabbage,Plant Protection,"INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF 
DIAMOND BACK MOTH  IN  CABBAGE CROP?","
Diamond back moth: Serious pest of cabbage. They lay eggs under surface leaves. Larva of greenish color with hair on body feed on leaves and make hole. In case of lack of proper control measures, it causes loss upto 80-90%.

At initial stage take spray of Neem Seed Kernel Extract@40gm/Ltr of water at head initiation stage. Repeat this spray with interval of 10-15days. Avoid spraying at curd formation. Take spray of Bt formulations@200gm/acre at 35 and 50 days after planting. In severe infestation take spray of Spinosad 2.5%SC@80ml/150Ltr of water.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cabbage,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF SUCKING PEST  IN  CABBAGE CROP?,"Sucking pest: They suck the sap from the leaves resulting in yellowing and drooping of leaves. Thrips results in curling of leaves, leaves become cup shaped or curved upward.

If incidence of sucking pest like Aphid and Jassid is observed take spray of Imidacloprid 17.8SL@60ml/acre using 150Ltr water. Dry weather causes infestation of sucking pest. Spray Thiamethoxam@ 80gm/150Ltr water for effective control.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cabbage,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF LEAF SPOT BLIGHT  IN  CABBAGE CROP?,"Leaf spot, blight: If infestation of leaf spot or blight is observed, to control take spray of Metalaxyl 8% + Mancozeb 64%WP@ 250gm/150Ltr of water along with sticker or Mancozeb@400gm/150litre or Carbendazim@400gm/150litre of water.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cabbage,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF DOWNY MILDEW IN CABBAGE?,"
Downy Mildew: Appearance of purplish-brown spots observed on lower side of leaves along with greyish white mold on leafs underside. Sanitation and crop rotation help in reducing infection. If infestation of downy is observed, it can be controlled by combined spraying of (Metalaxyl + Mancozeb)@2gm per litre. Spray three times with 10 days interval.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cabbage,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF BLACK ROT IN CABBAGE?,"Black rot: To protect crop from black rot, do seed treatment with Mercury chloride. Dip seeds in Mercury chloride@2gm/Ltr solution for 30min. After that dry them in shed. If infestation is observed in field take spray of Copper oxychloride @300gm + Streptomycin@6gm/150Ltr for better control.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cabbage,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF BLIGHT IN CABBAGE?,SCORE (Difenconazole 25 % EC) 8 ml in 15 liters of water should be sprayed.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Cabbage,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF YELLOWING  IN CABBAGE?,"19:19:19 60 g, Mikrolla 30 ml + M-45 30 g / 15 liters of water should be sprayed to eliminate yellowness in cabbage crop.","[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Cabbage,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF CATERPILLER IN CABBAGE?,Spray imamectin benzoate five to seven grams dissolved in 15 liters of water.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Cabbage,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF SUCKING PEST IN CABBAGE?,Trizophos 30 ml / 15 liters of water should be sprayed.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Cabbage,Fertilizer Uses,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME APPLICATION OF FERTILIZER IN CABBAGE CROP?,"Apply 55 kg urea, 155 kg super phosphate and 40 kg potash for cabbage. Apply 55 kg urea after one month for sowing.","[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Cabbage,Nutrient Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME NECESSARY NUTRITION OF CABBAGE?,"NITROGEN--50kg/acre, PHOSPHORUS --25kg/acre, POTASH--25 kg/acre
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cabbage,Nutrient Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FERTILIZER SPRAY FOR GROWTH OF CABBAGE?,00:52:34 60 g + micronutrient 30 ml + hummic 30 ml / 15 liters of water should be sprayed,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Cabbage,Fertilizer Uses,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FERTILIZER REQUIREMENT IN CABBAGE?,"UREA--110kg/acre, SSP--155kg/acre,MURIATE OF POTASH--40 kg/acre
","[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME BRINJAL CROP?,"Brinjal (Solenum melongena) belongs to family Solanaceae, considered native to India and is a widely grown vegetable in Asian countries. Also popular in other countries like Egypt, France, Italy and United States. Brinjal is a hardy crop than other vegetables. Due to its hardness, it can be successfully grown in dry area with low irrigation facilities. It is moderate source of Vitamins and minerals. It can grow throughout the year. India is second largest producer of Brinjal after China. In India major brinjal growing states are West Bengal, Orissa, Karnataka, Bihar, Maharashtra, Uttar Pradesh, and Andhra Pradesh.

","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOWING TIME OF  BRINJAL CROP?,"For first crop, prepare nursery in October and seedlings are ready for transplantation in November.
Second crop, prepare nursery in November and transplantation in first fortnight of February.
Third crop, sow nursery in February-March and transplantation before end of April.
Fourth crop, sow nursery in July and transplantation in August.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SUITABLE TEMPARARTURE OF BRINJAL CROPS?,"The suitable temparature: Sowing Temparature- 15-20 degree, 
Normal Temperature- 15-32 degree,Harvesting Temperature- 30-35 degree (summer),21-26 degree (winter),Rainfall- 600-1000mm
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOWING TEMPARARTURE OF BRINJAL CROPS?,Sowing Temparature- 15-20 degree,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME NORMAL TEMPARARTURE OF BRINJAL CROPS?,Normal Temperature- 15-32 degree,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME HARVESTING TEMPARARTURE OF BRINJAL CROPS?,"Harvesting Temperature- 30-35 degree (summer),21-26 degree (winter)","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME RAINFALL OF BRINJAL CROPS?,Rainfall- 600-1000mm,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SUITABLE TIME OF  BRINJAL CROP?,"For first crop, prepare nursery in October and seedlings are ready for transplantation in November.
Second crop, prepare nursery in November and transplantation in first fortnight of February.
Third crop, sow nursery in February-March and transplantation before end of April.
Fourth crop, sow nursery in July and transplantation in August.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOIL MANAGEMENT OF  BRINJAL CROP?,"Brinjal is a hardy crop so it can be grown on different type of soils. As it is a long duration crop, it requires well drained fertile sandy loam soil which is best suited for its cultivation and gives good yield. For early crop light soil are good and for high yield clay loam, silt loam are suitable. For good growth pH of soil should be 5.5 to 6.6.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FIELD PREPARATION OF  BRINJAL CROP?,"Before transplanting the soil should be well prepared by deep ploughing 4-5 times and levelled. When the field is well prepared and levelled, the beds of suitable size are made in the field before transplanting.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SPACING OF  BRINJAL CROP?,Spacing:The spacing generally depends on the variety (size and spread and bearing period) soil fertility. Use row to row spacing of 60 cm and plant to plant spacing of 35-40 cm.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOWING DEPTH OF  BRINJAL CROP?,Sowing Depth:In nursery sow seeds at depth of 1 cm and then covered with soil.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME HARVESTING OF  BRINJAL CROP?,"Brinjal is harvested when the fruit attain proper size, color and before ripening stage. The fruit should have glossy appearance, attractive bright color to fetch good prices in the market.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME POST HARVESTING OF  BRINJAL CROP?,"Brinjal fruits cannot be stored at room temperature for long duration because of high transpiration rate and water loss. Brinjal fruit can be stored for 2-3 weeks at 10-11 temperature and 92% relative humidity. After harvesting, Grading is done on the basis of Super, Fancy and Commercial. For packing, use gunny bags or baskets.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME METHOD OF SOWING OF  BRINJAL CROP?,Method of sowing: Transplantation of seedling in main field.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME TRANSPLANTING TIME OF BRINJAL?,"Season of transplanting- February-March, June-July, and January.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME 4 TYPES OF FLOWER OF BRINJAL?,"Brinjal produces 4 types of flowers with different style length. (Long style, short style, medium style and pseudo short style). For seed production and better yield, the long and medium style is desirable.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME HARVESTING TIME OF BRINJAL?,"Season of Harvest- April-June, September.-November, March-May","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Water Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WATER MANAGEMENT OF  BRINJAL CROP?,Irrigate the field after every third or fourth day during the summer season and after 12 to 15 days during the winter season. Timely irrigation is very important for high yields of brinjal. Brinjal fields should be regularly irrigated to keep the soil moist during frosty days. Avoid water stagnation in field as brinjal cannot tolerate water logging.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Weed Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WEED MANAGEMENT OF  BRINJAL CROP?,"Generally two - four weeding and hoeing are necessary for weed control, aeration and for the good growth of plants. Mulching with black polythene film reduces weed growth and maintains soil temperature.

To control weeds efficiently, do pre-plant soil application of Fluchloralin@800-1000 ml/acre or Oxadiazon@400g/acre and pre-plant surface spraying of Alachlor@2 ltr/acre for better results.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Fertilizer Uses,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME BETTER/GOOD/FERTILIZER USE S OF  BRINJAL CROP?,"At time last ploughing apply well decomposed cow dung@10ton/acre in soil. Crop required Nitrogen@25kg, Phosphorus@25kg and Potash@12kg/acre in life cycle of crop. Apply N:P:K fertilizer dose in form of Urea@55kg/acre , SSP@155kg/acre and MOP@20kg/acre. Apply Full dose of Phosphorus, Potash and Nitrogen at time of transplanting. After two picking apply 25 kg of Nitrogen per acre.

WSF: Apply Humic acid@1Ltr/acre or do soil application of 5 kg granules/acre, in initial vegetative growth of crop. It will help in better vegetative growth and good yield. 10-15 days after transplantation take spray of 19:19:19 along with micronutrient@2.5 to 3gm/Ltr of water. In vegetative growth, sometime due to low temperature plant cannot absorb nutrients from soil, plant get weak and give yellow appearance. In such situation give spray of 19:19:19 or 12:61:00@5-7gm/Ltr of water. If required, repeat spray after 10-15 days. 40-45 days after transplantation, take spray of 20%Boron@1gm along with micronutrient@2.5 to 3 gram per litre of water. To fulfil nutrient requirement and to increased yield by 10-15%, give two sprays of 13-00-45@10gm/Ltr of water. Give first spray at 50 days and second 10 days after first spray. When the crop is in flowering or fruiting stage, take spray of 0:52:34 or 13:0:45@5-7gm/Ltr of water. In high temperature flower drop is observed, to control flower drop take spray of NAA@5ml/10Ltr water when crop is in flowering stage. Repeat spray after 20-25 days.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SPRAY FOR FLOWERING IN BRINJAL?,Spray with nitrobenzene 20% in 30 ml /15 liters of water.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME BRINJAL VARIETIES?,"Punjab Bahar: Plant height is about 93 cm. Fruits are of round, dark purple shinning color having less seeds. It gives average yield of 190 qtl/acre.

Punjab No 8: Plants are of medium height. Fruits are of medium size, round shape having light purple color. It gives average yield of 130 qtl/acre.

Jamuni GOI (S 16): Variety developed by Punjab Agriculture University. Fruits are long plumy and shining purple color.

Punjab Barsati: Variety developed by Punjab Agriculture University. These are tolerant to fruit borer. Fruits are of Medium size, long and purple color. It gives average yield of 140 qtl/acre. 

Punjab Neelam: Variety developed by Punjab Agriculture University. Fruits are of long purple color.It gives average yield of 140 qtl/acre.

Punjab Sadabahar: Variety developed by Punjab Agriculture University. Fruits are of long black color.It gives average yield of 130 qtl/acre.

PH 4: Variety developed by Punjab Agriculture University. Fruits are medium size and long. Fruits are of dark purple color. It gives average yield of 270 qtl/acre.

PBH-5: Released in 2017. It gives an average yield of 225qtl/acre. It has long, shining and black-purple color fruit.

PBHR-41: Released in 2016. It gives an average yield of 269qtl/acre. It has round, moderate to large, shining and is greenish purple color fruits. 
 
PBHR-42: Released in 2016. It gives an average yield of 261qtl/acre. It has egg-round shape, moderate, shining, and black-purple color fruits.
 
PBH-4: Released in 2016. It gives an average yield of 270qtl/acre. It has moderately long, shining and black-purple color fruits.
 
Punjab Nagina: Released in 2007. It gives an average yield of 145qtl/acre. It has black-purple color and shining fruits. The variety is ready for harvesting after 55 days of sowing. 
 
BH 2: Released in 1994. It gives an average yield of 235qtl/acre. The average weight of fruit is 300gm. 
 
Punjab Barsati: Released in 1987. It gives an average yield of 140qtl/acre. It has moderately long and shining purple fruit. 
 

Other States Variety:

Pusa Purple Long: Early maturing variety. Ready to harvest in 70-80 days after sowing in winter season and 100-110 days during summer season. Plant having medium height, fruits are of long, purple color. It gives average yield of 130 qtl/acre.

Pusa Purple Cluster: Developed by ICAR, New Delhi. Medium duration variety. Fruits are of deep purple color and borne in clusters. It is moderately resistant to bacteria wilt.

Pusa Hybrid 5: Fruits are long with dark purple color. Ready to harvest in 80-85 days. Gives average yield of 204 qtl/acre. 

Pusa Purple Round: It is tolerant to little leaf and shoot and fruit borer.

Pant Rituraj: Fruits are round with attractive purple color with less seed. Gives average yield of 160 qtl/acre.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
