Vegetables,Brinjal,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME IMPROVED VARIETIES OF BRINJAL?,"Improved varieties of brinjal - PUNJAB Neelam, PUNJAB Barsati, PUNJAB Sadabahar, PUNJAB Nagina, PUNJAB Ronak, PBHR-41, PBHR-42, PBH-2, PBH-3, PBH-4 ,PBH-5.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Seeds,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SEED MANAGEMENT OF  BRINJAL CROP?,"Seed Rate
Use seed rate of 300-400 gm for preparing seedling for one acre land sowing.

Seed Treatment
For sowing use only Trusted and good seeds. Before sowing do seed treatment with Thiram@3gm or Carbendazim@3gm/kg of seeds. After chemical treatment, treat seeds with Trichoderma viride@4gm/kg of seed, dry in shed and sow immediately.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Seeds,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SEED TREATMENT OF  BRINJAL CROP?,"Seed Treatment:
For sowing use only Trusted and good seeds. Before sowing do seed treatment with Thiram@3gm or Carbendazim@3gm/kg of seeds. After chemical treatment, treat seeds with Trichoderma viride@4gm/kg of seed, dry in shed and sow immediately.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Seeds,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME NURSERY MANAGEMENT AND TRANPLANTING OF BRINJAL CROP?,"Seeds of brinjal are sown in nursery beds which are 3 meter long, 1 meter wide and15 cm high. Well rotten farm yard manure is then mixed in nursery bed. Nursery bed is then drenched with Captan solution two days before sowing to avoid the attack of damping off disease in brinjal nursery. Then seeds are sown in rows 5 cm apart and covered the nursery with compost or dry leaves. Light irrigation is done. The nursery beds should be covered with black polythene sheets or paddy straw till the seed germinates. Healthy seedlings having 3-4 leaves or 12-15 cm in height are ready for transplanting. Transplanting is done in evening and light irrigation is done after planting.

Apply water to the nursery beds before transplanting so that seedling can be easily uprooted.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF FRUIT AND SHOOT BORER   IN  BRINJAL CROP?,"Fruit and Shoot Borer: It is one of the major and serious insect pests of brinjal. A short pinkish caterpillar bores into the terminal shoot and eats internal tissue in initial stages, later it bores into the young fruit. The large holes can be seen on the infected fruits. The insect affected fruits become unfit for consumption.

Scout field every week after transplanting for fruit and shoot borer infestation. Remove and destroyed infected fruits. Take spray of Triazophos@20ml/10Ltr water and Neem extract@50gm/Ltr, one month after transplanting. Repeat spray with interval of 10-15 days. When crop is in flowering stage take spray of Chlorantraniliprole 18.5%SC (Coragen)@5ml+Teepol@5ml in 12 Ltr of water, twice with 20 days interval.

In initial stage of infestation, take spray of 5% Neem extract@50gm/Ltr. If infestation is seen in field take sprayed of 25% Cypermethrin@2.4 ml/10Ltr of water on affected crops. For high population spray Spinosad@1ml/Ltr of water. Avoid spraying of Triazophos or any other insecticide after fruit maturation and harvest.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF APHIDS  IN  BRINJAL CROP?,"Aphids: The plants are also attacked by mite, aphids and mealy bug. They suck the sap from the leaves resulting in yellowing and drooping of leaves.

If infestation of Aphid, white fly is observed in field to control take spray of Deltamethrin + Triazophos combination@ 10ml/10Ltr of water. To keep check on white fly spray with Acetamiprid@5gm/15Ltr of water.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Plant Protection,"INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF 
THRIPS  IN  BRINJAL CROP?","Thrips: To check severity of thrips, keep blue sticky traps@6-8 per acre and to reduce the incidence take spray of Verticillium lecani@5gm/Ltr of water. If incidence of thrips is more, to control take spray of Fipronil@2ml/Ltr of water.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF MITE  IN  BRINJAL CROP?,"
Mite: If infestation of Mite is observed in field, to control take spray of Abamectin@1-2ml/Ltr or Fenazaquin@2ml/Ltr of water.

","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF LEAF EATING CATERPILLAR IN  BRINJAL CROP?,"Leaf eating caterpillar: Some time Incidence of caterpillars is seen mostly at initial stage of crop.

To control spray with neem based pesticides. If those are not that effective and infestation become high then only take spray of chemicals pesticides like Emamectin benzoate@4gm or Lambda Cyhalothrin@2ml/1Ltr of water.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME OF ROOT KNOT NEMATODES IN BRINJAL?,"Root Knot Nematodes: It is common in brinjal crop. These are more harmful at initial stage of seedlings. They cause root galls. Due to infestation of root knot nematodes, plant get stunted, give yellow appearance and thus affect yield.
Avoid monocropping and follow crop rotation. Incorporate Carbofuran or Phorate@5-8kg/acre in the soil.

","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME OF DAMPING OFF IN BRINJAL?,"Damping Off: Moist and poorly drain soil causes damping off disease. It is soil borne disease. Water soaking and shrivelling of stem occurs. Seedlings killed before emergence. If it appears in nursery the entire lot of seedling may get destroyed. It is a serious disease of brinjal.

Before sowing do seed treatment with Thiram@3gm per Kg of seeds. Do soil solarisation of nursery soil. If damping off is observed in nursery. Drained out water and drenched soil of nursery with Copper Oxychloride@3gm/Ltr of water.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL MEOF PHOMOPSIS BLIGHT AND FRUIT ROT IN BRINJAL?,"Phomopsis Blight and Fruit Rot: Dark brown color spots appear on leaves. The fruit show watery lesion and becomes black in appearance.

Before sowing do seed treatment with Thiram@3gm per kg of seeds. Use blight disease resistant variety for cultivation. If infestation observed in field take spray of Zineb@2gm/Ltr of water or Mancozeb@2.5gm per litre of water.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF LITTLE LEAF IN BRINJAL?,"Little Leaf: The affected leaves become thinner. The petal turn green leaf like. Infected plant does not bear fruit. The disease is transmitted by leaf hopper.

Use disease resistant variety. In nursery use 10% Foret (20 gm, for 3 X 1 m broad bed). At time of sowing apply Phorate in between two rows of seeds. If infection observed, at initial stage, removed disease affected plants. Spray the crop with Dimethoate or Oxydemiton Methyl@1ml per litre of water. Little leaf is spread mainly through Aphid infestation, to keep check on Aphid Population spray with Thiamethoxam 25%WG@5gm/15Ltr of water.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF MOSAIC IN BRINJAL?,"Mosaic: Light and green patches observed on leaves. Small bubbles or Blisters are form on leaves and leaf size remains small. 

Select healthy and disease free seeds for cultivation. Uproot and destroyed infected plant away from field. Recommendations given for aphids may be adopted. (Take spray of Acephate 75SP@1gm/Ltr or Methyl demeton 25EC@2ml/Ltr of water or Dimethoate@2ml/Ltr of water.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF WILT IN BRINJAL?,"Wilt: Dropping of entire leaves along with yellowing of crops. Wilting or drying of entire plant is seen. If infected stems cut and dipped in water, a white milky stream appears.

Follow crop rotation. Cultivation of brinjal after french bean helps in controlling wilt. Remove and destroyed infected plant parts away from field. Avoid water stagnation in the field, to control wilt drench soil with of Copper Oxychloride@2.5gm/1Ltr of water.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF LEAF CATERPILLAR AND BEETLE MANAGEMENT IN BRINJAL?,Spray 2 ml + neem oil 3 ml + sticky liquid 1 ml of water in a liter of water.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF SHOOT BORER OR CUTWORM IN BRINJAL?,Spray Corazan 5 ml/15 liter of water should be sprayed.( Chloranthraniprole 18.5 % EC).,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF FRIUT BORER IN BRINJAL?,Daceys at 100-4 ml/15 liters of water (Deltamethrin 100% EC) .,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF BLIGHT ATTACK IN BRINJAL?,Microla 30ml + Saf (Carbendazim 12% + Mancozeb 63%) 30g/15L of water should be sprayed.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF VIRUS ATTACK IN BRINJAL?,Actra (Thiomithosome 25%) 5 gm + Anthracol 30 gm/15 liter of water should be sprayed.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF SUCKING PEST ATTACK IN BRINJAL?,Sprayed Confidor 10 ml + Bavistein (Carbendazim 50% WP) 30 g/15 liters of water.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF WHITE FLY ATTACK IN BRINJAL?,Actra 5 gm/15 liter of water should be sprayed.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF  LEAF MINER OF THRIPS IN BRINJAL?,Spray 400 roger (dimethoate 30 EC) in 100 liters of water per acre to prevent thrips and tunnel borer attack in brinjal crop.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME THE CONTROL OF TERMITE IN STANDING CROP OF BRINJAL?,Apply 1 liter of Chlorpyrifos 20 EC mixed with 15-20 kg of sand in a moist.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME BETTER YIELD METHOD  OF BRINJAL?,"For best yield, spray 1 kg NPK in 100 liters of water at 13:00:45 per acre after flowering.","[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME YELLOWING OF BRINJAL?,Mikrolla 30ml +M-45 30g/15 liters of water should be sprayed.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WHAT PREVENTIVE MEASURES SHOULD BE TAKEN TO CONTROL PESTS ON BRINJAL CROP?,Preventive measures on brinjal crop should be sprayed with 30 ml of Nimboli extract in 15 liters of water.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME ATTACK OF SHOOT BORER ON BRINJAL?,Tracer (Spinosad 45 SC) - 3.5 ml / 10 l mixed with water and spray.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME  FLOWER DROP IN BRINJAL CROP?,Spray with calcibor 30 gms / 15 liters of water.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME  PREVENTION FOR NEMATODE MANAGEMENT IN BRINJAL?,Apply 3 - 5 kg of carboperen per acre.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Nutrient Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FERTILIZER SPRAY FOR BRINJAL FOR FLOWERING?,Eggplant should be sprayed with 12:61:00 - 70 grams of Microla - 30 ml in 15 liters of water for flower growth.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Nutrient Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME NECESSARY NUTRITION OF BRINJAL?,"NITROGEN--25kg/acre, PHOSPHORUS --25kg/acre, POTASH--12 kg/acre
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Nutrient Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FOLIAR APPLICATION OF BRINJAL?,5 g of potassium nitrate sprinkle with a liter of water.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Nutrient Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME GROWTH OF BRINJAL?,Spray 2 ml / 1 liter of humic acid.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Nutrient Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME BIO-FERTILIZER APPLICATION OF BRINJAL?,"Mix 1 kg of fertilizer per acre with 1 kg of trichoderma, phosphobacteria, pseudomonas fluoresens, 50 kg of fertilizer and apply it.","[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Nutrient Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME IMPROVING OF FRUITING IN BRINJAL?,Spray 1 KG NPK (13:0:45) mixed with 100 liters of water for one acre to get better fruit from brinjal crop.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Vegetables,Brinjal,Fertilizer Uses,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FERTILIZER REQUIREMENT IN BRINJAL?,"UREA--55kg/acre, SSP--155kg/acre,MURIATE OF POTASH--20 kg/acre
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Coriander,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CORIANDER CROP?,"Coriander is an annual herb plant used as a spice in kitchen. It is mostly grown for its fruit and green leaves to provide flavor in dishes. Dry seeds of coriander contain essential oils which are used in confectionary, to mask offensive odours in pharmaceutical industry and for flavoring liquors. Green leaves are good source of Vitamin C and are used for making chutney, soups and sauces etc. Coriander also has good medicinal value. Tamil Nadu, Karnataka, Madhya Pradesh and Rajasthan are major producers of Coriander in India.

","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Coriander,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOWING TIME OF  CORIANDER CROP?,"For vegetable purpose, optimum time for sowing is first week of October and when grown for seed purpose, complete sowing in last week of October to first week of November.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Coriander,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SUITABLE TEMPARARTURE OF CORIANDER CROPS?,"The suitable temparature: Sowing Temparature- 15-25 degree, 
Normal Temperature- 15-28 degree,Harvesting Temperature- 22-28 degree, Rainfall- 70-100mm
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Coriander,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOWING TEMPARARTURE OF CORIANDER CROPS?,Sowing Temparature- 15-25 degree,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Coriander,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME NORMAL TEMPARARTURE OF CORIANDER CROPS?,Normal Temperature- 15-28 degree,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Coriander,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME HARVESTING TEMPARARTURE OF CORIANDER CROPS?,Harvesting Temperature- 22-28 degree,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Coriander,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME RAINFALL OF CORIANDER CROPS?,Rainfall- 70-100mm,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Coriander,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SUITABLE TIME OF  CORIANDER CROP?,"For vegetable purpose, optimum time for sowing is first week of October and when grown for seed purpose, complete sowing in last week of October to first week of November.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Coriander,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOIL MANAGEMENT OF  CORIANDER CROP?,It can grow in all types of soil but well drained loamy soils are suitable for good growth. pH range of soil should be 8-10.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Coriander,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FIELD PREPARATION OF  CORIANDER CROP?,"Land should be prepared well by giving 2-3 deep ploughing followed by planking to make uniform and leveled beds. Before last ploughing, add 40qtl/acre of well decomposed cow dung in soil.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Coriander,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SPACING OF  CORIANDER CROP?,Spacing:Keep row to row distance of 30 cm and plant to plant spacing of 15 cm.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Coriander,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOWING DEPTH OF  CORIANDER CROP?,Sowing Depth:Depth of soil should not more than 3 cm.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Coriander,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME HARVESTING OF  CORIANDER CROP?,"When crop attained 20-25 cm height harvesting for green leaves can be started. Three to four cutting can be taken. When crop is grown for seed purpose, it is ready for harvesting in April month. Harvest when capsule gets matures but having green color. Over ripe capsule fetch lower price.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Coriander,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME POST HARVESTING OF  CORIANDER CROP?,"After harvesting allowed crop to dry in sunlight for 6-7 days. After proper drying, carry out threshing after then cleaning operation.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Coriander,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME METHOD OF SOWING OF  CORIANDER CROP?,Method of sowing: Use Pora method for sowing.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Coriander,Water Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WATER MANAGEMENT OF  CORIANDER CROP?,Irrigation should be given according to soil moisture present in the soil. First irrigation should be given immediately after sowing of seeds. Subsequent irrigations should be given at 10 to 12days interval.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Coriander,Weed Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WEED MANAGEMENT OF  CORIANDER CROP?,"At initial growth stage of coriander, weed is a serious problem. Take one or two weeding operations to keep field weed free. Take first weeding 4week after sowing and second 5-6week after sowing.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Coriander,Fertilizer Uses,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME BETTER/GOOD/FERTILIZER USE S OF  CORIANDER CROP?,"Apply Nitrogen@40kg in the form of Urea@90kg/acre in three splits. Apply half at the time of sowing and remaining in two equal splits after first and second cutting of leaves. When crop is grown for seed purpose, apply Nitrogen@30kg/acre i.e 65kg/acre in two doses, half at sowing time and remaining at time of flower initiation.

To attain fast growth 15-20 days after germination take spray of Triacontanol hormone@20ml/10Ltr. Also one spray of N:P:K(19:19:19) fertilizer@75gm/15Ltr of water at 20 days of sowing helps in good and faster growth of crop. For obtaining more yield, spray Brassinolide@50ml/acre in150Ltr water, 40-50 days after sowing. Take second spray after 10 days. Also one spray of Mono ammonium Phosphate 12:61:00@45gm/15Ltr of water at leaf and branches growing stage helps in good growth and increases yield.

","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Coriander,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CORIANDER VARIETIES?,"Local: Its average height is about 60 cm. Its flowers are of white color and fruits are of light green to yellowish color. Ready to harvest in 175-180 days. Gives average yield of 3.5qtl/acre.

Punjab Sugandh: Variety having green leaves of medium size with excellent aroma. It gives four cutting of green leaves. It gives average yield of 150qtl/acre for green leaves and 3.5qtl/acre of seed yield.

Other state varieties:

GC 1: Grains are of medium size, round and yellow colored. Ready to harvest in 112 days. It is tolerant to wilt and powdery mildew. Gives average yield of 4.5qtl/acre.

GC 2: Tall and semi-spreading variety with medium size grains. It is tolerant to wilt and powdery mildew. Gives average yield of 5.8qtl/acre

CO 1: Dwarf variety with small size brown grains. Ready to harvest in 100-120 days. Gives average yield of 2qtl/acre. 

CO 2: Medium size yellowish brown grains, Ready to harvest in 90-100 days. Gives average yield of 2.08qtl/acre.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Coriander,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CORIANDER LOCAL VARIETIEY?,Local: Its average height is about 60 cm. Its flowers are of white color and fruits are of light green to yellowish color. Ready to harvest in 175-180 days. Gives average yield of 3.5qtl/acre.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Coriander,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CORIANDER VARIETIEY  PUNJAB SUGANDH?,Punjab Sugandh: Variety having green leaves of medium size with excellent aroma. It gives four cutting of green leaves. It gives average yield of 150qtl/acre for green leaves and 3.5qtl/acre of seed yield.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Coriander,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CORIANDER VARIETIEY GC 1?,"GC 1: Grains are of medium size, round and yellow colored. Ready to harvest in 112 days. It is tolerant to wilt and powdery mildew. Gives average yield of 4.5qtl/acre.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Coriander,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CORIANDER VARIETIEY GC 2?,GC 2: Tall and semi-spreading variety with medium size grains. It is tolerant to wilt and powdery mildew. Gives average yield of 5.8qtl/acre,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Coriander,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CORIANDER VARIETIEY CO 1?,CO 1: Dwarf variety with small size brown grains. Ready to harvest in 100-120 days. Gives average yield of 2qtl/acre.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Coriander,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CORIANDER VARIETIEY CO 2?,"CO 2: Medium size yellowish brown grains, Ready to harvest in 90-100 days. Gives average yield of 2.08qtl/acre.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Coriander,Seeds,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SEED MANAGEMENT OF  CORIANDER CROP?,"Seed Rate
For sowing one acre land, seed rate of 8-10kg is used. 

Seed treatment
For quick germination, before sowing crushed, break seeds into 2 parts. Before sowing, soak seeds in water for 8-12 hr. To prevent crop from wilt , root rot and damping off disease, treat seeds with Trichoderma viride/ Pseudomonas fluorescens @4gm/kg of the seeds before sowing.

","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Coriander,Seeds,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SEED TREATMENT OF  CORIANDER CROP?,"Seed Treatment:
For quick germination, before sowing crushed, break seeds into 2 parts. Before sowing, soak seeds in water for 8-12 hr. To prevent crop from wilt , root rot and damping off disease, treat seeds with Trichoderma viride/ Pseudomonas fluorescens @4gm/kg of the seeds before sowing.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Coriander,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF APHID  IN  CORIANDER CROP?,"Aphid: If Infestation of Aphid is observed, to control take spray of Imidacloprid@6ml/10Ltr water or Thiamethoxam@4gm/10Ltr of water.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Coriander,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF POWDERY MILDEW  IN  CORIANDER CROP?,"Powdery Mildew: Patchy, White powdery growth appears on upper surface of leaves.

If infestation is observed take Spray of water soluble Sulphur@20gm/10Ltr of water. If needed repeat spray with interval of 10days or take spray of Propiconazole10EC (Topas)@200ml/acre in 200Ltr of water.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Coriander,Plant Protection,"INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF 
GRAIN MOULD  IN  CORIANDER CROP?","
Grain Mould: To prevent crop from grain mould, take spray of Carbendazim@200gm/acre 20 days after grain set.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Coriander,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF ROOT ROT  IN  CORIANDER CROP?,"
Root rot: To protect crop from root rot, as preventive measure do soil application of Neem Cake@60gm/acre. Also treat seeds with Trichoderma viride@4gm/kg of seed.

If infestation of root rot, observed in field to control, drenched soil with Carbendazim @5gm/Ltr of water or Copper oxychloride@2gm/litre of water.

","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Coriander,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF LEAF EATING CATERPILLAR IN  CORIANDER CROP?,"Leaf eating caterpillar: Some time Incidence of caterpillars is seen mostly at initial stage of crop.

To control spray with neem based pesticides. If those are not that effective and infestation become high then only take spray of chemicals pesticides like Emamectin benzoate@4gm or Lambda Cyhalothrin@2ml/1Ltr of water.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Coriander,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF YELLOWING IN  CORIANDER CROP?,"For better growth of Coriander and to remove yellowing, you should spray NPK 19:19:19 with manganese sulpahte.","[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Spices,Coriander,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF BLIGHT IN  CORIANDER CROP?,"KOTHIMBIR KARAPA NIYANTRAN -M-45, 30 gm/15 liters of water should be sprayed.","[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Spices,Coriander,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF FUNGUS IN  CORIANDER CROP?,Cothimber Karpa Control - M 45 (Mancozeb 75% WP) 30 gms / 15 liters of water should be taken and sprayed.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Spices,Coriander,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF APHIDS IN  CORIANDER CROP?,Spray with Pride (Acetamapride 20 SP) 07 g / 15 liters of water,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Spices,Coriander,Nutrient Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME NECESSARY NUTRITION OF CORIANDER?,"NITROGEN--40kg/acre, PHOSPHORUS --0kg/acre, POTASH--0kg/acre
","[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Spices,Coriander,Nutrient Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME BETTER GROWTH OF CORIANDER?,Spray 19: 19: 19 by spraying 30 grams of solution in 15 liter of water for the growth of coriander crop.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Spices,Coriander,Fertilizer Uses,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FERTILIZER REQUIREMENT IN CORIANDER?,"UREA--90kg/acre, SSP--depend on soil test,MURIATE OF POTASH--depend on soil test.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Coriander,Fertilizer Uses,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME BIO-FERTILIZER REQUIREMENT IN CORIANDER?,"1 kg of Azospirillum, 1 kg of phosphobacteria and 20 kg of fertilizer per acre.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Coriander,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME VARIETIES IN CORIANDER?,"1.Sadhana (CS-4)
2.Sindhu (CS-2)
3.Sudha (LCC-128)
4.Swathi (CS-6)
5.APHU Dhania-1 (LCC-170)
6.Suguna (LCC-236)
7.Suruchi (LCC-234)
8.Susthira (LCC-219)","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Ginger,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME GINGER CROP?,"Ginger, known as ""Adrakh"" is most important major spice crop of India. India is leading producer of Ginger. Karnataka, Orissa, Assam, Meghalaya, Arunachal Pradesh and Gujarat are major ginger producing states.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Ginger,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOWING TIME OF  GINGER CROP?,Sowing is done by first week of May- June.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Ginger,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SUITABLE TEMPARARTURE OF GINGER CROPS?,"The suitable temparature: Sowing Temparature- 30-35 degree, 
Normal Temperature- 12-35 degree,Harvesting Temperature- 25-33 degree, Rainfall- 1500mm
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Ginger,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOWING TEMPARARTURE OF GINGER CROPS?,Sowing Temparature- 30-35 degree,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Ginger,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME NORMAL TEMPARARTURE OF GINGER CROPS?,Normal Temperature- 12-35 degree,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Ginger,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME HARVESTING TEMPARARTURE OF GINGER CROPS?,Harvesting Temperature- 25-33 degree,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Ginger,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME RAINFALL OF GINGER CROPS?,Rainfall- 1500mm,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Ginger,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SUITABLE TIME OF  GINGER CROP?,Sowing is done by first week of May- June.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Ginger,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOIL MANAGEMENT OF  GINGER CROP?,"It gives best results, when grown on well drained loamy soils also in sandy or clay loam or red loamy soils. Avoid water stagnation in field as it cannot survive in water logged conditions. Ideal pH range of 6-6.5 is required for good growth of crop. Avoid soil on which previously ginger was taken. Do not cultivate ginger crop on same site year after year.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Ginger,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FIELD PREPARATION OF  GINGER CROP?,"
Prepare field by ploughing land two - three times. After ploughing do planking operation. For turmeric planting, beds of 15 cm height, 1 m width and of convenient length are prepared. Keep distance of 50 cm between beds.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Ginger,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SPACING OF  GINGER CROP?,Spacing:keep plant distance of 15-20 cm between the row and 30 cm between two plant.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Ginger,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOWING DEPTH OF  GINGER CROP?,"Sowing Depth:Depth should be near about 3-4 cm.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Ginger,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME HARVESTING OF  GINGER CROP?,"In 8months crop is ready for harvesting. For fresh spice purpose, ginger is harvested from 6th month and if it is to be used for processing, then it is harvested after 8 months. Right time for harvesting of ginger is when leaves gets yellow and dry out completely. Remove rhizomes by dugging and after harvesting clean rhizomes by thoroughly washing in water for 2 to 3 times. Then dry them in shades for 2-3days.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Ginger,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME POST HARVESTING OF  GINGER CROP?,"For dry ginger purpose, only the outer skin is to be peeled and then dried in the sun for a week. Outer skin is removed with help of special knife or split bamboos with pointed end. Yield of dry ginger is about 16-25% of green ginger.

Storage: Fresh, disease free rhizomes are selected then treated with solution of Carbendazim + Mancozeb@40 gm/10 ltr of water for 30 min. It will prevent rotting of rhizome in storage. Then dry the rhizomes in shade. Store dried rhizome in pit of convenient size, covered with plank having 2-3 holes for aeration. Before storing rhizomes in pit, spread 1 inch thickness sand layers.

","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Ginger,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME METHOD OF SOWING OF  GINGER CROP?,"Method of sowing:Direct sowing also transplanting method is used for planting.

","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Ginger,Water Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WATER MANAGEMENT OF  GINGER CROP?,"It is grown as rainfed crop so provide irrigation depending upon rainfall intensity and rainfall frequency.After planting, crop is mulched with green leaves@50 qtl/acre. Repeat mulching@20 qtl/acre after every fertilizer application.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Ginger,Weed Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WEED MANAGEMENT OF  GINGER CROP?,"Third day after plantation take spray of Atrazine@4-5 gm/ltr on moist soil. To kill weeds that grow after first spray of weedkiller, 12-15 days after plantation take spray of Glyphosate@4-5 ml/Ltr water. After weedicide application, cover field with green manure or paddy straw.Earthing up operation is carried to enhanced root development. 50-60 days after planting take first earthing operation and next after 40 days.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Ginger,Fertilizer Uses,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME BETTER/GOOD/FERTILIZER USE S OF  GINGER CROP?,"At time of field preparation, apply well decomposed cow dung@150 qtl/acre in soil. Apply N:P:K@25:10:10 kg/acre in form of Urea@55 kg/acre, SSP@60 kg/acre and MOP@16 kg/acre. Full dose of Potash and Phosphorus are applied at time of rhizome planting. Nitrogen dose is given in two equal splits. First half dose of N is given 75 days after planting and remaining half dose is given three month after planting.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Ginger,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME GINGER VARIETIES?,"1.IISR Varada: It gives high yield of fresh as well as dry ginger yield. Ready to harvest in 200 days. It gives an average yield of 90 qtl/acre. 
2.IISR Mahima
3.Karthika
4.Suprabha
5.Suruchi

Other States Variety
1.Green Ginger variety: Rio-De-Janerio, china, Varadha.
2.Dry Ginger varieties: Maran, Nadia.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Ginger,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME GREEN GINGER VARIETIEY?,"Green Ginger variety: Rio-De-Janerio, china, Varadha.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Ginger,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME DRY GINGER VARIETIES?,"Dry Ginger varieties: Maran, Nadia.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Ginger,Seeds,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SEED MANAGEMENT OF  GINGER CROP?,"Seed Rate:
For sowing, select fresh and diseased free rhizomes (mother rhizomes as well as fingers) are used. Seed rate of 480-720 kg is sufficient for sowing one acre land.

Seed treatment:
Before sowing, carry out rhizome treatment with Mancozeb@3 gm/Ltr of water. Dip rhizomes for 30min in solution. It will protect rhizomes from fungal infestation. After treatment, dry rhizomes in shade for 3-4 hours.

","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Ginger,Seeds,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CROP TREATMENT OF  GINGER CROP?,"Seed Treatment:
Before sowing, carry out rhizome treatment with Mancozeb@3 gm/Ltr of water. Dip rhizomes for 30min in solution. It will protect rhizomes from fungal infestation. After treatment, dry rhizomes in shade for 3-4 hours.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Ginger,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF ROOT OR RHIZOME ROT  IN  GINGER CROP?,"Root or Rhizome Rot: To prevent crop from root rot, drench crop with Mancozeb@3 gm/Ltr or Metalaxyl@1.25 gm/Ltr at 30,60 and 90 days after planting.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Ginger,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF BACTERIAL WILT IN  GINGER CROP?,"Bacterial wilt: To prevent crop from bacterial wilt, drench plants with Copper oxychloride@3 gm/ltr of water immediately after disease is seen in field.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Ginger,Plant Protection,"INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF 
ANTHRACNOSE  IN  GINGER CROP?","

Anthracnose: If infestation is observed, to control take spray of Hexaconazole@10 ml or Mancozeb 75WP@25 gm/10 ltr of water+ 10 ml sticker.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Ginger,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF LEAF BLOTCH IN  GINGER CROP?,"Leaf Blotch: If infestation is observed to control take spray of Mancozeb@20 gm or Copper oxycloride@25 gm/10 ltr of water.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Ginger,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF BLIGHT AND LEAF SPOTS IN GINGER?,"
Blight and leaf spots: If infestation of blight and leaf spot is observed, take spray of Mancozeb@30 gm or Carbendazim@10 gm in 10 ltr water by interval of 15-20 alternatively. Or spray with Propiconazole@1 ml/Ltr of water.

","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Ginger,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF RHIZOME FLY IN GINGER?,"Rhizome fly: If Infestation of rhizome fly is observed in field, To control take spray of Acephate 75SP@15 gm in 10 ltr of water. Repeat the spray with 15 days interval.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Ginger,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF SHOOT BORER IN GINGER?,Shoot borer: If infestation of shoot borer is observed to control take spray of Dimethoate@2 ml/Ltr or Quinalphos@2.5 ml/ltr of water.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Ginger,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF SUCKING PEST IN GINGER?,Sucking pest: To control sucking pests take spray of neem based pesticide like Azadirachtin 0.3EC@ 2 ml/Ltr of water.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Ginger,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF FUNGAL ATTACK IN GINGER?,"For fungal control of ginger crop, fungicide containing Metalaxyl M4 and Mancozeb 64% should be sprayed at the rate of two grams per liter of water.","[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Spices,Ginger,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF CATERPILLER IN GINGER?,Chlorpyrifos 30 ml/15 liters of water should be sprayed.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Spices,Ginger,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF ROOT ROT IN GINGER?,Blue copper 30 g/15 l of water should be applied.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Spices,Ginger,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF ROOT BORER IN GINGER?,Chlorpyrifos 400 ml/200 liters of water should be sprayed for 1 acre.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Spices,Ginger,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF APHIDS IN GINGER?,Spray Karate 20 ml /15 liters of water.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Spices,Ginger,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF WHITE GRUB IN GINGER?,Chlorpyrifos 40 ml / 15 liters of water should be applied.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Spices,Ginger,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF RHIZOME ROT IN GINGER?,Chlorpyrifos 20 EC 30 ml /15 liters of water should be applied.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Spices,Ginger,Fertilizer Uses,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FERTILIZER SPRAY IN GINGER?,For ginger crop 13:40:13 g + Microla 30 ml + Ridomil Gold 40 g / 15 l water should be taken and sprayed.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Spices,Ginger,Nutrient Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME NECESSARY NUTRITION OF GINGER?,"NITROGEN--25kg/acre, PHOSPHORUS --10kg/acre, POTASH--10kg/acre
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Ginger,Fertilizer Uses,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FERTILIZER REQUIREMENT IN GINGER?,"UREA--55kg/acre, SSP--60kg/acre,MURIATE OF POTASH--16kg/acre.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Turmeric,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME TURMERIC?,"Turmeric is a perennial herb, native of south Asia. It is also known as ""Indian Saffron"" is sacred spice of India. It is principal ingredient in Indian culinary and used as flavouring and coloring agent. It is used in drug and cosmetic industry because of its anti-cancer and anti-viral property. Turmeric has special place in religious and ceremonial occasions. Rhizomes are used for propagation. Its leaves are long, broad and of bright green color and flowers are of pale yellow color. India is world largest producer, consumer and exporter of turmeric. In India, Andhra Pradesh, Orissa, West Bengal, Karnataka and Kerala are major producers of Turmeric.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Turmeric,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOWING TIME OF  TURMERIC CROP?,"To get higher yield, complete rhizome sowing in field by April end. It is also raised by transplanting method, for that rhizome transplantation should be completed within first fortnight of June. For transplanting 35-45 days old seedling is used.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Turmeric,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SUITABLE TEMPARARTURE OF TURMERIC CROPS?,"The suitable temparature: Sowing Temparature- 24-34 degree, 
Normal Temperature- 24-28 degree,Harvesting Temperature- 20-22 degree, Rainfall- 70-230cm
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Turmeric,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOWING TEMPARARTURE OF TURMERIC CROPS?,Sowing Temparature- 24-34 degree,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Turmeric,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME NORMAL TEMPARARTURE OF TURMERIC CROPS?,Normal Temperature- 24-28 degree,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Turmeric,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME HARVESTING TEMPARARTURE OF TURMERIC CROPS?,Harvesting Temperature- 20-22 degree,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Turmeric,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME RAINFALL OF TURMERIC CROPS?,Rainfall- 70-230cm,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Turmeric,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SUITABLE TIME OF  TURMERIC CROP?,"To get higher yield, complete rhizome sowing in field by April end. It is also raised by transplanting method, for that rhizome transplantation should be completed within first fortnight of June. For transplanting 35-45 days old seedling is used.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Turmeric,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOIL MANAGEMENT OF  TURMERIC CROP?,"It gives best results, when grown on well drained loamy soils also in sandy or clay loam or red loamy soils. Avoid water stagnation in field as it cannot survive in water logged conditions.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Turmeric,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FIELD PREPARATION OF  TURMERIC CROP?,"Prepared field by ploughing land, two - three times. After ploughing do planking operation. For turmeric planting, beds of 15cm height, 1m width and of convenient length are prepared. Keep distance of 50cm between beds.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Turmeric,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SPACING OF  TURMERIC CROP?,"Spacing:Sow rhizomes in line and keep distance of 30 cm between the row and 20 cm between two plant. After rhizome planting, straw mulch@ 2.5 ton/acre is applied in field.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Turmeric,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOWING DEPTH OF  TURMERIC CROP?,"Sowing Depth:Depth of soil should not exceed 3 cm.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Turmeric,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME HARVESTING OF  TURMERIC CROP?,"Depending upon variety, it takes 6-9months for harvesting. Right time for harvesting of turmeric is when leaves of turmeric gets yellow and dry out completely, Remove rhizomes by dugging and after harvesting clean rhizomes. Then dry them in shades for 2-3days. It will make peel hard and easy for boiling.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Turmeric,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME POST HARVESTING OF  TURMERIC CROP?,"After cleaning, rhizomes are boiled in water containing sodium bicarbonate (100gm sodium bicarbonate in 100Ltr water) for 1hour. For boiling of rhizomes, utensils, kadhai and boilers are used. To get better quality product, stop the boiling when froth comes out and white fumes appear giving out a typical odour (Price deciding factor). After boiling rhizomes are dried properly for 10-15days. After proper drying, polishing of rhizomes is done manually using wire mesh, gunny bags or mechanically by power operated drum. Then grading of polished rhizomes is done on basis of size, shape and color.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Turmeric,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME METHOD OF SOWING OF  TURMERIC CROP?,"Method of sowing:Direct sowing and transplanting method is used for planting.

","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Turmeric,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME EXCESSIVE GROWTH OF BRANCHES IN TURMERIC?,"If the plants are overpopulated, remove some plants and increase the spacing.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Turmeric,Water Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WATER MANAGEMENT OF  TURMERIC CROP?,"It is grown as rainfed crop so provide irrigation depending upon rainfall intensity and rainfall frequency. For light textured soil, in whole life cycle, 35-40 irrigations are required.

After planting, crop is mulched with green leaves@40-60 qtl/acre. Repeat mulching@30 qtl/acre after every fertilizer application.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Turmeric,Weed Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WEED MANAGEMENT OF  TURMERIC CROP?,"Apply Pendimethalin 30EC@800ml per acre or Metribuzin 70WP@400gm/acre in 200Ltr of water within two - three days after planting rhizomes. After weedicide application, cover field with green manure or paddy straw.

Earthing up operation is carried to enhanced root development. After 50-60 days of planting, carry out first earthing operation and next should be done after 40 days.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Turmeric,Fertilizer Uses,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME BETTER/GOOD/FERTILIZER USE S OF  TURMERIC CROP?,"At the time of field preparation, apply well decomposed cow dung@150 qtl/acre in soil. Apply N:P:K@10:10:10 kg/acre in form of Urea@25 kg/acre, SSP@60 kg/acre and MOP@16 kg/acre. Full dose of Potash and Phosphorus are applied at time of rhizome planting. Nitrogen dose is given in two equal splits. First half dose of N is given 75 days after planting and remaining half dose is given three month after planting.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Turmeric,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME TURMERIC VARIETIES?,"Punjab Haldi 1: Medium heighted plant with green leaves and long, medium thick rhizomes. Flesh is of dark yellow color and skin is of brown color. Ready to harvest in 215 days and its average yield is 108 qtl/acre. 

Punjab Haldi 2: Tall variety with light green, broad leaves and long, thick rhizomes. Flesh is of yellow color and skin is of brown color. Ready to harvest in 240 days and its average yield is 122 qtl/acre. 

Other States Variety

Popular Variety: Amalapuram, Armour, Dindigam, Erode, Krishna, Kodur, Vontimitra, P317, GL Purm I and II, RH2 and RH10

Rajapuri, Salem, Sangli turmeric, Nizamabad bulb.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Turmeric,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME TURMERIC VARIETIEY PUNJAB HALDI 1?,"Punjab Haldi 1: Medium heighted plant with green leaves and long, medium thick rhizomes. Flesh is of dark yellow color and skin is of brown color. Ready to harvest in 215 days and its average yield is 108 qtl/acre.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Turmeric,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME POPULER TURMERIC VARIETIES?,"Popular Variety: Amalapuram, Armour, Dindigam, Erode, Krishna, Kodur, Vontimitra, P317, GL Purm I and II, RH2 and RH10,Rajapuri, Salem, Sangli turmeric, Nizamabad bulb.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Turmeric,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME TURMERIC VARIETIEY PUNJAB HALDI 2?,"Punjab Haldi 2: Tall variety with light green, broad leaves and long, thick rhizomes. Flesh is of yellow color and skin is of brown color. Ready to harvest in 240 days and its average yield is 122 qtl/acre.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Turmeric,Seeds,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SEED MANAGEMENT OF  TURMERIC CROP?,"Seed Rate:
For sowing, select fresh and diseased free rhizomes (mother rhizomes as well as fingers) are used. Seed rate of 6-8 qtl is sufficient for sowing one acre land.

Seed treatment:
Before sowing, carry out rhizome treatment with Quinalphos 25EC@20ml + Carbendazim@10gm/10Ltr of water and prepare solution. Then dip rhizomes for 20min in solution. It protects rhizomes from fungal infestation.

","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Turmeric,Seeds,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CROP TREATMENT OF  TURMERIC CROP?,"Seed Treatment:
Before sowing, carry out rhizome treatment with Quinalphos 25EC@20ml + Carbendazim@10gm/10Ltr of water and prepare solution. Then dip rhizomes for 20min in solution. It protects rhizomes from fungal infestation.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Turmeric,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF BLIGHT AND LEAF SPOTS  IN  TURMERIC CROP?,"Blight and leaf spots: If infestation of blight and leaf spot is observed, take spray of Mancozeb@30 gm or Carbendazim@30gm in 10 ltr water by interval of 15-20 alternatively. Or spray with Propiconazole@2ml/ltr of water.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Turmeric,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF ROOT OR RHIZOME ROT IN  TURMERIC CROP?,"Root or Rhizome Rot: To prevent crop from root rot, drench crop with Mancozeb@3gm/Ltr at 30, 60 and 90 days after planting.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Turmeric,Plant Protection,"INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF 
BACTERIAL WILT  IN  TURMERIC CROP?","
Bacterial wilt: To prevent crop from bacterial wilt, drench plants with Copper oxychloride@3gm/Ltr of water immediately after disease is seen in field.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Turmeric,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF LEAF BLOTCH IN  TURMERIC CROP?,"Leaf Blotch: If infestation is observed to control take spray of Mancozeb@20gm or Copper oxycloride@25gm/10Ltr of water.
 
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Turmeric,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF RHIZOME FLY IN TURMERIC?,"
Rhizome fly: If Infestation of rhizome fly is observed in field, to control take spray of Acephate 75SP@600gm in 100Ltr of water. Repeat the spray with 15days interval.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Turmeric,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF SUCKING PEST IN TURMERIC?,"Sucking pest: To control sucking pests take spray of neem based pesticide like Azadirachtin 0.3EC@ 2 ml/Ltr of water.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Turmeric,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF SHOOT BORER IN TURMERIC?,"
Shoot borer: If infestation of shoot borer is observed, take spray of Dimethoate@250ml/150Ltr or Quinalphos@250ml/150Ltr of water to control shoot borer.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com,  Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Turmeric,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF BACTERIAL WILT IN TURMERIC?,Spray copper oxychloride at the rate of 3g per liter to prevent bacterial wilt in turmeric.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Spices,Turmeric,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF CATERPILLER  IN TURMERIC?,Chlorpyrifos 2 ml / 1 liter of water should be sprayed.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Spices,Turmeric,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF APHIDS IN TURMERIC?,Alika 8 ml + Bavistein 30 g / 15 liters of water should be sprayed.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Spices,Turmeric,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF STEM BORER IN TURMERIC?,You should be sprayed with Nuvan 20 ml/15 liters of water (Dichlorvos 76% EC) on turmeric.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Spices,Turmeric,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF FUNGAL ATTACK IN TURMERIC?,Ridomil Gold should be taken in 30 grams / 15 liters of water and sprayed.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Spices,Turmeric,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF WHITE GRUB IN TURMERIC?,Chlorpyrifos 20% EC + Cypermethrin 5 % - 40 ml / 15 liters of water should be applied.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Spices,Turmeric,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF FUNAL ATTACK IN TURMERIC?,Spraying Ridomil Gold 30g + Micro with 30 ml / 15 liters of water.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Spices,Turmeric,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF ROOT ROT IN TURMERIC?,Apply Ridomil Gold 600 gm per acre for root rot control on turmeric crop.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Spices,Turmeric,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF SOIL BORNE PEST ATTACK IN TURMERIC?,Hamala 550 40 ml / 15 liters of water should be diluted (Chlorpyrifos 20%EC + Cypermethrin 4%) and sprayed.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Spices,Turmeric,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF RHIZOME ROT ATTACK IN TURMERIC?,"Applied Chlorpyrifos 500 ml + M-45, 500 gms by Alvani / EKAR / 200 LITAR water.","[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Spices,Turmeric,Fertilizer Uses,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FERTILIZER SPRAY IN TURMERIC?,Blue copper should be taken in 30 grams / 15 liters of water and sprayed,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Spices,Turmeric,Nutrient Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME GROWTH OF TURMERIC?,For Turmeric Growth - 00:52:34 (Mono Potassium Phosphate) 3000 gm + Microla 1000 ml + Saf (Carbendazim 12% + Mancozeb 63%) 400 gm /200 liter water should be sprayed for 1 acre.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
