Fruits,Papaya,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME PAPAYA  VARIETIEY   CO.2?,CO.2: Large size fruits and plant has medium height.,[Reference: www.apnikheti.com]
Fruits,Papaya,Seeds,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SEED MANAGEMENT OF  PAPAYA CROP?,"Seed rate:
Use 150-200gm seeds for per acre land.

Seed treatment:
Before seed sowing, treat the seeds with Captan@3gm to protect the plant from soil borne diseases.",[Reference: www.apnikheti.com]
Fruits,Papaya,Seeds,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SEED TREATMENT OF  PAPAYA CROP?,"Seed treatment:
Before seed sowing, treat the seeds with Captan@3gm to protect the plant from soil borne diseases.",[Reference: www.apnikheti.com]
Fruits,Papaya,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME  NURSERY MANAGEMENT AND TRANSPLANTING OF  PAPAYA CROP?,"The seedlings are prepared in the polythene bags having dimensions of 25 X 10cm. In these polythene, 8-10 holes are done having 1mm diameter on lower part for proper drainage of water. Polythene bags are filled with equal proportions of FYM, soil and sand. Mainly seeds are sown in polythene bags in 2nd week of July to 3rd week for September. Before sowing treat the seeds with Captan@3gm per kg seeds. Drenching is done with Captan@0.2% when seedlings emerge out to protect them from damping off disease. Transplanting of seedlings is done in September-October month.",[Reference: www.apnikheti.com]
Fruits,Papaya,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF STEM ROT  IN  PAPAYA CROP?,"Stem rot: Water like wet spots are seen on plant stem. The symptoms get spread on all sides of the plant. Plant leaves fall apart before it is fully developed.
Treatment: To control this disease spray with M-45@300gm in 150ltr water.",[Reference: www.apnikheti.com]
Fruits,Papaya,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF POWDERY MILDEW  IN  PAPAYA CROP?,"Powdery mildew: Patchy, white powdery growth appears on upper surface of leaves also on main stem of infected plant. It parasitizes the plant using it as a food source. In severe infestation it causes defoliation and premature fruit ripening.

Treatment: Spraying of Thiophanate methyl 70% WP@300gm in 150-160ltr water/acre is done.",[Reference: www.apnikheti.com]
Fruits,Papaya,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF ROOT ROT OR WILT  IN  PAPAYA CROP?,"Root rot or wilt: The disease causes rotting of roots which ultimately result in plant wilting.
Treatment: To control this disease drenching with Saaf@400gm in 150ltr water.",[Reference: www.apnikheti.com]
Fruits,Papaya,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF PAPAYA MOSAIC  IN  PAPAYA CROP?,"Papaya mosaic: The symptoms appear on top young leaves of the plants.
Treatment: To control this pest spraying with Malathion@300ml in 150ltr water is done.",[Reference: www.apnikheti.com]
Fruits,Papaya,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF APHID  IN  PAPAYA CROP?,"Aphid: They suck the sap of the plant. Aphids help in spreading disease in plants.
Treatment: To control this pest spraying with Malathion@300ml in 150ltr water is done.",[Reference: www.apnikheti.com]
Fruits,Papaya,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF FRUIT FLY  IN  PAPAYA CROP?,"Fruit fly: The female lays eggs in the mesocarp, after hatching the maggots feed themselves on fruit pulp which will destroy the fruit.
Treatment: To control this pest spraying with Malathion@300ml in 150ltr water is done.",[Reference: www.apnikheti.com]
Spices,Sugarcane,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SUGARCANE?,"Sugarcane, Saccharum officinarum L. is a perennial gras. It belongs to bamboo family and it is indigenous to India. It is the main source of sugar, jaggery and khandsari. About two-thirds of the total sugarcane produced in India is consumed for making jaggery and khandsari and only one third of it goes to sugar factories. It also provides raw material for manufacturing alcohol. Brazil is largest producer of sugarcane followed by India, China, Thailand, Pakistan and Mexico. In India, Maharashtra is largest producer of sugar and it contributes about 34% of sugar in country followed by Uttar Pradesh.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Sugarcane,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOWING TIME OF  SUGARCANE CROP?,"In Punjab, planting season of sugarcane is from September to October and February to March. Sugarcane takes generally one year to mature therefore called as Eksali.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Spices,Sugarcane,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SUITABLE TEMPARARTURE OF SUGARCANE CROPS?,"The suitable temparature: Sowing Temparature- 20-25 degree, 
Normal Temperature- 20-30 degree,Harvesting Temperature- 20-30 degree, Rainfall- 75-150cm
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
