Oilseeds,Mustard,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME PRIVATE COMPANY VARIETIES OF MUSTARD?,"Pioneer 45S42: High yielding variety having medium maturity. Ready to harvest 125-130 days. Suitable under all soil conditions. Its grains are bold and high pod density. It give average yield is 12.5 qtl per acre.

Pioneer 45S35 : High yielding and early maturing variety. It give average yield is 12.5 qtl per acre.

Pioneer 45S46 : High yielding and medium duration variety. Its grains are bold with good oil percentage. It give average yield is 12.5 qtl per acre.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Oilseeds,Mustard,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME INDIAN MUSTARD VARIETIES?,"RH 0749: Suitable for growing in Haryana, Punjab, Delhi, Jammu and North Rajasthan. It is high yielding variety having more number of seeds per silique. Ready to harvest in 146-148 days. Seeds are bold and having oil percentage of 40%. It give average yield of 10.5-11 qtl/acre.

RH 0406: Suitable for growing in rainfed areas. Ready to harvest in 142-145 days. It give average yield of 8.8 - 9.2 qtl/acre.

T 59 (Varuna): It is suitable under all climatic conditions. Ready to harvest in 145-150 days. Gives oil content about 39%. It gives average yield of 6-8 qtl/acre.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Oilseeds,Mustard,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME GOBHI SARSON VARIETIES OF MUSTARD?,"GSL 1: Ready to harvest in 160 days. Crop is short and not lodge easily. It gives average yield of 6.7 qtl/acre. Seeds contains 44.5% oil content.

PGSH51: Ready to harvest in 162 days. Tall and high yielding hybrid gives average yield of 7.9 qtl/acre. Seeds content 44.5% oil content.

Gobhi sarson (canola type): Oil of canola variety is good for health of human.

Hyola PAC 401: It is medium heighted crop and ready to mature in 150 days. Seeds are brownish black and contain about 42% oil. It gives average yield of 6.74 qtl/acre.

GSC 6: Recommended for timely sown crop under irrigated conditiom. Seeds are bold and content 39.1% oil content. And gives average yield of 6.07 qtl/acre.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Oilseeds,Mustard,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME RAYA VARIETIES OF MUSTARD?,"RLM 619: It is recommended for cultivation in irrigated and rainfed area. It is ready to harvest in 143 days. Its seed are bold and contain 43% oil. It is resistive to white rust, blight and downy mildew. Gives average yield of 8 qtl/acre.

PBR 91: It get ready to harvest in 145 days. It show resistant to blight, rust and insect pest. It gives average yield of 8.1 quintal/acre.

PBR 97: Suitable for cultivation under rainfed condition. Ready to harvest in 136 days. Grains are medium bold and contain 39.8% oil content. Gives average yield of 5.2 qtl/acre.

PBR 210: Suitable for timely sown and irrigated condition. Ready to harvest in 150 days. It gives average yield of 6 qtl/acre.

RLC 3: Tall variety, ready to harvest in 145 days. Its average yield is about 7.3 qtl/acre. Its oil content 41.5%.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Oilseeds,Mustard,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME TORIA VARIETIES OF MUSTARD?,"PBT 37: Early maturity variety, matures in 91 days. It is suitable for toria-wheat cultivation. Seeds are dark brown and bold in size. It gives average yield of 5.4 qtl/acre and seeds contains 41.7% oil.

TL 15: It is early maturity variety. It required 88 days to mature. It gives average yield of 4.5 qtl/acre.

TL 17: Ready to harvest in 90 days. Suitable for multiple cropping. It gives average yield of 5.2 qtl/acre.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Oilseeds,Mustard,Seeds,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SEED MANAGEMENT OF  MUSTARD CROP?,"Seed Rate:
When rapeseed - mustards are grown individually then it required seed rate of 1.5 kg seeds per acre. Do thinning operations three week after sowing and maintain only healthy seedlings.

Seed Treatment:
To protect seed from soil borne pest and disease, before sowing do seed treatment with Thiram@3gm per kg of seeds.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Oilseeds,Mustard,Seeds,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SEED TREATMENT OF  MUSTARD CROP?,"Seed treatment:
To protect seed from soil borne pest and disease, before sowing do seed treatment with Thiram@3gm per kg of seeds.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Oilseeds,Mustard,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FUNGICIDE NAME  OF  MUSTARD CROP?,"Fungicide name Quantity (Dosage per kg seed)
Carbendazim 2gm
Captan 2-3gm
Thiram 5gm
Mancozeb 4gm
Chlorpyriphos 20EC 12.5ml
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Oilseeds,Mustard,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME ROTATION OF  MUSTARD CROP?,"Mustardate Kharif Fodder/Gobhi sarson+Toria /Potato/Peas/Toria/Rabi crops rotation can be taken up successfully where irrigation facilities exist. Avoid sowing Mustard in the same field year after year, as this practice results in heavy build- up of soil-borne diseases.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Oilseeds,Mustard,Fertilizer Uses,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WATER SOLUABLE FERTILIZER OF  MUSTARD CROP?,"To improve pod filling spraying of nutrient solution is important. This can be prepared by soaking DAP@2.5 kg, Ammonium sulphate@1kg and Borax@500 gm in 37 lit of water overnight. The next day morning it can be filtered and about 16 litre of mixture can be obtained and it may be diluted with 234 lit of water so as to made up to 200 litre to spray for one acre. Planofix@4ml/15 ltr can also be mixed while spraying. This can be sprayed on 25th and 35th day after sowing.

","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Oilseeds,Mustard,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF APHID  IN  MUSTARD CROP?,"Aphid: They suck the sap and plant get weak, pale and plant remain stunted and in later stage do not bear pods.

To control, do timely sowing of crop. Avoid excessive use of nitrogen fertilizer. In infestation is observed in field, take spray of any one pesticide like Thiamethoxam@80gm or Quinalphos or Oxydemeton@250ml or Chlorpyriphos @200ml in 100-125Ltr water per acre.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Oilseeds,Mustard,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF PAINTED BUG IN  MUSTARD CROP?,"
Painted bug: It destroyed crop at germination stage also at maturity stage. They suck sap and leads to drying of crop.
Application of irrigation three to four week after sowing help in reducing pest population. If infestation is observed in field, take spray of Malathion @ 400ml/acre.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Oilseeds,Mustard,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF HAIRY CATERPILLAR  IN  MUSTARD CROP?,"Hairy caterpillar: Young larva feed on leaves and destroyed them completely.
If infestation is observed in field, take spray of Malathion 5% dust@15kg/acre or Dichlorvos@200ml/acre in 100-125ltr of water.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Oilseeds,Mustard,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF BLIGHT  IN  MUSTARD CROP?,"Blight: Dark brown spot with dot like bodies developed on stem, branches, leaflet and pods. In severe infestation, withering of stem and pod is observed.
For cultivation use resistant varieties. On incidence of disease spray with Indofil M-45 or Captan @ 260gm/100Ltr of water per acre. If necessary repeat the spray at interval of 15days.


","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Oilseeds,Mustard,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF DOWNY MILDEW  IN  MUSTARD CROP?,"
Downy Mildew: Whitish growth is observed on lower surface of leaves. The leaves give green or yellow coloration appearance.
Destroyed debris of previous crop before sowing of crop. Spray crop with Indofil M-45 @ 400gm in 150 Ltr of water per acre for four times with interval of 15 days.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Oilseeds,Mustard,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF WHITE RUST  IN  MUSTARD CROP?,"White Rust: White pustules are observed on leaves, stem and on flower. Swelling of affected part is observed. Because of infection flower become sterile.
If infestation observed in field, to control spray with Metalaxyl 8%+Mancozeb 64% @ 2gm/Ltr of water or spray with Copper oxychloride @ 25gm/Ltr of water. If necessary repeat the spray with interval of 10-15days.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Oilseeds,Mustard,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF APHID IN MUSTARD CROP?,Spray 40 g Actara 25 WG or 400 ml malathion or 600 ml chlorpyrifos 20 EC mixed with 80-100 liters of water per acre.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Oilseeds,Mustard,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF BLIGHT AND DOWNY MILDEW IN RAPESEED-MUSTARD?,Spray 250 grams of Blytox or Indofil M45 in 200 liters of water.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Oilseeds,Mustard,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF CATERPILLAR IN MUSTARD?,Spray 250 ml of Acalx (Quinlphas 25 EC) or 1 liter of chlorpyrifos in 60-80 liters of water.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Oilseeds,Mustard,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF HAIRY CATERPILLAR IN RAPESEED-MUSTARD?,Spray 400 ml of Acalx (Quinlphas 25 EC) or 200 ml of Nuvan 85 SL or 1 liter of Chlorpyrifos in 100 liters of water.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Oilseeds,Mustard,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF PAINTED BUG IN MUSTARD?,"Application of irrigation three to four weeks after sowing helps reduce the pest population. If attack is seen in the field, spray malathion 400 ml per acre.","[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Oilseeds,Mustard,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME THE YELLOWING OF LEAVES OF MUSTARD DUE TO HEAVY IRRIGATION?,Spray 2% urea (2 kg urea in 100 liters of water) per acre to prevent mustard yellowing after heavy waterlogging.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Oilseeds,Mustard,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME THE CONTROL OF PHOSPHOROUS DEFICIENCY IN MUSTARD?,Spray 1 kg NPK in 100 liters of water at 17:44:00 per acre.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Oilseeds,Mustard,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME THE CONTROL OF SULPHUR DEFICIENCY IN MUSTARD?,"Add 100 kg of gypsum per acre at the time of land preparation in sulfur deficient soils. If the phosphorus content in the form of single superphosphate is given to the wheat crop, gypsum is not required and if sulfur deficiency is found, gypsum can be added to the standing crop as well. Or spray 500 grams of soluble sulfur 80% in 200 liters of water.","[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Oilseeds,Mustard,Nutrient Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME NECESSARY NUTRITION OF TORIA MUSTARD?,"NITROGEN--25kg/acre, PHOSPHORUS --8kg/acre, POTASH--depend on soil test
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Oilseeds,Mustard,Fertilizer Uses,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FERTILIZER REQUIREMENT IN TORIA MUSTARD?,"UREA--55kg/acre, SSP--20kg/acre,MURIATE OF POTASH--depend on soil test
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Oilseeds,Mustard,Nutrient Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME NECESSARY NUTRITION OF RAYA AND GOBI SARSON MUSTARD?,"NITROGEN--40kg/acre, PHOSPHORUS --12kg/acre, POTASH--6kg/acre
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Oilseeds,Mustard,Fertilizer Uses,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FERTILIZER REQUIREMENT IN RAYA AND GOBI SARSON MUSTARD?,"UREA--95kg/acre, SSP--75kg/acre,MURIATE OF POTASH--10kg/acre
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Oilseeds,Soybean,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOYBEAN?,"Soybean called as golden beans is belongs to legume family. It is native of East Asia. It is a rich source of Protein also excellent source of fibre. Oil extracted from soybean contain small amount of saturated fat. In Punjab, it plays an important role in crop diversification.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Oilseeds,Soybean,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOWING TIME OF  SOYBEAN CROP?,First fortnight of June is best time for sowing Soybean.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Oilseeds,Soybean,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SUITABLE TEMPARARTURE OF SOYBEAN CROPS?,"The suitable temparature: Sowing Temparature- 28-38 degree, 
Normal Temperature- 18-38 degree,Harvesting Temperature- 18-25 degree, Rainfall- 30-60cm
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Oilseeds,Soybean,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOWING TEMPARARTURE OF SOYBEAN CROPS?,Sowing Temparature- 28-38 degree,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Oilseeds,Soybean,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME NORMAL TEMPARARTURE OF SOYBEAN CROPS?,Normal Temperature- 18-38 degree,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Oilseeds,Soybean,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME HARVESTING TEMPARARTURE OF SOYBEAN CROPS?,Harvesting Temperature- 18-25 degree,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Oilseeds,Soybean,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME RAINFALL OF SOYBEAN CROPS?,Rainfall- 30-60cm,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Oilseeds,Soybean,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SUITABLE TIME OF  SOYBEAN CROP?,First fortnight of June is best time for sowing Soybean.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Oilseeds,Soybean,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOIL MANAGEMENT OF  SOYBEAN CROP?,"It gives good result, when grown on well drained, fertile loamy soils. pH of 6 to 7.5 is favourable for optimum yield of soybean. Water logged, saline/alkaline soils are not suitable for its cultivation. Low temperature affect crop severely.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Oilseeds,Soybean,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FIELD PREPARATION OF  SOYBEAN CROP?,Prepared field by giving two to three ploughings followed by planking.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Oilseeds,Soybean,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SPACING OF  SOYBEAN CROP?,Spacing:While sowing use row to row spacing of 45 cm and plant to plant spacing of 4-7 cm.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Oilseeds,Soybean,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOWING DEPTH OF  SOYBEAN CROP?,"Sowing Depth:Sow seeds at depth of 2.5-5 cm.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Oilseeds,Soybean,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME HARVESTING OF  SOYBEAN CROP?,"Pods become dry and leaves changes their color to yellow and fall of, it is sign of crop is ready for harvesting. Harvest the crop with sickle or by hand. After harvesting, carry out threshing operation.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Oilseeds,Soybean,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME POST HARVESTING OF  SOYBEAN CROP?,"After drying, carry out proper cleaning of seeds. Remove small size seeds, damaged seeds and crop stalks.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Oilseeds,Soybean,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME METHOD OF SOWING OF  SOYBEAN CROP?,"Method of sowing:Sow seeds with help of seed drill.

","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Oilseeds,Soybean,Water Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WATER MANAGEMENT OF  SOYBEAN CROP?,Overall crop required three to four irrigation. Irrigation at time of pod filling stage is necessary. Water stress at this period will affect yield drastically. Apply irrigation depending upon rainfall conditions. No irrigation required in good rainfall conditions.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Oilseeds,Soybean,Weed Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WEED MANAGEMENT OF  SOYBEAN CROP?,"To keep field weed free, two hoeing are required, give first hoeing 20 days after sowing and second hoeing 40 days after sowing.To control weed chemically, after sowing, within two days, take spray of Pendimethalin@800 ml/acre in 100-200 ltrs of water.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Oilseeds,Soybean,Fertilizer Uses,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME BETTER/GOOD/FERTILIZER USE S OF  SOYBEAN CROP?,"Apply FYM or well decomposed cowdung@4 ton/acre. Also apply Nitrogen@12.5 kg and Phosphorus@32 kg in form of Urea@28kg and SSP@200 kg per acre at time of sowing.To obtain good growth and optimum yield, take spray of Urea@3 kg/150 ltr of water on 60th and 75th day after sowing.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Oilseeds,Soybean,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOYBEAN IMPROVED VARIETIES?,"SL 525 (2003): It has bright, brilliant, cream-colored grains with a light black (grey) hilum that are all the same size. 37.2 percent of the protein and 21.9 percent of the oil in its grains. In addition to tolerating stem blight and root-knot nematode, it is resistant to the yellow mosaic virus. It needs 144 days to reach maturity. Itsaverage seed yield is about 6.1 quintals per acre.

SL 744 (2010): Its grains are bright and light yellow in colour, and its hilum is grey. Its grains are made up of 21.0 percent oil and 42.3 percent protein. It is resistant to soybean mosaic and the yellow mosaic virus. It matures in about 139 days. It produces about 7.3 quintals of seeds per acre on average.

SL 958 (2014): Its grains are shiny and light yellow in colour, and its hilum is black. Protein makes up 41.7 percent of its grains, and oil makes up 20.2 percent. It has a high level of immunity to soybean mosaic virus and yellow mosaic virus. The maturation period is roughly 142 days. Its average seed output per acre is around 7.3 quintals.

","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
