","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Green Gram,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME GREEN GRAM  VARIETIEY   PS 16?,PS 16: Suitable for cultivation in all over the country. Ready to harvest in 60-65 days. Gives average yield of 4 - 4.8 qtl/acre.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Green Gram,Seeds,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SEED MANAGEMENT OF  GREEN GRAM CROP?,"Seed Rate:
For Kharif season, use seed rate of 8-9 kg/acre whereas for summer season used seed rate of 12-15 kg/acre.

Seed Treatment:
Seed should be treated with Captan or Thiram @3 gm/kg of seed before sowing.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Green Gram,Seeds,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SEED TREATMENT OF  GREEN GRAM CROP?,"Seed treatment:
Seed should be treated with Captan or Thiram @3 gm/kg of seed before sowing.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Green Gram,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FUNGICIDE NAME  OF  GREEN GRAM CROP?,"Fungicide name Quantity (Dosage per kg seed)
Captan 3gm
Thiram 3gm

","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Green Gram,Plant Protection,"INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF SUCKING PEST (JASSID, APHID, WHITE FLY)  IN  GREEN GRAM CROP?","Sucking pest (Jassid, aphid, white fly): If infestation is observed, take spray of Malathion @ 375ml or Dimethoate @ 250ml or Oxydemeton Methyl @ 250ml/acre.
For white fly control, take spray of Thiamethoxam @40gm Triazophos@600ml/acre. If necessary take second spray 10days after first spray.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Green Gram,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF MITE  IN  GREEN GRAM CROP?,Mite: If infestation is observed take spray of Dimethoate 30EC @150ml/acre.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Green Gram,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF BLISTER BEETLE  IN  GREEN GRAM CROP?,"Blister beetle: They cause damage at flowering stage. They feed on flowers, buds thus prevent grain formation.If infestation is observed, take spray of Indoxacarb 14.5SC @ 200ml or Acephate 75SC @ 800gm/acre. Carry out spraying in evening hours and if necessary take second spray 10days after first spray.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Green Gram,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF POD BORER  IN  GREEN GRAM CROP?,"Pod Borer: Serious pest cause heavy loss in yield. If infestation is observed, take spray of Indoxacarb 14.5SC @ 200ml or Acephate 75SP @ 800gm or Spinosad 45SC @ 60ml/acre. Repeat spray after two weeks.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Green Gram,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF TOBACCO CATERPILLAR  IN  GREEN GRAM CROP?,"Tobacco caterpillar: If infestation is observed, take spray of Acephate 57SP @ 800gm/acre or Chlorpyriphos 20EC @1.5Ltr/acre. If necessary take second spray 10days after first spray.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Green Gram,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF HAIRY CATERPILLAR  IN  GREEN GRAM CROP?,"Hairy Caterpillar: To control hairy caterpillar pick caterpillar manually and destroyed by crushing or putting in kerosene water when infestation is low. In case of high infestation, take spray of Quinalphos @500ml or Dichlorvos @200ml/acre.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Green Gram,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF YELLOW MOSAIC VIRUS  IN  GREEN GRAM CROP?,"Yellow mosaic virus: It is spread due to white fly. Irregular yellow, green patches are observed on leaves. Pods not developed on infected plants.Grow yellow mosaic virus resistant varieties. For white fly control, take spray of Thiamethoxam@40gm, Triazophos@ 600ml/acre. If necessary take second spray 10days after first spray.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Green Gram,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF CERCOSPORA LEAF SPOT IN  GREEN GRAM CROP?,"Cercospora leaf spot: As a preventive measure, do seed treatment with Captan and Thiram. Use cercospora leaf spot resistant variety. If infestation is observed take spray of Zineb 75WP @400gm/acre. Take two to three sprays at interval of 10 days.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Green Gram,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL MECONTROL OF TOBACCO CATERPILLAR  IN SUMMER GREEN GRAM?,Spray 150 ml Rimon 10 EC (Novaluran) or Chlorpyrifos 20 EC 1.5 liters in 100 liters of water,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Pulses,Green Gram,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME BETTER FRUITING OF GREEN GRAM?,NPK (19:19:19) can be sprayed for growth of mung bean and NPK (13-0-45) for high yield.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Pulses,Green Gram,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF CERCOSPORA LEAF SPOT IN GREEN GRAM CROP?,"For prevention of leaf spot disease in mongoose, spray 400 grams of Jineb 75 WG (Dithan Z-78) in 100 liters of water per acre and spray at 10 day intervals.","[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Pulses,Green Gram,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF GROWN UP LARVAE AMERICAN BOLL WORM IN GREEN GRAM?,Control of large American weevils in mango Tracer 48 SC (Spinosad) 60 ml or 200 ml Avant 15 SC/ Avant 15 EC (Indoxacarb) or 60 ml Kaurjan 18.5 SC* (Chlorantraniliprole) Spray per acre in 125 liters of water.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Pulses,Green Gram,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME THE BETTER GROWTH OF SUMMER GREEN GRAM?,Spray 1 kg of NPK 19:19:19 in 100 liters of water per acre.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Pulses,Green Gram,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF BORER IN SUMMER GREEN GRAM?,Spray 150 ml of Rimon 10 EC (Novaluran) in 100 liters of water .,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Pulses,Green Gram,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL MESUMMER GREEN GRAM PRODUCTION?,5 to 6 quintal of mung bean per acre can be obtained by planting summer mung bean depending on the variety.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Pulses,Green Gram,Nutrient Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME NECESSARY NUTRITION OF GREEN GRAM?,"NITROGEN--5kg/acre, PHOSPHORUS --16kg/acre, POTASH--As per soil test result
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Green Gram,Fertilizer Uses,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FERTILIZER REQUIREMENT IN GREEN GRAM?,"UREA--12kg/acre, SSP--100kg/acre,MURIATE OF POTASH--As per soil test result
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Kidney Bean,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME KIDNEY BEAN?,"Kidney beans is also known as the chilli bean because of its dark red color and the visually resemblance the shape of a kidney. Kidney beans are a good source of protein also it is excellent source of molybdenum. It contain good source of cholesterol-lowering fibre. Rajma is a popular dish from the North Indian cuisine made from red kidney beans. Maharashtra, Jammu and Kashmir, Himachal Pradesh, Uttarakhand, West Bengal, Uttar Pradesh, Tamil Nadu, Kerala and Karnataka are major kidney bean growing states in India.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Kidney Bean,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOWING TIME OF  KIDNEY BEAN CROP?,"For spring season, best time for Kidney beans cultivation is February-March and for Kharif season, it is sown during May-June month. In Punjab, some farmers sow Kidney beans in last week of January.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Kidney Bean,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SUITABLE TEMPARARTURE OF KIDNEY BEAN CROPS?,"The suitable temparature: Sowing Temparature- 22-25 degree, 
Normal Temperature- 15-25 degree,Harvesting Temperature- 28-30 degree, Rainfall- 60-15mm
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Kidney Bean,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOWING TEMPARARTURE OF KIDNEY BEAN CROPS?,Sowing Temparature- 22-25 degree,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Kidney Bean,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME NORMAL TEMPARARTURE OF KIDNEY BEAN CROPS?,Normal Temperature- 15-25 degree,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Kidney Bean,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME HARVESTING TEMPARARTURE OF KIDNEY BEAN CROPS?,Harvesting Temperature- 28-30 degree,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Kidney Bean,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME RAINFALL OF KIDNEY BEAN CROPS?,Rainfall- 60-15mm,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Kidney Bean,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SUITABLE TIME OF  KIDNEY BEAN CROP?,"For spring season, best time for Kidney beans cultivation is February-March and for Kharif season, it is sown during May-June month. In Punjab, some farmers sow Kidney beans in last week of January.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Kidney Bean,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOIL MANAGEMENT OF  KIDNEY BEAN CROP?,It can be grown on wide range of soils from light sandy to heavy clay soils. Well drained loamy soil is good for kidney beans cultivation. It is very sensitive to saline soils. Gives best result when pH of soil is 5.5 to 6.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Kidney Bean,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FIELD PREPARATION OF  KIDNEY BEAN CROP?,Give two to three ploughing to bring soil at fine tilth. Make field level so that water stagnation should not occurred in main field. Crop is very sensitive to water logging. At last ploughing apply Farmyard Manure or well decomposed cow dung@60-80qtl/acre.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Kidney Bean,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SPACING OF  KIDNEY BEAN CROP?,Spacing:For early sown varieties use spacing of 45-60 cm between rows and 10-15 cm between plants. For pole type varieties sown at distance of 1 m in hill@3-4plant per hill.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Kidney Bean,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOWING DEPTH OF  KIDNEY BEAN CROP?,Sowing Depth:Sow the seeds at depth of 6-7 cm.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Kidney Bean,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME HARVESTING OF  KIDNEY BEAN CROP?,"Harvest when pods are full grown and ripe and there color turn to yellow. Also leaves turn yellow and majority of leaves drop. Depending upon variety use pods are ready to harvest 7-12 days after flowering. Overall crop is ready to harvest in 120-130 days. Do harvesting at right time as delay cause shattering. Keep harvested plant for three-four days in sun. After proper drying of crop, threshing is done with help of bullocks or with sticks.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Kidney Bean,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME POST HARVESTING OF  KIDNEY BEAN CROP?,"Kidney beans required little processing after harvesting but take care during storage to maintain good quality. Before storing, do sorting and remove damaged, infected beans. Heat and humidity cause deterioration in quality so always stored beans in cool, dark and dry place.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Kidney Bean,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME METHOD OF SOWING OF  KIDNEY BEAN CROP?,"Method of sowing:For sowing dibbling method used. In plain area seeds are sown in line or on bed where as in hilly areas, seeds are sown on ridge.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Kidney Bean,Water Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WATER MANAGEMENT OF  KIDNEY BEAN CROP?,"For better germination of seed give pre-sowing irrigation. 6-7 irrigations are required during growing season. Irrigation on 25th day after sowing and three irrigation at 25 days interval are necessary to get optimum yield. Give irrigation prior to blooming, during flowering and at pod development stage, water stress at these stage will lead to yield loss.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Kidney Bean,Weed Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WEED MANAGEMENT OF  KIDNEY BEAN CROP?,Initial growth period is crucial for crop growth. Avoid weed infestation at this stage. Complete weeding operations synchronized along with fertilizer and irrigation operations. Use Fluchloralin@ 800ml/acre or Pendimethalin@1ltr per acre as pre-emergence weedicide.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Kidney Bean,Fertilizer Uses,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME BETTER/GOOD/FERTILIZER USE S OF  KIDNEY BEAN CROP?,Apply Nitrogen@40kg/acre and Phosphorus@25kg/acre in form Urea@87kg and SSP@150kg/acre. Do soil testing before sowing for accurate fertilizer application.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Kidney Bean,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME KIDNEY BEAN IMPROVED VARIETIES?,"VL Rajma 125: Suitable for timely sown of Uttarakhand Hills. 4-5 seeds per pods and 100 seed weight about 41.38 gm.

RBL 6: Suitable for irrigated areas of Punjab state. 6-8 seeds per pod and seeds are of light green color.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Kidney Bean,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME KIDNEY BEAN  VARIETIEY   VL RAJMA 125?,"VL Rajma 125: Suitable for timely sown of Uttarakhand Hills. 4-5 seeds per pods and 100 seed weight about 41.38 gm.

","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Kidney Bean,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME KIDNEY BEAN  VARIETIEY   RBL 6?,RBL 6: Suitable for irrigated areas of Punjab state. 6-8 seeds per pod and seeds are of light green color.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Kidney Bean,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME KIDNEY BEAN  HIGH YIELD VARIETIEY?,"HUR 15, HUR-137, Amber and Arun. Also Arka Komal, Arka Suvidha, Pusa Parvathi, Pusa Himalatha, VL Boni 1, Ooty 1.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Kidney Bean,Seeds,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SEED MANAGEMENT OF  KIDNEY BEAN CROP?,"Seed Rate:
For early sown varieties use seed rate of 30-35kg/acre. For pole type varieties sown at distance of 1m in hill@3-4plant per hill with seed rate of 10-12kg/acre.

Seed Treatment:
Before sowing treat seeds with Thiram@4gm per Kg of seeds. Dried seed in shade and then sown immediately.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Kidney Bean,Seeds,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SEED TREATMENT OF  KIDNEY BEAN CROP?,"Seed treatment:
Before sowing treat seeds with Thiram@4gm per Kg of seeds. Dried seed in shade and then sown immediately.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Kidney Bean,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FUNGICIDE NAME  OF  KIDNEY BEAN CROP?,"Fungicide name Quantity (Dosage per kg seed)
Captan 3gm
Thiram 3gm

","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Kidney Bean,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME ROTATION OF  KIDNEY BEAN CROP?,"Kidney Bean follows Kharif crop like mash, fodder, Kidney Bean, maize etc.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Kidney Bean,Fertilizer Uses,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WATER SOLUABLE FERTILIZER OF  KIDNEY BEAN CROP?,"To improve pod filling spraying of nutrient solution is important. This can be prepared by soaking DAP@2.5 kg, Ammonium sulphate@1kg and Borax@500 gm in 37 lit of water overnight. The next day morning it can be filtered and about 16 litre of mixture can be obtained and it may be diluted with 234 lit of water so as to made up to 200 litre to spray for one acre. Planofix@4ml/15 ltr can also be mixed while spraying. This can be sprayed on 25th and 35th day after sowing.

","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Kidney Bean,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF THRIPS  IN  KIDNEY BEAN CROP?,"Thrips: Commonly observed pest. Mostly observed in dry weather. They suck sap from the foliage and results in curling of leaves. Also causes flower drop. To check severity of thrips incidence, keep blue sticky traps @6-8 per acre. Also to reduce the incidence spray Verticillium lecani@5gm/Ltr water
2) If incidence of thrips is more, then take spray of Imidacloprid 17.8SL or Fipronil @1ml/Ltr water or Acephate 75% WP@1gm/Ltr.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Kidney Bean,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF APHID  IN  KIDNEY BEAN CROP?,"Aphid: They suck sap from the leaf. They excrete honey like substance and developed sooty mould i.e blackish colour fungus on the Calyx and pods thus deteriorate quality of product.
To control take spray of Acephate 75SP@1gm/Ltr or Methyl demeton 25EC@2ml/Ltr of water. Soil application of granular insecticides viz Carbofuran, Phorate@4-8kg/acre on 15 and 60 days after transplanting were also effective.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Kidney Bean,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF MITE  IN  KIDNEY BEAN CROP?,"Mite: These are widely distributed pest observed throughout the world. Nymphs and adults feed exclusively on the lower surface of the leaves. Infected leaves gives cup shape appearance. Heavy infestation results in defoliation, bud shedding and drying of leaves.
If Infestation of yellow mite is observed in field, spray of Chlorfenapyr@15ml/Ltr, Abamectin@15ml/Ltr are found effective. Mites is a serious pest and it may cause yield loss up to 80%. For effective control spray Spiromesifen 22.9SC @200ml/acre/180Ltr of water.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Kidney Bean,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF POWDERY MILDEW  IN  KIDNEY BEAN CROP?,"Powdery Mildew: Patchy, White powdery growth appear on lower side of leaves. It parasitizes the plant using it as a food source. It can developed at any stage of crop development. In severe infestation it causes defoliation.
Avoid water lodging in field. Keep field clean. To Control spray with Hexaconazole along with sticker@1ml/Ltr of water. In case of sudden rain, chances of powdery mildew. Mild infestation take spray of water soluble Sulphur@ 20gm/10Ltr of water 2-3 times with interval of 10 days.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Kidney Bean,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF WILT  IN  KIDNEY BEAN CROP?,"Wilt: Moist and poorly drain soil causes damping off disease. It is soil borne disease. Water soaking and shrivelling of stem occurs. Seedlings killed before emergence. 
To control Wilt, Drench nearby soil with Copper oxychloride@25gm or Carbendazim@20gm/10Ltr of water. To control Wilting of plants due to root rot do drenching with Trichoderma bio fungus@2.5kg/500Ltr water, near to roots of plants.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Kidney Bean,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF YELLOW MOSAIC  IN  KIDNEY BEAN CROP?,"Yellow Mosaic: Light and green patches observed on leaves. In early stage plant growth get stops. Yellowing, chlorotic ring spots on leaves and fruits. Select healthy and disease free seeds for cultivation. Uproot and destroyed infected plant away from field.If observed in field to control it take spray of Acephate 75SP@600gm/200Ltr or Methyl demeton 25EC@2ml/Ltr of water.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Kidney Bean,Nutrient Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME NECESSARY NUTRITION OF KIDNEY BEAN?,"NITROGEN--40kg/acre, PHOSPHORUS --25kg/acre, POTASH--As per soil test result
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Kidney Bean,Fertilizer Uses,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FERTILIZER REQUIREMENT IN KIDNEY BEAN?,"UREA--87kg/acre, SSP--150kg/acre,MURIATE OF POTASH--As per soil test result
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Mash,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME MASH?,"It is one of the most important pulse crops of India. It is rich source of protein and phosphoric acid. It is used as dal and it is important ingredient of breakfast. In India, major mash areas are Madhya Pradesh, Uttar Pradesh, Punjab, Maharashtra, West Bengal, Andhra Pradesh and Karnataka. In Punjab, it is cultivated on 2.2 thousand hectares (2012-13).","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Mash,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOWING TIME OF  MASH CROP?,"Optimum time for kharif sowing is last week of June to first week of July. Optimum time for summer cultivation is from March to April. For sub-mountainous region, complete sowing from 15-25 July.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Mash,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SUITABLE TEMPARARTURE OF MASH CROPS?,"The suitable temparature: Sowing Temparature- 25-35 degree, 
Normal Temperature- 15-30 degree,Harvesting Temperature- 18-25 degree, Rainfall- 50-75cm
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Mash,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOWING TEMPARARTURE OF MASH CROPS?,Sowing Temparature- 25-35 degree,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Mash,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME NORMAL TEMPARARTURE OF MASH CROPS?,Normal Temperature- 15-30 degree,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Mash,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME HARVESTING TEMPARARTURE OF MASH CROPS?,Harvesting Temperature- 18-25 degree,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Mash,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME RAINFALL OF MASH CROPS?,Rainfall- 50-75cm,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Mash,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SUITABLE TIME OF  MASH CROP?,"Optimum time for kharif sowing is last week of June to first week of July. Optimum time for summer cultivation is from March to April. For sub-mountainous region, complete sowing from 15-25 July.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Mash,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOIL MANAGEMENT OF  MASH CROP?,"Saline - alkaline soil, also waterlogged soils are not suitable for mash cultivation. For good growth, it required stiff loamy or heavy soils with good water retentive capacity.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Mash,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FIELD PREPARATION OF  MASH CROP?,To bring soil to fine tilth give two to three ploughing. After each ploughing carry out planking. Keep field weed free.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Mash,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SPACING OF  MASH CROP?,"Spacing:Use row spacing of 30 cm and plant to plant spacing of 10 cm for Kharif sowing. For Rabi sowing use row spacing of 22.5 cm and plant to plant spacing of 4-5 cm.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Mash,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOWING DEPTH OF  MASH CROP?,Sowing Depth:Sow seeds at depth of 4-6 cm. Mash grown in hilly areas are of better quality.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Mash,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME HARVESTING OF  MASH CROP?,Best time for harvesting of mash is when leaves are shed and pods become greyish black. Cut crop with sickle and then spread harvested crop on floor to dry. Then threshing is done and seeds are separated from pods.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Mash,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME POST HARVESTING OF  MASH CROP?,"Kidney beans required little processing after harvesting but take care during storage to maintain good quality. Before storing, do sorting and remove damaged, infected beans. Heat and humidity cause deterioration in quality so always stored beans in cool, dark and dry place.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Mash,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME METHOD OF SOWING OF  MASH CROP?,Method of sowing:For sowing use Kera or Pora method or sow seeds by seed drill.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Mash,Water Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WATER MANAGEMENT OF  MASH CROP?,Mash is grown as a kharif crop. If needed provide irrigation depending upon the climatic conditions.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Mash,Weed Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WEED MANAGEMENT OF  MASH CROP?,"To keep field weed free, one or two hoeing are required. Take first hoeing one month after sowing. To control weed chemically, after sowing, within two days, take spray of Pendimethalin@1Ltr/acre in 100-200Ltrs of water.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Mash,Fertilizer Uses,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME BETTER/GOOD/FERTILIZER USE S OF  MASH CROP?,"At time of sowing, apply Nitrogen@5kg in form of Urea@11kg per acre and Phosphorus@10kg in form of SSP@60kg/acre.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Mash,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME MASH IMPROVED VARIETIES?,"Mash 338: Suitable for Kharif sowing. Dwarf and short duration variety. Ready to harvest in 90 days. Each pod contains bold and black 6-7 seeds. It is resistant to mosaic virus and leaf spot. Gives average yield of 3.5 qtl/acre. 

Mash 114: Suitable for Kharif sowing. Dwarf and short duration variety. Ready to harvest in 85 days. Each pod contains bold and black 6-7 seeds. Gives average yield of 3.7qtl/acre.
 
Mash 218: Suitable for summer sowing. Short duration variety. Ready to harvest in 76 days. Each pod contains bold, dull black 6 seeds. Gives average yield of 4 qtl/acre. 
 
Mash 414: Suitable for summer sowing. Short duration variety. Ready to harvest in 73 days. Each pod contains bold, black 6-7 seeds. Gives average yield of 4.3 qtl/acre.
 
Mash 1008: Suitable for summer sowing. Ready to harvest in 73 days. It is fairly resistant to mosaic virus and leaf spot. Each pod contains bold, black 6-7 seeds. Gives average yield of 4.6 qtl/acre.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
