","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Mash,Seeds,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SEED MANAGEMENT OF  MASH CROP?,"Seed Rate:
For kharif sowing use seed rate of 7-8kg/acre whereas for summer sowing use seed rate of 19-20kg/acre of bold seeds.

Seed Treatment:
Before sowing treat seeds with Captan or Thiram or Mancozeb or Carbendazim@2.5gm per kg of seeds. After then dry them in shades. After chemical treatment treat seed with Rhizobium@2gm/kg of seeds.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Mash,Seeds,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SEED TREATMENT OF  MASH CROP?,"Seed treatment:
Before sowing treat seeds with Captan or Thiram or Mancozeb or Carbendazim@2.5gm per kg of seeds. After then dry them in shades. After chemical treatment treat seed with Rhizobium@2gm/kg of seeds.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Mash,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FUNGICIDE NAME  OF  MASH CROP?,"Fungicide/Insecticide name Quantity (Dosage per Kg seed)
Carbendazim 2.5gm
Captan 2.5gm
Thiram 2.5gm
Mancozeb 2.5gm
 

","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Mash,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF YELLOW MOSAIC VIRUS  IN  MASH CROP?,"Yellow mosaic virus: It is spread due to white fly. Irregular yellow, green patches are observed on leaves. Pods not developed on infected plants.Grow yellow mosaic virus resistant varieties. For white fly control, take spray of Thiamethoxam@40gm, Triazophos@ 600ml/acre. If necessary take second spray 10days after first spray.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Mash,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF CERCOSPORA LEAF SPOT  IN  MASH CROP?,"Cercospora leaf spot: As a preventive measure, do seed treatment with Captan and Thiram. Use cercospora leaf spot resistant variety. If infestation is observed take spray of Zineb 75WP@400gm/acre. Take two to three sprays at interval of 10days.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Mash,Plant Protection,"INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF SUCKING PEST (JASSID, APHID, WHITE FLY)  IN  MASH CROP?","Sucking pest (Jassid, aphid, white fly): If infestation is observed, take spray of Malathion@375ml or Dimethoate@250ml or Oxydemeton Methyl@250ml/acre.For white fly control, take spray of Thiamethoxam@40gm Triazophos@600ml/acre. If necessary take second spray 10days after first spray.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Mash,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF TOBACCO CATERPILLAR  IN  MASH CROP?,"Tobacco caterpillar: If infestation is observed, take spray of Acephate 57SP@800gm/acre or Chlorpyriphos 20EC@ 1.5Ltr/acre. If necessary take second spray 10days after first spray. 
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Mash,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF WHITE FLY  IN  MASH CROP?,Spray 40 grams of Ektra 25 WG (thiamethoxam) in 100 liters of water per acre for the prevention of whitefly.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Mash,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF HAIRY CATERPILLAR  IN  MASH CROP?,"Hairy Caterpillar: To control hairy caterpillar pick caterpillar manually and destroyed by crushing or putting in kerosene water when infestation is low. In case of high infestation, take spray of Quinalphos@500ml or Dichlorvos@200ml/acre.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Mash,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF POD BORER  IN  MASH CROP?,"Pod Borer: Serious pest cause heavy loss in yield. If infestation is observed, take spray of Indoxacarb 14.5SC@200ml or Acephate 75SP@800gm or Spinosad 45SC@60ml/acre. Repeat spray after two weeks.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Mash,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF MITE  IN  MASH CROP?,Mite: If infestation is observed take spray of Dimethoate 30EC@150ml/acre.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Mash,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF BLISTER BEETLE IN  MASH CROP?,"Blister beetle: They cause damage at flowering stage. They feed on flowers, buds thus prevent grain formation. If infestation is observed, take spray of Indoxacarb 14.5SC@200ml or Acephate 75SC@800gm/acre. Carry out spraying in evening hours and if necessary take second spray 10 days after first spray.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Mash,Nutrient Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME NECESSARY NUTRITION OF MASH?,"NITROGEN--5kg/acre, PHOSPHORUS --10kg/acre, POTASH--As per soil test result
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Mash,Fertilizer Uses,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FERTILIZER REQUIREMENT IN MASH?,"UREA--11kg/acre, SSP--60kg/acre,MURIATE OF POTASH--As per soil test result
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Mash,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME GROWTH REGULATOR USED TO IMPROVING POD FILLING IN MASH?,Spray 1 KG NPK (13:0:45) mixed with 100 liters of water for one acre.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Pulses,Pigeon Pea,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME PIGEON PEA?,"It is a popular pulses crop and it is rich source of Protein. It is cultivated in tropical and semitropical regions. It is important legumes crop of rain fed and semi-arid tropics and it can grow as single crop or intermixed with cereals. It enriches soil through symbiotic nitrogen fixation. Andhra Pradesh, Gujarat, Karnataka, Madhya Pradesh, Maharashtra and Uttar Pradesh are major Pigeon pea producing states in India.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Pigeon Pea,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOWING TIME OF  PIGEON PEA CROP?,Timely sowing of crop is important as delay in sowing leads to yield loss. Sow crop in second fortnight of May for obtaining high grain yield,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Pigeon Pea,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SUITABLE TEMPARARTURE OF PIGEON PEA CROPS?,"The suitable temparature: Sowing Temparature- 25-33 degree, 
Normal Temperature- 30-35 degree,Harvesting Temperature- 35-40 degree, Rainfall- 600-650mm
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Pigeon Pea,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOWING TEMPARARTURE OF PIGEON PEA CROPS?,Sowing Temparature- 25-33 degree,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Pigeon Pea,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME NORMAL TEMPARARTURE OF PIGEON PEA CROPS?,Normal Temperature- 30-35 degree,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Pigeon Pea,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME HARVESTING TEMPARARTURE OF PIGEON PEA CROPS?,Harvesting Temperature- 35-40 degree,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Pigeon Pea,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME RAINFALL OF PIGEON PEA CROPS?,"Rainfall- 600-650mm
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Pigeon Pea,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SUITABLE TIME OF  PIGEON PEA CROP?,Timely sowing of crop is important as delay in sowing leads to yield loss. Sow crop in second fortnight of May for obtaining high grain yield,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Pigeon Pea,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOIL MANAGEMENT OF  PIGEON PEA CROP?,It grows on variety of soil. It gives best result on fertile and well drained loamy soils. The saline-alkaline or waterlogged soils are unfit for its cultivation. It can grow successfully on soils having pH ranges from 6.5 to 7.5.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Pigeon Pea,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FIELD PREPARATION OF  PIGEON PEA CROP?,"Prepared land by taking one deep ploughing followed by two or three times harrowing. Planking should be followed after each ploughing. It cannot withstand in water logging conditions, prepared field in such a way that water stagnation should not take place. Crop Rotation: Follow crop rotation of Arhar with Wheat or Barley or Sufed Senji or Sugarcane.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Pigeon Pea,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SPACING OF  PIGEON PEA CROP?,"Spacing:For sowing use spacing of 50 cm between the rows while 25 cm between the plant.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Pigeon Pea,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOWING DEPTH OF  PIGEON PEA CROP?,Sowing Depth:Seed are sown with help of seed drill at depth of about 7-10 cm.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Pigeon Pea,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME HARVESTING OF  PIGEON PEA CROP?,"For vegetable purpose harvest plant when leaves and pods are of green color. For grain purpose, when 75-80% pods turn brown and dry, it is right time of harvesting. Delay in harvesting result in damage of seeds. Harvesting can be done manually by cutting stem or by Machine. After harvesting keep bundles of plant upright for drying purpose. Grains are removed from plant by threshing or by traditionally i.e beating plants with sticks.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Pigeon Pea,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME POST HARVESTING OF  PIGEON PEA CROP?,Grains of harvested crop must be well dried before storage. And take care to avoid the pulse beetle infestation in storage.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Pigeon Pea,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME METHOD OF SOWING OF  PIGEON PEA CROP?,Method of sowing:Seeds can be sown by broadcasting method but line sowing with help of seed drill is more efficient way of sowing for good yield.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Pigeon Pea,Water Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WATER MANAGEMENT OF  PIGEON PEA CROP?,"Three to four week after sowing apply first irrigation. Remaining irrigations are depends upon rainfall intensity. Flower initiation and pod setting stages are the most crucial to drought stress. Therefore, irrigation at these stages is essential for good yield. Avoid excessive irrigation as it leads to more vegetative growth and incidence of Phytophthora and alternaria blight. Do not apply irrigation after mid-September; it will affect maturity of crop.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Pigeon Pea,Weed Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WEED MANAGEMENT OF  PIGEON PEA CROP?,"Take one hoeing, about three weeks after sowing and another hoeing about six week after sowing. Apply Pendimethalin @ 1Ltr/acre in 150-200ltr of water as pre-emergence herbicide within 2 days after sowing, followed by hand weeding six to seven weeks after sowing.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Pigeon Pea,Fertilizer Uses,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME BETTER/GOOD/FERTILIZER USE S OF  PIGEON PEA CROP?,"Apply N:P:K @ 6:16:12kg/acre in form of Urea @ 13kg, DAP @ 35kg or SSP @ 100kg, and MOP @ 20kg/acre. Drill all fertilizer in soil at time of sowing. Apply fertilizer based on soil testing results. Also K should be apply when soil testing show deficiency of it. In DAP is to be used, do not apply Nitrogen fertilizer.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,Pigeon Pea,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME PIGEON PEA IMPROVED VARIETIES?,"AL-15: It is a short duration variety, matures in 135 days. Pods are borne in clusters. It gives average yield of 5.5 qtl/acre.

AL 201: It is early maturity variety. It matures in about 140 days. Main stem is stronger than side branches. Each pod contains 3-5 yellowish brown and medium size seeds. It gives average yield of 6.2 qtl/acre.

PPH 4: First Arhar hybrid in Punjab. It matures in 145 days. Plants are tall and about 2.5 to 3 meter tall. Each pod contains 5 yellowish brown seeds of medium size. It gives average yield of 7.2-8 qtl/acre.

PAU 881 (2007): Its an early maturing variety with an indeterminate growth habit. It develops in 132 days and leaves the field in plenty of time to sow the next wheat crop. Its plants reach a height of about 2 metres. Pods are abundant, with each pod containing about 3-5 yellow brown, medium-sized seeds. Its average grain yield per acre is around 5.1 quintals.

AL 882 (2018): It has a semi-determinate growth habit and is a short statured, early maturing variety. It develops in about 132 days and leaves the field in plenty of time for the next wheat crop to be sown. Its plants are compact and grow to be between 1.6 and 1.8 metres tall. Pods are produced in various and scattered clusters near the top of the plant. Podding is abundant, with each pod containing 3-5 medium-sized yellowish brown seeds. The average grain yield per acre is around 5.4 quintals.

IPA 206: It is a long duration variety resistant to Wilt, Medium seed size seeds with oval shape and purple coloured seed coat. Its average yield is 10q/acre. It is recommended for UP area.

IPA 203: It shows resistance to Sterility Mosaic disease (SMD), Fusarium wilt, and phytophthora blight, large seed size with high yielding (7-8q/acre) nature. It is recommended for NPEZ (North East Plain Zone).

UPAS-120: This variety matures earlier (120-125 days). These are medium-sized, semi-spreading plants. The seeds are small and light brown. The average yield per acre is 6-8 quintals. It is vulnerable to the sterility mosaic disease.

ICPL 151 (Jagriti): Ready to harvest in 120-130 days. It gives average yield of 4 to 5 qtl/acre.

Pusa Ageti: Dwarf bold seeded variety, ready to harvest in 150 to 160 days. It gives average yield of 5 qtl /acre.

Pusa 84: Medium tall, semi spreading variety, ready to harvest in 140 to 150 days.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
