Pulses,RiceBean,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME RICEBEAN?,"Ricebean is known as Vigna umbellata as botanical name. It is a perennial legume having an average height of 30-100 cm and can be grown up to 200 cm. The leaves are trifoliate having leaflets 6-9 cm long. The flowers are bright yellow in color which bears fruits. Fruits are cylindrical which bears the seed of 6-8 mm in size. It is found in Indo-China, Southern China, Nepal, Bangladesh and India. Himachal Pradesh, Uttaranchal, Assam, Manipur, Meghalaya, Mizoram, Nagaland, Sikkim, Tripura, Madhya Pradesh and Chhattisgarh are major rice bean growing states in India.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,RiceBean,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOWING TIME OF  RICEBEAN CROP?,"As it is a kharif season crop, sowing is done mainly in the first third week of July month.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,RiceBean,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SUITABLE TEMPARARTURE OF RICEBEAN CROPS?,"The suitable temparature: Sowing Temparature- 30-35 degree, 
Normal Temperature- 18-37degree,Harvesting Temperature- 35-40 degree, Rainfall- 60-150cm
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,RiceBean,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOWING TEMPARARTURE OF RICEBEAN CROPS?,Sowing Temparature- 30-35 degree,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,RiceBean,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME NORMAL TEMPARARTURE OF RICEBEAN CROPS?,Normal Temperature- 18-37degree,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,RiceBean,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME HARVESTING TEMPARARTURE OF RICEBEAN CROPS?,Harvesting Temperature- 35-40 degree,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,RiceBean,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME RAINFALL OF RICEBEAN CROPS?,Rainfall- 60-150cm,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,RiceBean,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SUITABLE TIME OF  RICEBEAN CROP?,"As it is a kharif season crop, sowing is done mainly in the first third week of July month.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,RiceBean,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOIL MANAGEMENT OF  RICEBEAN CROP?,"It is grown in the variety of soil ranging from loamy to sandy loam soil having a good drainage system. It grows moderately on poor or light fertile soil. Avoid cultivation in the saline-alkaline soil, sandy or having waterlogged soils. Do not grow rice bean in light soils as it causes root-knot nematode problem to the crop.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,RiceBean,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FIELD PREPARATION OF  RICEBEAN CROP?,"For rice bean plantation, it requires fine seedbed which is well prepared by the farmer. For good plant standing it requires prepared seedbed. Seed germination is done on fine seedbed and transplanting is done on prepared nursery beds.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,RiceBean,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SPACING OF  RICEBEAN CROP?,"Spacing:For sowing use spacing of 50 cm between the rows while 25 cm between the plant.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,RiceBean,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOWING DEPTH OF  RICEBEAN CROP?,Sowing Depth:Seed should be sown at depth of 3-4 cm.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,RiceBean,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME HARVESTING OF  RICEBEAN CROP?,"For vegetable purpose harvest plant when leaves and pods are of green color. For grain purpose, when 75-80% pods turn brown and dry, it is right time of harvesting. Delay in harvesting result in damage of seeds. Harvesting can be done manually by cutting stem or by Machine. After harvesting keep bundles of plant upright for drying purpose. Grains are removed from plant by threshing or by traditionally i.e beating plants with sticks.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,RiceBean,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME POST HARVESTING OF  RICEBEAN CROP?,Grains of harvested crop must be well dried before storage. And take care to avoid the pulse beetle infestation in storage.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,RiceBean,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME METHOD OF SOWING OF  RICEBEAN CROP?,"Method of sowing:1.Broadcasting
2.Dibbling
3.Kera/Pora/Seed drill","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,RiceBean,Water Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WATER MANAGEMENT OF  RICEBEAN CROP?,"In monsoon, there is no need for irrigation. But when monsoon doesn occur on time or drought occurs then apply irrigation 2-3 times in the post-monsoon period.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,RiceBean,Weed Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WEED MANAGEMENT OF  RICEBEAN CROP?,Frequent weeding and hoeing are required to keep the field weed free. 1-2 hoeing are required after 30-50 days of sowing to control the weeds. Mulching is also an effective way to reduce soil temperature along with weed control.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,RiceBean,Fertilizer Uses,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME BETTER/GOOD/FERTILIZER USE S OF  RICEBEAN CROP?,"At the time of land preparation, apply well rotten farmyard manure @10-15t/acre. Apply fertilizer dose of nitrogen @6kg/acre (urea @13kg/acre) and phosphorus pentoxide @8kg/acre (single superphosphate @50kg/acre).","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,RiceBean,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME RICEBEAN IMPROVED VARIETIES?,"RBL 6: Developed in the year 2002. The variety is resistant to viral, fungal and bacterial diseases. The growth of this variety is fast. The pod formation, its development and its maturity all occur at the same time. Seeds of this variety are green in color and are resistant to insect pests. The variety matures within 125 days and gives 6 quintals/acre of average yield.

RBL 1: Developed by PAU, Ludhiana. Normal duration and high yielding crop. Gives average yield of 6qtl/acre.

RBL 35: Early maturing variety, developed by PAU, Ludhiana. Gives average yield of 6 qtl/acre.

RBL 50: High yielding variety, developed by PAU, Ludhiana. It is normal duration crop. Gives average yield of 6.5 qtl/acre.
 
PRR2: Normal duration, high yielding variety developed by GBPUA&T. It give average yield of 6qtl/acre.

BRS 1: High yielding variety, developed by NBPGR, Bhowali. It is Suitable for hilly region. This variety seeds are having black color. It give average yield of 7 qtl/acre.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Pulses,RiceBean,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME RICEBEAN  VARIETIEY   RBL 6?,"RBL 6: Developed in the year 2002. The variety is resistant to viral, fungal and bacterial diseases. The growth of this variety is fast. The pod formation, its development and its maturity all occur at the same time. Seeds of this variety are green in color and are resistant to insect pests. The variety matures within 125 days and gives 6 quintals/acre of average yield.

","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
