Cereals,Maize,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SYMPTOMS OF BANDED LEAF AND SHEATH BLIGHT IN MAIZE CROPS?,"Water soaked, straw colored necrotic lesions alternating with dark brown bands develop on basal leaf sheaths. Lesions enlarge and coalesce with each other.
In severe cases, developing ears are completely damaged and dry up prematurely with cracking of husk.",[Reference: PoP (package of practices)]
Cereals,Maize,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SYMPTOMS OF PYTHIUM STALK ROT IN MAIZE CROPS?,"In this disease, basal internodes become soft, dark brown water soaked, causing the plants lodge. Damaged internodes commonly twist before the plants lodge.",[Reference: PoP (package of practices)]
Cereals,Maize,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SYMPTOMS OF MAYDIS LEAF BLIGHT (MLB) IN MAIZE CROPS?,"It generally appears in warm tropical and sub-tropical areas to wet temperate climate. Young lesions are small and diamond shaped. As they mature, they elongate. Lesions may coalesce, producing a complete rurning of large areas of the leaves.",[Reference: PoP (package of practices)]
Cereals,Maize,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SYMPTOMS OF BACTERIAL STALK ROT IN MAIZE CROPS?,"Water soaking and rotting of basal stem especially the leaf sheaths followed by rapid rotting of basal internodes. 
The rind loses its natural green colour and gives appearance as if boiled in water. 
The rotten stalks emit a characteristic fermenting odour and may break over from the second or third basal internode. 
The infected plants wilt.",[Reference: PoP (package of practices)]
Cereals,Maize,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SYMPTOMS OF BROWN STRIPE DOWNY MILDEW IN MAIZE CROPS?,"It is characterized by the presence of long, narrow, brownish, interveinal stripes on leaves. 
Whitish downy fungal growth may be observed on close examination on underside of the stripes.",[Reference: PoP (package of practices)]
Cereals,Maize,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SYMPTOMS OF POST FLOWERING STALK ROTS IN MAIZE CROPS?,"Plants wilt after flowering. 
The rind and basal internodes become discoloured. 
On splitting, the discolouration of the pith progressing upward is also seen.",[Reference: PoP (package of practices)]
Cereals,Maize,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF SEED ROT AND SEEDLING BLIGHT IN MAIZE CROP?,Use disease free seed.,[Reference: PoP (package of practices)]
Cereals,Maize,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF POST FLOWERING STALK ROTS IN MAIZE CROP?,"Grow improved varieties such as PMH 13, PMH 11 and PMH 1).",[Reference: PoP (package of practices)]
Cereals,Maize,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF MAYDIS LEAF BLIGHT IN MAIZE CROP?,"Destroy the infected crop residue in the field. 
Grow improved varieties. 
Follow spray schedule as against Brown stripe downy mildew.",[Reference: PoP (package of practices)]
Cereals,Maize,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF BANDED LEAF AND SHEATH BLIGHT IN MAIZE CROP?,"Use of resistant/tolerant hybrids.Spray 100 ml Amistar Top 325 SC (azoxystrobin + difenoconazole) in 200 litres of water per acre at disease appearance. If needed, repeat the spray at 15 days interval.",[Reference: PoP (package of practices)]
Cereals,Maize,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF BACTERIAL STALK ROT IN MAIZE CROP?,Destroy the diseased plant debris. Keep the fields well drained. Apply Bleaching powder containing 33 Percentage chlorine@4 kg/acre as soil drench at pre-flowering stage.,[Reference: PoP (package of practices)]
Cereals,Maize,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF BROWN STRIPE DOWNY MILDEW IN MAIZE CROP?,Grow resistant varieties. Do Seed treatment with Metalaxyl@6 gm/kg of seeds. Remove infected plant and destroyed away from the field. Spray with Metalaxyl@1 gm/Ltr or Metalaxyl + Mancozeb@ 2.5 gm/Ltr of water.,[Reference: PoP (package of practices)]
Cereals,Maize,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CONTROL OF PYTHIUM STALK ROT IN MAIZE CROP?,Remove remains of previous crop and keep field clean before sowing. Maintained optimum plant population in field. Do Soil drenching with Captan at basal internode (5-7 week growth stage)@1 gm/Ltr of water.,[Reference: PoP (package of practices)]
Cereals,Maize,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME MAIZE VARIETIES FEATURE OF PMH 2 (2005)-RAINFED?,It has medium plant height with medium ear placement. Its leaves are medium sized and dark green. Tassel is of medium size and semi open. Silk is of green colour. Ears are medium long with orange flint grains having yellow caps. The cob colour is white.,[Reference: PoP (package of practices)]
Cereals,Maize,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME MAIZE VARIETIES FEATURE OF PUNJAB SWEET CORN 1 (2008)?,The leaves are broad and tassel is open with creamish anthers. Ears are medium long and the cob colour is white. Silk colour at the time of emergence is usually creamish. Husk cover is well developed and grains are orange in colour at maturity. This variety is highly suitable to use as sweet corn on commercial basis because Its developing and immature grains in green ears possess high sugar content.,[Reference: PoP (package of practices)]
Cereals,Maize,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME MAIZE VARIETIES FEATURE OF KESRI (1992)?,"Plant height and ear placement are medium. The ears are thick at the base, taper towards the tip and have good tip filling and husk cover.",[Reference: PoP (package of practices)]
Cereals,Maize,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME MAIZE VARIETIES FEATURE OF JC 4 (2021)?,"This composite has deep-orange and bold grains. It is tested very good for chappati quality parameters viz, taste, texture, appearance and flavour.",[Reference: PoP (package of practices)]
Cereals,Maize,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME MAIZE VARIETIES FEATURE OF PARBHAT (1987)?,"This composite has medium thick stem which resists lodging. Plant and ear height is medium tall. Husk covers are well developed. Ears are medium long and thick. The grains are medium bold, yellow-orange and semi-flint to flint.",[Reference: PoP (package of practices)]
Cereals,Maize,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME MAIZE VARIETIES FEATURE OF PMH 1 (2005)?,"This single cross hybrid has tall plants with well developed root system. The stem is zig-zag, sturdy and purple colored. The leaves are medium broad. Tassel is open and medium in size. Ears are medium long with yellow orange flint grains.",[Reference: PoP (package of practices)]
Cereals,Maize,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME MAIZE VARIETIES FEATURE OF JC 12 (2020)?,"The plants of this composite variety are medium tall in height with medium ear placement. It has medium thick stem which resists lodging and has heavy open tassel. Ears are medium long with good girth. This composite has semi-flint, yellow- orange grains.",[Reference: PoP (package of practices)]
Cereals,Maize,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME MAIZE VARIETIES FEATURE OF PMH 13 (2021)?,This single cross hybrid has tall plants with medium high ear placement. Leaves are dark green and broad. Tassel is medium and open. Ears are conico-cylindrical and long with light orange flint grains.,[Reference: PoP (package of practices)]
Cereals,Maize,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME MAIZE VARIETIES FEATURE OF PANCHGANGA (RABI)?,Features are- It is early maturing composite. It has white semi flint grains.,[Reference: PoP (package of practices)]
Cereals,Oats,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME Oats?,"Oats is an important Cereal crop as well as fodder crop. Cultivation of Oat is similar as wheat crop. It is mainly grown in Temperate and Subtropical climates. It can also thrive well in high-altitude tropics. They are very popular due to their health benefits. Oat meal is very famous food.Oats is rich in proteins and fiber. They also help in weight loss, controlling blood pressure and for building strong immune system.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Cereals,Oats,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOWING TIME OF Oats CROP?,Second week of October to last week of October is optimum time for sowing seeds.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Cereals,Oats,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SUITABLE TEMPARARTURE OF Oats CROPS?,"The suitable temparature: Sowing Temparature- 20-25 degree, 
Normal Temperature- 20-30 degree,Harvesting Temperature- 25-30 degree, Rainfall- 80-100mm
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Cereals,Oats,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOWING TEMPARARTURE OF Oats CROPS?,Sowing Temparature- 20-25 degree,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Cereals,Oats,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME NORMAL TEMPARARTURE OF Oats CROPS?,Normal Temperature- 20-30 degree,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Cereals,Oats,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME HARVESTING TEMPARARTURE OF Oats CROPS?,Harvesting Temperature- 25-30 degree,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Cereals,Oats,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME RAINFALL OF Oats CROPS?,Rainfall- 80-100mm,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Cereals,Oats,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SUITABLE TIME OF Oats CROP?,Second week of October to last week of October is optimum time for sowing seeds.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Cereals,Oats,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOIL MANAGEMENT OF Oats CROP?,It can be cultivated on all kinds of soil. Well drained loamy soil rich in organic matter is suitable for cultivation. pH range of 5 - 6.6 is optimum forOats.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Cereals,Oats,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FIELD PREPARATION OF Oats CROP?,Land should be properly prepared to form a weed free field. Ploughing should be done 6-8 times to gain higher yields. Oat crop can tolerate higher pH levels than barley and wheat. Propagation inOats is done through seeds.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Cereals,Oats,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SPACING OF Oats CROP?,Spacing:Spacing of 25-30 cm should be kept between rows.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Cereals,Oats,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SOWING DEPTH OF Oats CROP?,Sowing Depth:Depth should be 3-4 cm.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Cereals,Oats,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME HARVESTING OF Oats CROP?,"Oats are fully mature and ready to harvest after 4-5 months of sowing. To avoid grain shedding, Crop should be harvested in early April month.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Cereals,Oats,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME METHOD OF SOWING OF Oats CROP?,"Method of sowing:Sowing is done through drilling method, zero tillage drill.


","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Cereals,Oats,Water Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WATER MANAGEMENT OF Oats CROP?,"Oats are mainly cultivated as rain-fed crop. But if they are grown as irrigated crop, two irrigations should be given at 25-28 days interval from sowing.


","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Cereals,Oats,Weed Management,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WEED MANAGEMENT OF Oats CROP?,Weed management is not necessary in case if plants become successful to make a good crop stand. Weeds are less likely to occur inOats. 1-2 hoeing can be given as intercultural operations.,"[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Cereals,Oats,Fertilizer Uses,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME BETTER/GOOD/FERTILIZER USES OF Oats CROP?,"FYM should be added at the time of land preparation. Apply 30 kg of Nitrogen in form of (Urea 66 kg) and 8 kg of Phosphorus (in form of SSP@50 kg) per acre. Apply half dose of nitrogen and full dose of Phosphorus at the time of sowing. Apply remaining amount of Nitrogen, 30-40 days after sowing.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Cereals,Oats,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME Oats IMPROVED VARIETIES?,"Weston-11: It has been released in 1978 for cultivation in Punjab. Plants have height of about 150 cm. Grains are long and amber in color.

Kent: It is suitable for growing in all areas of India. Average plant height is 75-80 cm. This variety is resistant to rust, lodging and blight. It gives fodder yield of 210 qtl/acre.

OL-10: Suitable for cultivation in all irrigated areas of Punjab. Seeds are of medium size. Gives average fodder yield of 270 qtl/acre.

OL-9: Suitable for cultivation in all irrigated areas of Punjab. Seeds are of medium size. Gives average seed yield of 7 qtl/acre and fodder yield of 230 qtl/acre.

OL 11: Released in 2017. It gives an average yield of 245qtl/acre. The plants are leafy, long and wide leaf. 

Other States Varieties

Brunker-10: It is a quick growing variety having fine, narrow, smooth leaves. It is resistant against drought. It can be cultivated in areas of Punjab, Delhi, Haryana and Uttar Pradesh.

HFO-114: It is suitable for cultivating in all oat growing areas. It was released in 1974 by HAU, Hisar. This variety is tall and it is resistant to lodging. It has bold seeds and has an average yield of 7-8 qtl/acre of seed.

Algerian: This variety is suitable for irrigated areas. Average plant height is 100-120 cm. It has slow early growth and light green color leaves.

OS-6: Suitable for cultivation in all areas of India. Gives average green fodder yield of 210 qtl/acre.

Bundel Jai 851: Suitable for cultivation in all areas of India. It gives average green fodder yield of 188 qtl/acre.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Cereals,Oats,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME Oats VARIETIEY  WESTON-11?,"Weston-11: It has been released in 1978 for cultivation in Punjab. Plants have height of about 150 cm. Grains are long and amber in color.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Cereals,Oats,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME Oats VARIETIEY  KENT?,"Kent: It is suitable for growing in all areas of India. Average plant height is 75-80 cm. This variety is resistant to rust, lodging and blight. It gives fodder yield of 210 qtl/acre.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research, Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare]"
Cereals,Oats,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME Oats VARIETIEY  OL-10?,"OL-10: Suitable for cultivation in all irrigated areas of Punjab. Seeds are of medium size. Gives average fodder yield of 270 qtl/acre.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
