Cereals,Wheat,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WHEAT VARIETIEY  KALYANSONA?,"Kalyansona: A double dwarf wheat with wide adaptation recommended for cultivation all over India. This variety is very vulnerable to rust. It is, therefore, advisable to grow it only in rust free regions. It gives average yield of 12.4 quintals per acre.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, Punjab Agricultural University Ludhiana, Department of Agriculture, Indian Agricultural Research Institute New Delhi,
