Schemes,Machinery/Equipment Subsidy,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME POWER TILLER SCHEMESINFORMATION?,"In case of the SC, ST, Small & Marginal Farmers, Women and NE States` beneficiaries, the maximum permissible schemes per machine/equipment is Rs. 50,000 and the Pattern Assistance is 50 percent for the Power Tiller (below 8 BHP) and Rs. 75,000 for the 8BHP & above).",[Reference:https://krishijagran.com/farm-mechanization/how-to-get-schemes-on-power-tillers/]
Schemes,Machinery/Equipment Subsidy,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME TRACTOR  SCHEME DETAILS?,"Under the scheme, eligible farmers are provided 20 to 50 % schemes for purchase of a new tractor for farming. Scheme is implemented by the state authorities. schemes provided by the government is directly transferred to the bank account of the applicant. Applications can be submitted either in online or offline mode.",[Reference:https://nvshq.org/scheme/pm-kisan-tractor-scheme/]
Schemes,Machinery/Equipment Subsidy,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME TRACTOR SCHEMES ?,"A tractor is a crucial part of farming but all farmers cannot afford it due to its high cost. In such a situation, they have to rent a tractor, and this increases the cost. Considering this situation, the Government launched Tractor scheme under which eligible farmers are provided schemes to buy Tractors. The scheme is being already implemented in several states of the country at their own level such as Maharashtra, Madhya Pradesh, Assam, Bihar etc.",[Reference:https://nvshq.org/scheme/pm-kisan-tractor-scheme/]
Schemes,Machinery/Equipment Subsidy,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME TRACTOR SCHEMES REQUIRED DOCUMENT?,"1.Applicant Aadhar Card
2.Valid Id card- (like Voter id, PAN card, Passport, Driving license)
3.Legal documents of land possessed by the applicant
4.Bank Account Details/ Bank Passbook
5.Category certificate, as applicable
6.Capacity 
7.Passport sized Photograph of the applicant",[Reference:https://nvshq.org/scheme/pm-kisan-tractor-scheme/]
Schemes,Machinery/Equipment Subsidy,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME TRACTOR SCHEMES ELIGIBILITY?,"Nationality:
The primary criterion is that the applicant must be a permanent citizen of India.
Age Criteria:
One who is applying for this scheme should be of minimum age of 18 years and less than 60 years.
Any relaxation in age depends upon the state government decision.
Family Income:
Family income is also an important factor that cannot be neglected when we talk about eligibility conditions. The annual family income of candidates under this scheme should be less than 1.5 lakhs.
Other Criteria:
Farmer buys only one tractor under this scheme.
Applicants should not be already a beneficiary under similar kind of schemes scheme.
Applicants who have applied for the scheme must have agricultural land under his/her possession.
Applicant should fall under small or marginal farmer category.
Applicants ensure that they have not purchased any tractor in last 7 years.
Applications of such farmers will be considered who will satisfy all the aforementioned conditions. The verification of eligibility will be done through the verification of documents and certificates submitted by the candidates.",[Reference:https://nvshq.org/scheme/pm-kisan-tractor-scheme/]
Schemes,Machinery/Equipment Subsidy,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FROM WHERE CAN I DOWNLOAD CHC FARM MACHINERY MOBILE APP?,The App can be downloaded from Google play store by searching FARMS or FARMS Farm Machinery Solutions It is supported on devices with Android version 4.0 and above.,[Reference:https://agrimachinery.nic.in/Files/FAQ_CHC_MobAPP.pdf]
Schemes,Machinery/Equipment Subsidy,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME HOW OFTEN DO I NEED TO COMPLETE AN EXEMPTION CERTIFICATE?,Purchases of machinery and equipment require an exemption certificate for every individual purchase. Multiple purchases of the same agricultural supplies not typically used in agriculture or the same fertilizer and pesticides may use the same certificate by marking the appropriate checkbox.,[Reference:https://tax.vermont.gov/business-and-corp/sales-and-use-tax/exemptions/agricultural-equipment]
Schemes,Machinery/Equipment Subsidy,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WHAT ABOUT PARTS FOR MY MACHINERY OR EQUIPMENT?,"Parts purchased for exempt machinery or equipment are also exempt from sales tax. If you anticipate buying parts from the same dealer where you bought your equipment, you should select the checkbox indicating that on page 1 of the S-3A. Note: Parts does not mean implements. If it is a large implement for your machinery or equipment, you will need a new exemption certificate.

",[Reference:https://tax.vermont.gov/business-and-corp/sales-and-use-tax/exemptions/agricultural-equipment]
Schemes,Machinery/Equipment Subsidy,Government Schemes,"INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME  FOR MACHINERY AND EQUIPMENT, IT MUST BE USED 75% OF THE TIME IT IS IN USE FOR EXEMPT USES. WHAT IS AN EXEMPT USE?","Uses that qualify machinery or equipment for the exemption are those where it is used to produce tangible personal property for sale. In other words, the work on a farm or other agricultural or horticultural operation that is directly involved in producing the final product that will be sold. Common exempt uses include:

1.Machinery and equipment used to feed and water livestock and to administer medication to livestock
2.Machinery and equipment used to maintain sanitary conditions or health conditions in the immediate area of agricultural production
3.Machinery and equipment used to test and inspect the agricultural product during the actual farm production cycle
4.Machinery and equipment used in agriculture to handle and preserve agricultural products upon the premises, and to prevent or deter the destruction, injury, or spoilage of agricultural products, livestock, or plants
Cleaning, transportation, land clearing, or building repair are not exempt uses of equipment. Remember: now that the law has changed, machinery and equipment can be used up to 25% of the time for the non-exempt uses.",[Reference:https://tax.vermont.gov/business-and-corp/sales-and-use-tax/exemptions/agricultural-equipment]
Schemes,Machinery/Equipment Subsidy,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME THERE IS NOTHING ON HERE ABOUT FUELS IS NOT THAT EXEMPT IF USED FOR FARM PURPOSES?,"Electricity and fuel used directly and exclusively for farm purposes are not taxable. In most cases, no exemption certificate is required. Some supplies may require that Form S-3F is completed if the use is not obvious or if only a portion of the fuel purchased is exempt.

",[Reference:https://tax.vermont.gov/business-and-corp/sales-and-use-tax/exemptions/agricultural-equipment]
Schemes,Machinery/Equipment Subsidy,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME HOW OFTEN DO I NEED A NEW FORM?,"If you are using your Form S-3A for multiple purchases of supplies or fertilizer/pesticides, you should still renew it every 3 years. This ensures the most updated information about you as a purchaser is available to your seller, and it helps to ensure compliance with the exemption.",[Reference:https://tax.vermont.gov/business-and-corp/sales-and-use-tax/exemptions/agricultural-equipment]
Schemes,PM Kisan Credit card Yojna,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME PM KISAN CREDIT CARD YOJNA?,"The Pradhan Mantri Kisan Credit Card Yojana is the best scheme for Farmers who want financial support with a guarantee of Banks. All PM Kisan Yojana Beneficiary Farmers now can directly download the KCC Loan form and apply to banks. Either you can download the Kisan KCC Registration form from the official web portal www.pmkisan.gov.in or pmkisan.nic.in. Or else you can download it online or get it offline from public and private sector banks. Advantages of the KCC Scheme to the farmers:
**Simplifies disbursement procedures
**Removes rigidity regarding cash and kind
**No need to apply for a loan for every crop
**Assured availability of credit at any time enabling reduced interest burden for the farmer.
**Helps buy seeds, fertilizers at farmer's convenience and choice
**Helps buy on cash-avail discount from dealers
**Credit facility for 3 years no need for seasonal appraisal
**Maximum credit limit based on agriculture income
**Any number of withdrawals subject to credit limit
**Repayment only after harvest
**Rate of interest as applicable to agriculture advance
**Security, margin and documentation norms as applicable to agricultural advance
**Access to adequate and timely credit to farmers
**Full year's credit requirement of the borrower taken care of. Minimum paper work and simplification of documentation for withdraw of funds from the bank.
**Flexibility to draw cash and buy inputs.
**Assured availability of credit at any time enabling reduced interest burden for the farmer. Flexibility of drawals from a branch other than the issuing branch at the discretion of the bank.
","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, vikaspedia.in/agriculture/agri-credit/revised-kisan-credit-card-scheme]"
Schemes,PM Kisan Credit card Yojna,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME PM KISAN CREDIT CARD LOAN PROVIDER BANK?,"These are some of the public sector banks lists which provides KCC Loan:
1.Cooperative Banks
2.National Bank for Agriculture and Rural Development (NABARD)
3.State Bank of India (SBI)
4.National Payments Corporation of India (NPCI)
5.Industrial Development Bank of India (IDBI)
Here are some private sector bank lists and names which are as follows to get PM Kisan Credit Card Yojana 2021 Loan Form. You can get the form from these banks too.
1.HDFC Bank
2.PNB
3.ICICI Bank
4.Axis Bank
5.Indian Overseas Bank
6.Bank Of India
7.Odisha Gramya Bank",[Reference: www.apnikheti.com]
Schemes,PM Kisan Credit card Yojna,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME PM KISAN CREDIT CARD FORM DOWNLOAD ONLINE?,"If you want to download KCC Form 2021 Online then you need to follow the below steps:
1.You need to open the website https://pmkisan.gov.in/.
2.Go to the farmers corner.
3.Move to the tab of Download Kisan Credit Card.
4.You will get the option of download their the form.
5.Download it and save.",[Reference: www.apnikheti.com]
Schemes,PM Kisan Credit card Yojna,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME PM KISAN CREDIT CARD DOCUMENT LIST?,"KCC Loan Documents List:
The Kisan Credit Card Loan Yojana Benefits will get only eligible Farm, However, you need to the checklist of documents required to fill out an application for of pmkisan.gov.in KCC Form 2021 below.

The farmer must have owner of cultivable land.
Tenant farmers, Oral lessees and Share Croppers farmers can apply.
1.Aadhaar card
2.Resident Proof
3.Land Documents
4.PAN Card
5.Valid Mobile Number
6.Passport Size Photo
**The KCC Loan limit will be up to Rs. 1.60 lakh and you can Tie up Rs 3 lakhs. However, these limits vary from bank to bank.",[Reference: www.apnikheti.com]
Schemes,PM Kisan Credit card Yojna,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME PM KISAN CREDIT CARD LIMIT?,"The KCC Loan limit will be up to Rs. 1.60 lakh and you can Tie up Rs 3 lakhs. However, these limits vary from bank to bank.",[Reference: www.apnikheti.com]
Schemes,PM Kisan Credit card Yojna,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME PM KISAN CREDIT CARD ELIGIBILITY?,"Eligibility:
1.All farmers-individuals/Joint borrowers who are owner cultivators.
2.Tenant farmers, Oral lessees and Share Croppers etc.
3.SHGs or Joint Liability Groups of farmers including tenant farmers, share croppers etc.,
 **The criteria for eligible beneficiaries under KCC for Animal Husbandry and Fisheries is as follows
Fishery:
1.Inland Fisheries and Aquaculture - Fishers, Fish Farmers (individual & groups/ partners/ share croppers/ tenant farmers), Self Help Groups, Joint Liability Groups and women groups. The beneficiaries must own or lease any of the fisheries related activities such as pond, tank, open water bodies, raceway, hatchery, rearing unit, possess necessary license for fish farming and fishing related activities, and any other State specific fisheries and allied activities.
2.Marine Fisheries - Beneficiaries listed above, who own or lease registered fishing vessel/boat, possess necessary fishing license/permission for fishing in estuary and sea, fish farming/mariculture activities in estuaries and open sea and any other State specific fisheries and allied activities.
3.Poultry and small ruminant - Farmers, poultry farmers either individual or joint borrower, Joint Liability Groups or Self Help Groups including tenant farmer of sheep/goats/pigs/poultry/ birds /rabbit and having owned/rented/leased sheds.
4.Dairy - Farmers and Dairy farmers either individual or joint borrower, Joint Liability Groups or Self Help Groups including tenant farmers having owned /rented/leased sheds.
",[Reference: vikaspedia.in/agriculture/agri-credit/revised-kisan-credit-card-scheme]
Schemes,PM Kisan Credit card Yojna,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME PM KISAN CREDIT CARD LOAN FOR SINGLE CROP?,"For farmers raising single crop in a year:
**Short term credit limit is fixed for the first year depending upon
1.the crops cultivated as per proposed cropping pattern & scale of finance
2.post-harvest/ household / consumption requirements
3.Maintenance expenses of farm assets, crop insurance, Personal Accident Insurance Scheme (PAIS) and Asset insurance.
4.Scale of finance for the crop (as decided by District Level Technical Committee) x Extent of area cultivated + 10% of limit towards post-harvest / household / consumption requirements + 20% of limit towards repairs and maintenance expenses of farm assets + crop insurance, PAIS & asset insurance.
**For every successive years (2nd, 3rd, 4th, and 5th year), the limit will be stepped up @10%.",[Reference: vikaspedia.in/agriculture/agri-credit/revised-kisan-credit-card-scheme]
Schemes,PM Kisan Credit card Yojna,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME PM KISAN CREDIT CARD LOAN FOR MORE THAN ONE CROP?,"For farmers raising more than one crop in a year, the limit is to be fixed as above depending upon the crops cultivated as per proposed cropping pattern for the first year and an additional 10% of the limit towards cost escalation / increase in scale of finance for every successive year (2nd, 3rd, 4th and 5th year). It is assumed that the farmer adopts the same cropping pattern for the remaining four years also. In case the cropping pattern adopted by the farmer is changed in the subsequent year, the limit may be reworked.",[Reference:vikaspedia.in/agriculture/agri-credit/revised-kisan-credit-card-scheme]
Schemes,PM Kisan Credit card Yojna,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME PM KISAN CREDIT CARD  TEAM LOAN?,"Term loans for investments towards land development, minor irrigation, purchase of farm equipments and allied agricultural activities. The banks may fix the quantum of credit for term and working capital limit for agricultural and allied activities, etc., based on the unit cost of the asset/s proposed to be acquired by the farmer, the allied activities already being undertaken on the farm, the bank judgment on repayment capacity vis-a-vis total loan burden devolving on the farmer, including existing loan obligations.

The long term loan limit is based on the proposed investments during the five year period and the bank perception on the repaying capacity of the farmer.",[Reference:vikaspedia.in/agriculture/agri-credit/revised-kisan-credit-card-scheme]
Schemes,PM Kisan Credit card Yojna,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME PM KISAN CREDIT CARD MAXIMUM PERMISSIBLE LIMIT?,Maximum Permissible Limit: The short term loan limit arrived for the 5th year plus the estimated long term loan requirement will be the Maximum Permissible Limit (MPL) and treated as the Kisan Credit Card Limit.,[Reference:vikaspedia.in/agriculture/agri-credit/revised-kisan-credit-card-scheme]
Schemes,PM Kisan Credit card Yojna,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME PM KISAN CREDIT CARD LOAN FOR MARGINAL FARMERS?,"For Marginal Farmers:
A flexible limit of Rs.10,000 to Rs.50,000 be provided (as Flexi KCC) based on the land holding and crops grown including post harvest warehouse storage related credit needs and other farm expenses, consumption needs, etc., plus small term loan investments like purchase of farm equipments, establishing mini dairy/backyard poultry as per assessment of Branch Manager without relating it to the value of land. The composite KCC limit is to be fixed for a period of five years on this basis. Wherever higher limit is required due to change in cropping pattern and/or scale of finance, the limit may be arrived at as per the estimation.",[Reference:vikaspedia.in/agriculture/agri-credit/revised-kisan-credit-card-scheme]
Schemes,PM Kisan Credit card Yojna,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME PM KISAN CREDIT CARD LOAN FOR ANIMAL HUSBANDRY AND FISHERIES?,"For Animal Husbandry and Fisheries:

*The scale of finance will be fixed by the District Level Technical Committee (DLTC) based on local cost worked out on the basis of per acre/per unit/per animal/per bird etc.

*The working capital components in fisheries, under the scale of finance, may include recurring cost towards seed, feed, organic and inorganic fertilisers, lime/other soil conditioners, harvesting and marketing charges, fuel/electricity charges, labour, lease rent (if leased water area) etc. For capture fisheries, working capital may include the cost of fuel, ice, labouring charges, mooring/landing charges etc. may form part of the scale of finance.

*The working capital components in Animal Husbandry, under the scale of finance, may include recurring cost towards feeding, veterinary aid, labour, water and electricity supply.

",[Reference:vikaspedia.in/agriculture/agri-credit/revised-kisan-credit-card-scheme]
Schemes,PM Kisan Credit card Yojna,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME PM KISAN CREDIT CARD REPAYMENT PERIOD?,"Repayment Period:
1.The repayment period for short terms loans may be fixed by banks as per the anticipated harvesting and marketing period for the crops for which a loan has been granted.
2.The term loan component will be normally repayable within a period of 5 years depending on the type of activity / investment as per the existing guidelines applicable for investment credit.
3.Financing banks at their discretion may provide longer repayment period for term loan depending on the type of investment.
",[Reference: vikaspedia.in/agriculture/agri-credit/revised-kisan-credit-card-scheme]
Schemes,PM Kisan Credit card Yojna,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME PM KISAN CREDIT CARD SALIENT FEATURES SCHEME?,"1.Eligible farmers to be provided with a Kisan Credit Card and a pass book or card-cum-pass book.
2.Revolving cash credit facility involving any number of drawals and repayments within the limit.
3.Limit to be fixed on the basis of operational land holding, cropping pattern and scale of finance.
4.Entire production credit needs for full year plus ancillary activities related to crop production to be considered while fixing limit.
5.Sub-limits to cover short term, medium term as well as term credit are fixed at the discretion of banks.
6.Card valid for 5 years subject to annual review. As incentive for good performance, credit limits could be enhanced to take care of increase in costs, change in cropping pattern, etc.
7.Conversion/reschedulement of loans also permissible in case of damage to crops due to natural calamities.
8.Security, margin, rate of interest, etc. as per RBI norms.
9.Operations may be through issuing branch (and also PACS in the case of Cooperative Banks) through other designated branches at the discretion of bank.
10.Withdrawals through slips/cheques accompanied by card and passbook.
11.Crop loans disbursed under KCC Scheme for notified crops are covered under Crop Insurance Scheme, to protect the interest of the farmer against loss of crop yield caused by natural calamities, pest attacks etc
",[Reference:vikaspedia.in/agriculture/agri-credit/revised-kisan-credit-card-scheme]
Schemes,PM Kisan Credit card Yojna,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME PM KISAN CREDIT CARD PERSONAL ACCIDENT INSURANCE SCHEME?,"Scheme covers risk of KCC holders against death or permanent disability resulting from accidents caused by external, violent and visible means, as under: Death due to accident (within 12 months of the accident) caused by outward, violent and visible means -- Rs.50,000/- Permanent total disability -- Rs.50,000/- Loss of two limbs or two eyes or one limb and one eye -- Rs.50,000/- Loss of one limb or one eye -- Rs.25,000/-

1.Nominated office of insurance company to issue a Master Insurance Policy to each DCCB/RRB covering all its KCC holders.
2.Premium payable Rs.15/- for a one year policy while Rs.45/- for a 3-year policy.
3.Designated insurance company will nominate one office at district level to function as nodal office for co-ordinating implementation of personal accident insurance scheme for KCC holders in the district.
4.Insurance coverage available under Policy only from date of receipt of premium at insurance company
5.Banks to ensure to incorporate name of Nominee in Kisan Credit Card-cum-Pass Book.
6.Simplified claim settlement procedure evolved under Scheme whereby an Enquiry-cum-Verification Committee comprising Branch Manager of implementing bank, Lead Bank Officer and representative of insurance company to certify nature of accident causing disability/death and recommend settlement of insurance claims.
",[Reference:vikaspedia.in/agriculture/agri-credit/revised-kisan-credit-card-scheme]
Schemes,PM Kisan Credit card Yojna,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME RUPAY KISAN CREDIT CARDS?,"RuPay is an Indian domestic card scheme conceived and launched by the National Payments Corporation of India (NPCI). It was created to fulfill the Reserve Bank of India desire to have a domestic, open loop, and multilateral system of payments in India. RuPay facilitates electronic payment at all Indian banks and financial institutions, and competes with MasterCard and Visa in India.

NABARD, in January, 2013 set up Special Project Unit- Kisan Credit Card (SPU-KCC) with a mandate for encouraging cooperative banks and Regional Rural Banks across the country to issue Rupay KCC debit cards. The overarching goal is to develop cash-less eco system by enabling the farming community to avail all new banking facilities at par with urban area of the country",[Reference:vikaspedia.in/agriculture/agri-credit/revised-kisan-credit-card-scheme]
Schemes,PM Kisan Credit card Yojna,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME  KISAN CREDIT CARDS BENEFIT/ADVANTAGE?,"Advantages of the KCC Scheme to the farmers:
**Simplifies disbursement procedures
**Removes rigidity regarding cash and kind
**No need to apply for a loan for every crop
**Assured availability of credit at any time enabling reduced interest burden for the farmer.
**Helps buy seeds, fertilizers at farmer's convenience and choice
**Helps buy on cash-avail discount from dealers
**Credit facility for 3 years no need for seasonal appraisal
**Maximum credit limit based on agriculture income
**Any number of withdrawals subject to credit limit
**Repayment only after harvest
**Rate of interest as applicable to agriculture advance
**Security, margin and documentation norms as applicable to agricultural advance
**Access to adequate and timely credit to farmers
**Full year's credit requirement of the borrower taken care of. Minimum paper work and simplification of documentation for withdraw of funds from the bank.
**Flexibility to draw cash and buy inputs.
**Assured availability of credit at any time enabling reduced interest burden for the farmer. Flexibility of drawals from a branch other than the issuing branch at the discretion of the bank.",[Reference:vikaspedia.in/agriculture/agri-credit/revised-kisan-credit-card-scheme]
Schemes,PM Kisan Credit card Yojna,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME  KISAN CREDIT CARDS TOLL FREE NUMBER?,A countrywide common eleven digit Toll Free number 1800-180-1551 or 1551 has been allotted for Kisan Call Centres.,[Reference:agricoop.nic.in/sites/default/files/Kisan%20Call%20Center%20%28KCC%29.pdf]
Schemes,PM Kisan Credit card Yojna,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME HOW TO APPLY PM KISAN CREDIT CARD?,"The application process for the Kisan credit card can be done online, as well as, offline.

->Online
1.Visit the website of the bank you wish to apply for the kisan credit card scheme.
2.From the list of options, choose the Kisan Credit Card.
3.On clicking the option of apply the website will redirect you to the application page.
4.Fill the form with the required details and click on submit.
5.On doing so, an application reference number will be sent.
6.If you are eligible, the bank will get back to you for the further process within 3-4 working days.
->Offline
Offline applications can be done by visiting the branch of the bank of your choice or by downloading the application form from the website of the bank as well. The applicant can visit the branch and begin the application process with the help of the bank representative. Once the formalities are done, the bank loan officer can help with the loan amount for the farmer.",[Reference: https://www.bankbazaar.com/kisan-credit-card.html]
Schemes,PM Kisan Credit card Yojna,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME  KISAN CREDIT CARDS TOLL FREE NUMBER ALL OVER INDIA?,A countrywide common eleven digit Toll Free number 1800-180-1551 or 1551 has been allotted for Kisan Call Centres.,[Reference:agricoop.nic.in/sites/default/files/Kisan%20Call%20Center%20%28KCC%29.pdf]
Schemes,PM Kisan Credit card Yojna,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WHAT ARE THE SECURITY NORMS FOR FINANCING UNDER KISAN CREDIT CARD?,"For limits upto Rs.1.60 lakh & limts upto Rs.3 lakh (in case of tie up), security is the
hypothecation of crops. For limits above the specified norms, mortgage of land/ or
third party guarantee in addition to hypothecated crops / assets.",[Reference:https://www.unionbankofindia.co.in/pdf/faq-agri-products.pdf]
Schemes,PM Kisan Credit card Yojna,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WHAT ARE BENEFITS PROVIDED BY GOVT OF INDIA TO IMPROVE FINANCE UNDER KCC?,"The interest subvention @2% and prompt repayment incentive benefit @3% on KCC
loan (i.e. crop loan+ working capital loan for animal husbandry and fisheries) will
be available on an overall limit of Rs. 3 lakh per annum and subject to a maximum
limit of Rs. 2 lakh per farmer involved in activities only related to animal husbandry
and / or fisheries.",[Reference:https://www.unionbankofindia.co.in/pdf/faq-agri-products.pdf]
Schemes,PM Kisan Credit card Yojna,Government Schemes,"INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WHAT IS THE MARGIN FOR FINANCING UNDER THE SCHEME
?","No specific margin is necessary for finance to production credit. For investment credit, margin varies with the purpose of investment. However no margin is required for loan upto Rs.1.60 lakh.
",[Reference:https://www.unionbankofindia.co.in/pdf/faq-agri-products.pdf]
Schemes,PM Kisan Credit card Yojna,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WHAT IS THE REPAYMENT PERIOD ALLOWED UNDER PM KISAN CREDIT CARD YOJNA SCHEME?,"The repayment period may be fixed by banks as per the anticipated harvesting and marketing period for the crops for which the loan has been granted. Repayment period for term loan is decided based on the type of investment.The loan in case of fisheries & animal husbandry, will be in the nature of a revolvingcash credit limit. Repayment will be fixed as per the cash flow/income generation pattern of the activity undertaken by the borrower.",[Reference:https://www.unionbankofindia.co.in/pdf/faq-agri-products.pdf]
Schemes,PM Kisan Credit card Yojna,Government Schemes,"INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WHAT IS THE VALIDITY PERIOD OF THE KISAN CREDIT CARD
?","The limit is valid for 5 years, subject to annual review.",[Reference:https://www.unionbankofindia.co.in/pdf/faq-agri-products.pdf]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Kisan Maan-Dhan Yojana,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME PRADHAN MANTRI KISAN MAAN-DHAN YOJANA SCHEME?,"Government has launched the Pradhan Mantri Kisan Maan DhanYojana (PM-KMY) on 12.9.2019 with a view to provide social security to Small and Marginal Farmers in their old age when they have no means of livelihood and minimal or no savings to take care of their expenses.


1.It is voluntary and contributory for farmers in the entry age group of 18 to 40 years and a monthly pension of Rs. 3000/- will be provided to them on attaining the age of 60 years.
2.The farmers will have to make a monthly contribution of Rs.55 to Rs.200, depending on their age of entry, in the Pension Fund till they reach the retirement date i.e. the age of 60 years.
3.The monthly contributions will fall due on the same day every month as enrolment date. The beneficiaries may also chose an option to pay their contributions on quarterly, 4-monthly or half-yearly basis. Such contributions will fall due on the same day of such period as the date of enrollment.
4.The spouse is also eligible to get a separate pension of Rs.3000/- upon making separate contributions to the Fund.
5.The Life Insurance Corporation of India (LIC) shall be the Pension Fund Manager and responsible for Pension pay out.
6.In case of death of the farmer before retirement date, the spouse may continue in the scheme by paying the remaining contributions till the remaining age of the deceased farmer. If the spouse does not wish to continue, the total contribution made by the farmer along with interest will be paid to the spouse. If there is no spouse, then total contribution along with interest will be paid to the nominee.
7.If the farmer dies after the retirement date, the spouse will receive 50% of the pension as Family Pension. After the death of both the farmer and the spouse, the accumulated corpus shall be credited back to the Pension Fund.
8.The beneficiaries may opt voluntarily to exit the Scheme after a minimum period of 5 years of regular contributions. On exit, their entire contribution shall be returned by LIC with an interest equivalent to prevailing saving bank rates.
9.The farmers, who are also beneficiaries of PM- Kisan Scheme, will have the option to allow their contribution debited from the benefit of that Scheme directly.
10.In case of default in making regular contributions, the beneficiaries are allowed to regularize the contributions by paying the outstanding dues along with prescribed interest. Until 1 month from first unpaid contribution, no late fee would be charged. Three payment cycles demand would be raised for payment of contribution without any interest.","[Reference: www.apnikheti.com, vikaspedia.in]"
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Kisan Maan-Dhan Yojana,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME ELIGIBILITY OF PRADHAN MANTRI KISAN MAAN-DHAN YOJANA SCHEME?,"Eligibility:
1.Small and Marginal Farmer (SMF) - a farmer who owns cultivable land upto 2 hectare as per land records of the concerned State/UT.
2.Age of 18- 40 years.",[Reference:https://vikaspedia.in/schemesall/schemes-for-farmers/pm-kisan-maan-dhan-yojana]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Kisan Maan-Dhan Yojana,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FUNDING DETAILS OF PRADHAN MANTRI KISAN MAAN-DHAN YOJANA SCHEME?,"Funding:
1.The scheme is supported by the Central Government.
2.The funding pattern is 90% by the Central Government and 10% by the State Government.
3.The 10% state share shall consist of cash contribution of the State, beneficiary contribution or the contribution of other non-governmental organizations.",[Reference: www.apnikheti.com]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Kisan Maan-Dhan Yojana,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME PRADHAN MANTRI KISAN MAAN-DHAN YOJANA SCHEME FUND ALLOCATION?,"Allocation of funds:
1.The entire X Plan outlay (Rs.226.07 crores) for the scheme shall be utilized for activities to be implemented by States/ districts.
2.The decision on use of funds will be taken at 3 levels namely Centre, State and District.
3.An amount of Rs. 167.56 crores amounting to 77.53% has been allocated for district level programmes.
4.An amount of Rs. 22.15 crores amounting to 10.25% has been allocated for State level programmes.
5.An amount of Rs. 26.41 crores amounting to 12.22% shall be available under the control of the Government of India.
6.This amount shall be utilized for innovative activities to be approved by the Government of India.
7.However, implementation of these activities will be done by States/districts.",[Reference: www.apnikheti.com]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Kisan Maan-Dhan Yojana,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME PRADHAN MANTRI KISAN MAAN-DHAN YOJANA SCHEME BENEFITS?,"Under this scheme, a minimum fixed pension of Rs.3,000/- is provided to the small and marginal farmers, subject to certain exclusion criteria, on attaining the age of 60 years. It is a voluntary and contributory pension scheme. The eligible farmer is required to contribute to a Pension Fund between Rs.55 to Rs.200 per month depending on the entry age. The Central Government also contributes in equal amount to the Pension Fund.

",[Reference:https://vikaspedia.in/schemesall/schemes-for-farmers/pm-kisan-maan-dhan-yojana]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Kisan Maan-Dhan Yojana,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME HOW TO APPLY PRADHAN MANTRI KISAN MAAN-DHAN YOJANA SCHEME?,"Step 1: Interested SMFs willing to join the scheme are requested to visit their nearest Common Service Centre (CSC).

Step 2: They are required to submit the following prerequisites for the enrolment process:

***Aadhaar Card
***Savings Bank Account Number along with IFSC Code (Bank Passbook or Cheque Leaf /Passbook or copy of bank statement as evidence of bank account).
Step 3: Pay the initial contribution amount in cash to the Village Level Entrepreneur (VLE).

Step 4: The VLE will key-in the Aadhaar number, name of the subscriber and his date of birth, as printed on the Aadhaar card for authentication.

Step 5: The VLE will require details like bank account details, mobile number, email address, spouse (if any) and nominee details to complete the online registration by filling up the form online.

Step 6: System will automatically calculate the monthly contribution payable according to the age of the applicant.

Step 7: Subscriber is required to pay the 1st subscription amount in cash to the VLE.

Step 8: System generates the Enrolment cum Auto Debit mandate form that is required to be signed by the subscriber. VLE will scan the same and upload it into the system.

Step 9: The subscriber is given a unique Kisan Pension Account Number (KPAN) and a Kisan Card will be printed with all the details.",[Reference:https://www.creditmantri.com/pradhan-mantri-kisan-maan-dhan-yojana/]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Kisan Maan-Dhan Yojana,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL MEWHAT IS THE DEFINITION OF SMALL & MARGINALIZED LANDHOLDER FARMER RELATING TO THIS SCHEME?,"A small and marginal landholder farmer is defined as a farmer who owns cultivable land up to 2 hectares, as per land record of the concerned State/UT.",[Reference:https://www.creditmantri.com/pradhan-mantri-kisan-maan-dhan-yojana/]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Kisan Maan-Dhan Yojana,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CAN I AVAIL BENEFIT UNDER THIS SCHEME IF I OWN MORE THAN 2 HECTARES OF LAND?,No. Any individual farmer owning more than 2 hectares of cultivable land shall not be eligible to get benefits under the scheme.,[Reference:https://www.creditmantri.com/pradhan-mantri-kisan-maan-dhan-yojana/]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Kisan Maan-Dhan Yojana,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL MEWHAT WILL HAPPEN IF THE APPLICANT HAS SUBMITTED INCORRECT INFORMATION TO GET BENEFITS UNDER THE SCHEME?,"If it is found out that the applicant declared incorrect information, the beneficiary shall be liable to get back his contributions without any interest thereon. The Central Government matching contribution will be stopped.",[Reference:https://www.creditmantri.com/pradhan-mantri-kisan-maan-dhan-yojana/]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Kisan Maan-Dhan Yojana,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL MECAN I APPLY FOR THIS SCHEME IF I DONT OWN ANY LAND?,No. Land holding is a primary criterion to be eligible to get the benefit under the scheme.,[Reference:https://www.creditmantri.com/pradhan-mantri-kisan-maan-dhan-yojana/]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Kisan Maan-Dhan Yojana,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL MEHOW WILL THE SUBSCRIBER CHANGE HIS BANK DETAILS OR ANY OTHER DETAILS WHICH ARE NOT CORRECT?,"A subscriber, who desires to change the bank details or any other details which are incorrect, will approach CSC(Common Services Center) or the Village Level Entrepreneur (VLE) present at the CSC, along with Pradhan Mantri Kisan Maan-dhan Yojana number and Aadhaar Card. However, the Date of Birth of the Subscriber cannot be changed at any time.The VLE at CSC will validate the credentials of the Member on the payment of the
Amount / Fee as prescribed by the Government from time to time",[Reference:https://static.pib.gov.in/WriteReadData/specificdocs/documents/2022/jan/doc20221185101.pdf]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Kisan Maan-Dhan Yojana,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL MEWHAT IS THE ALTERNATIVE MECHANISM FOR REGISTRATION OF ELIGIBLE BENEFICIARIES OTHER THAN ENROLMENT THROUGH CSC?,The eligible beneficiaries may alternatively also enroll themselves by physically contacting the State Nodal Officers (SNOs) or agencies designated by them in their respective districts.,[Reference:https://static.pib.gov.in/WriteReadData/specificdocs/documents/2022/jan/doc20221185101.pdf]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Kisan Maan-Dhan Yojana,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL MEWILL THE APPLICANT FARMERS / THEIR SPOUSES BE CHARGED ANY FEE FOR ENROLMENT UNDER THE SCHEME?,The enrolment at CSC Centres13 is free of cost and the applicant farmers / their spouses shall not have to pay any charge for the purpose.,[Reference:https://static.pib.gov.in/WriteReadData/specificdocs/documents/2022/jan/doc20221185101.pdf]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Kisan Maan-Dhan Yojana,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL MEWHEN WOULD CSC ISSUE A PENSION CARD TO THE SUBSCRIBER?,"Upon completion of enrollment process at Common Service Centres (CSC), an enrollment-cum-auto-debit-mandate a form will be generated for taking consent of those farmers who are also beneficiaries of PM-Kisan Scheme for auto-debiting their PM-Kisan benefits from their bank accounts and signed by the subscriber. In respect of those farmers who are not beneficiaries of PM-Kisan Scheme, the enrollment-cumauto-debit-mandate form will be generated for taking their consent for auto-debiting
their active bank accounts and signed by the subscriber.
The CSC Centres would scan the signed enrollment-cum-auto-debit mandate form and upload the same on the CSC system. Subsequent to this a pension card would be generated and given to the subscriber as proof of the pension account having been opened.",[Reference:https://static.pib.gov.in/WriteReadData/specificdocs/documents/2022/jan/doc20221185101.pdf]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Kisan Maan-Dhan Yojana,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL MEWHAT WILL BE THE DUE DATE FOR MONTHLY CONTRIBUTIONS?,"The monthly contributions will fall due on the same day every month as enrollment date. The beneficiaries may also choose an option to pay their contributions on quarterly, four-monthly or half-yearly basis. Such contributions will fall due on the same day of such period as the date of enrollment.",[Reference:https://static.pib.gov.in/WriteReadData/specificdocs/documents/2022/jan/doc20221185101.pdf]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Kisan Maan-Dhan Yojana,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL MEARE STATE/UT GOVERNMENTS PERMITTED TO SHARE THE BURDEN OF INDIVIDUAL SMF BENEFICIARY CONTRIBUTION?,Yes. The State / UT Governments will have the option of sharing the burden of individual SMF beneficiary contribution.,[Reference:https://static.pib.gov.in/WriteReadData/specificdocs/documents/2022/jan/doc20221185101.pdf]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Kisan Maan-Dhan Yojana,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL MEWHAT WOULD CONSTITUTE A PENSION FUND?,"The Central Government through the Department of Agriculture
, Cooperation and Farmers Welfare shall also contribute an equal amount as contributed by the eligible subscriber, to the Pension Fund account of such co-contributions shall be maintained separately by the LIC and these co-contributions along with fund earnings from time to time shall be utilized for pension payment on the date of vesting. Co-contributions
would not be paid to subscribers in case of pre-mature exits. In such a case, the cocontributions along with fund earnings will be transferred back to the Pension Fund.
",[Reference:https://static.pib.gov.in/WriteReadData/specificdocs/documents/2022/jan/doc20221185101.pdf]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Kisan Maan-Dhan Yojana,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL MECAN CONTRIBUTION TO THE SCHEME BE MADE FROM THE BENEFITS RECEIVED FROM PMKISAN SCHEME?,"Yes. The SMFs shall have the option to allow payment of his/her voluntary
contribution to the Scheme from the financial benefits received by them from the PMKISAN Scheme, directly.The eligible SMFs who are desirous of using their PM-Kisan benefit for contributing for Pradhan Mantri Kisan Maan-dhan Yojana, will have to sign and submit an enrollment-cum-auto debit mandate form for giving their consent for auto-debiting their bank accounts, in which their PM-Kisan benefits are credited, so that their
contributions are automatically paid.
",[Reference:https://static.pib.gov.in/WriteReadData/specificdocs/documents/2022/jan/doc20221185101.pdf]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Kisan Maan-Dhan Yojana,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL MEWHO WILL ACT AS PENSION FUND MANAGER FOR THE SCHEME?,Life Insurance Corporation of India (LIC) shall be the Pension Fund Manager and responsible for Pension Pay-Out.,[Reference:https://static.pib.gov.in/WriteReadData/specificdocs/documents/2022/jan/doc20221185101.pdf]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Kisan Maan-Dhan Yojana,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL MEWHAT KIND OF INFORMATION NEEDS TO BE PROVIDED BY THE BENEFICIARY AT THE TIME OF REGISTRATION?,"The beneficiary will provide following information at the time of registration
1.Farmer/ Spouse name and date of birth
2.Bank account number
3.IFSC/ MICR Code
4.Mobile Number
5. Aadhaar Number
6.Other customer information is available in the passbook which is required for mandatory registration.
",[Reference:https://static.pib.gov.in/WriteReadData/specificdocs/documents/2022/jan/doc20221185101.pdf]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana (PMFBY),Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME PRADHAN MANTRI FASAL BIMA YOJANA (PMFBY)?,"
Sowing of Kharif Crops has started with the arrival of the monsoon in the country. The government has issued a notification for Crop Insurance. The Agriculture Department has said that farmers should insure their crops for protection from natural disasters. The process of getting insurance for Kharif crops 2020 has started in most of the states.Farmers who have taken crop loans through Kisan Credit Card (KCC), their crop automatically comes under the purview of insurance. Other farmers can insure the crop as per their choice. Crop insurance or fasal bima can also be done at the Common Services Centers.It is important to mention that crop insurance is voluntary and it is completely farmers decision to insure his crop or not. Every year, due to flood, storms, hailstorms, heavy rains or drought, farmers' crops get destroyed. To protect crops from natural havoc, the Central Government has launched the Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana (PMFBY). The scheme was launched on 13 January 2016.Those farmers who want to insure their crop can register themselves on the official website of the Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana - https://pmfby.gov.in/. Farmers can also take advantage of this scheme by going to their nearest bank.Under PMFBY, farmers have to pay 2 percent premium for Kharif crop and 1.5 percent premium for Rabi crop. The scheme also provides insurance cover for commercial and horticultural crops. In this, however, farmers have to pay a 5 percent premium.",[Reference:https://krishijagran.com/agriculture-world/pmfby-how-farmers-can-apply-for-pradhan-mantri-fasal-bima-yojana-step-by-step-process-inside/]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana (PMFBY),Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME PRADHAN MANTRI FASAL BIMA YOJANA (PMFBY) COVERED IN FARMER?,"1.All farmers growing notified crops in a notified area during the season who have insurable interest in the crop are eligible.
2.Compulsory coverage: The enrolment under the scheme, subject to possession of insurable interest on the cultivation of the notified crop in the notified area, shall be compulsory for following categories of farmers.
3.Farmers in the notified area who possess a Crop Loan account/KCC account (called as Loanee Farmers) to whom credit limit is sanctioned/renewed for the notified crop during the crop season.",[Reference: www.apnikheti.com]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana (PMFBY),Government Schemes,"INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME, HOW TO ENROLL PRADHAN MANTRI FASAL BIMA YOJANA (PMFBY)?","Both Loanee and Non-Loanee farmers are to be enrolled in the National Crop Insurance Portal(NCIP) belong to Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers welfare, New Delhi. Banks who are lending Seasonal Crop Loans to the farmers are responsible to upload the data in the NCIPIn case of Non-loanee farmers, Intermediaries, Common Service Centers (CSCs), farmers on their own and other Agencies are to upload the data in the NCIP, along with the uploading 4 documents.Premium must be paid by way of NEFT only and DD or Cheques are not accepted. Similarly offline applications for enrollment are not accepted as every application needs to be filled-in online.",[Reference:nationalinsurance.nic.co.in/en/pradhan-mantri-fasal-bima-yojana-pmfby]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana (PMFBY),Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME COVERAGE OF CROPS IN PRADHAN MANTRI FASAL BIMA YOJANA (PMFBY)?,"Coverage of Crops:
1.Food crops (Cereals, Vegetables and Pulses),
2.Oilseeds
3.Annual Commercial / Annual Horticultural crops.
In addition for perennial crops, pilots for coverage can be taken for those perennial horticultural crops for which standard methodology for yield estimation is available.",[Reference:nationalinsurance.nic.co.in/en/pradhan-mantri-fasal-bima-yojana-pmfby]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana (PMFBY),Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME RISKS COVERED UNDER PRADHAN MANTRI FASAL BIMA YOJANA (PMFBY)?,"Risks covered under the scheme:
1.Yield Losses (standing crops, on notified area basis).
2.Comprehensive risk insurance is provided to cover yield losses due to non-preventable risks, such as Natural Fire and Lightning, Storm, Hailstorm, Cyclone, Typhoon, Tempest, Hurricane, Tornado. Risks due to Flood, Inundation and Landslide, Drought, Dry spells, Pests/ Diseases also will be covered.
3.In cases where majority of the insured farmers of a notified area, having intent to sow/plant and incurred expenditure for the purpose, are prevented from sowing/planting the insured crop due to adverse weather conditions, shall be eligible for indemnity claims upto a maximum of 25 per cent of the sum-insured.
4.In post-harvest losses, coverage will be available up to a maximum period of 14 days from harvesting for those crops which are kept in ut & spreadcondition to dry in the field.
5.For certain localized problems, Loss / damage resulting from occurrence of identified localized risks like hailstorm, landslide, and Inundation affecting isolated farms in the notified area would also be covered.",[Reference: www.apnikheti.com]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana (PMFBY),Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL MEHOW TO APPLY  PRADHAN MANTRI FASAL BIMA YOJANA (PMFBY)?,"Farmers who have taken loans from banks or co-operative societies can enrol through the same bank. And, farmers who have taken no loans can apply through banks, brokers, CSC e-Governance Services India Limited or directly through the website. To apply for online crop insurance under PMFBY, follow the given steps-

1.Visit PMFBY Website
2.Click on farmer Corner 
3.If you are already registered, you can proceed to get enrolled under the scheme. However, new farmers will have to register themselves by filling the registration form.",[Reference:https://www.paisabazaar.com/saving-schemes/pradhan-mantri-fasal-bima-yojana-pmfby/]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana (PMFBY),Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME PRADHAN MANTRI FASAL BIMA YOJANA (PMFBY) REQUIRED DOCUMENTS?,"Here is a rundown of all the documents required for the Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana:

1.Passport size photograph of the farmer
2.Identity proof of the farmer (Aadhar card, PAN card, Voter ID, Driving license, or Passport)
3.Address proof of the farmer (Aadhar card, Voter ID, Driving license, or Passport)
4.If the field is owned by the farmer, the Khasra paper and account number need to be kept together
5.In case the crop is only sown in the field, evidence for the same need to be presented
6.As evidence, the farmers should get a letter written from people such as Pradhan, Sarpanch, Goan Pradhan, Patwari, etc.",[Reference:https://www.bajajallianz.com/blog/announcements/quick-overview-on-pmfby-crop-insurance-scheme.html]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana (PMFBY),Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL MEWHAT ARE THE TAX BENEFITS FOR FARMERS UNDER THIS SCHEME?,This scheme has been exempted from the service tax.,[Reference:https://www.bajajallianz.com/blog/announcements/pradhan-mantri-fasal-bima-yojna-faqs.html]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana (PMFBY),Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL MEWHAT ARE THE PERILS COVERED FOR THE POST-HARVEST LOSS UNDER PMFBY SCHEME?,"Post-harvest yield loss is assessed on individual plot/farm occurring due to hailstorm, cyclone, cyclonic rains and unseasonal rainfall when the harvested crop is kept lying on the fields ""in cut and spread"" condition for drying of the crop up to 14 days from harvesting of the crop.",[Reference:https://www.bajajallianz.com/blog/announcements/pradhan-mantri-fasal-bima-yojna-faqs.html]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana (PMFBY),Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL MEWHEN IS THE RIGHT TIME TO ENROLL IN THE PRADHAN MANTRI BIMA FASAL YOJNA?,"All the enrolments under this scheme should be done before the cutoff date as mentioned in the State Government notification of every state. Also, the farmer should pay the share of his premium duly remitted by the Bank or Intermediary within the cutoff date to the Insurance Company. If there is a delay in enrolling and submitting the premium beyond the cutoff date, then the Insurance Company has the right to reject coverage",[Reference:https://www.bajajallianz.com/blog/announcements/pradhan-mantri-fasal-bima-yojna-faqs.html]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana (PMFBY),Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL MEWHAT SHOULD BE DONE IN CASE OF LOSSES INCURRED DUE TO PREVENTED SOWING?,"In case of loss due to prevented sowing, there is no need for the insured farmer to intimate the insurance company. This will be a widespread calamity and the assessment is based on area approach. This benefit is triggered when a majority of farmers are unable to sow their crop because of weather conditions.",[Reference:https://www.bajajallianz.com/blog/announcements/pradhan-mantri-fasal-bima-yojna-faqs.html]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana (PMFBY),Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL MEHOW CAN FARMERS INTIMATE ABOUT THE LOCALIZED LOSSES TO THE INSURANCE COMPANY?,Farmers may intimate the details of the loss within 72 hours of the calamity either to us or the concerned bank or local agriculture department/district officials. They can also reach us using the toll-free number 1800-209-5959.,[Reference:https://www.bajajallianz.com/blog/announcements/pradhan-mantri-fasal-bima-yojna-faqs.html]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana (PMFBY),Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL MEWHAT ARE THE RISKS COVERED UNDER PMFBY SCHEME?,"The Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojna scheme covers the following risks:

1.Prevented Sowing/Planting Risk
2.Standing Crop (Sowing to Harvesting)
3.Post-Harvest Losses
4.Localized Risk",[Reference:https://www.bajajallianz.com/blog/announcements/pradhan-mantri-fasal-bima-yojna-faqs.html]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana (PMFBY),Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME HOW IS THE SUM INSURED DECIDED FOR AN INDIVIDUAL FARMER?,"The formula for calculating the Sum Insured for an individual farmer under this scheme is:
Sum Insured = scale of finance per hectare * area of the notified crop by the farmers",[Reference:https://www.bajajallianz.com/blog/announcements/pradhan-mantri-fasal-bima-yojna-faqs.html]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana (PMFBY),Government Schemes,INFORMAITION REGARDING WHERE CAN FARMERS INSURE THEIR CROPS?,"Loanee farmers are compulsorily insured through the banks from where they avail their crop loan. Non-Loanee farmers can insure their crop either by visiting CSC centers or offices of insurance companies. Farmers can also approach banks or agents & brokers of insurance companies, or online on the farmer portal as well.",[Reference:https://www.bajajallianz.com/blog/announcements/pradhan-mantri-fasal-bima-yojna-faqs.html]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana (PMFBY),Government Schemes,INFORMAITION REGARDING WHICH FARMERS ARE ELIGIBLE FOR THIS SCHEME?,"Under the PMFBY and RWBCIS scheme, both Loanee and Non-Loanee farmers can be insured.",[Reference:https://www.bajajallianz.com/blog/announcements/pradhan-mantri-fasal-bima-yojna-faqs.html]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana (PMFBY),Government Schemes,INFORMAITION REGARDING WHO ARE LOANEE AND NON-LOANEE FARMERS?,"All the farmers who have availed loans from one or more financial institutions for Seasonal Agricultural Operations (SAO) of the notified crops are referred to as loanee farmers. Whereas, the farmers who have not availed any loan from any recognized financial institution are referred to as non-loanee farmers.",[Reference:https://www.bajajallianz.com/blog/announcements/pradhan-mantri-fasal-bima-yojna-faqs.html]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana (PMFBY),Government Schemes,INFORMAITION REGARDING WHICH CROPS ARE INSURED UNDER THESE SCHEMES?,"Following crops are insured under this scheme:

1.Food crops (Cereals, Vegetables, Pulses)
2.Oilseeds
3.Annual Commercial/ Annual Horticultural crops
",[Reference:https://www.bajajallianz.com/blog/announcements/pradhan-mantri-fasal-bima-yojna-faqs.html]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana (PMFBY),Government Schemes,INFORMAITION REGARDING WHAT ARE THE DIFFERENT COMPONENTS OF THE PMFBY SCHEME?,"The PMFBY scheme has two components, which provides coverage to the farmers (loanee & non-loanee):

1.Compulsory component: All the loanee farmers are compulsorily covered and provided insurance as per the provisions mentioned in the scheme.

2.Voluntary component: This component is optional for non-loanee farmers. The procedure to opt for this component is:

3.The farmers willing to avail this benefit should approach the nearest bank / authorized channel partner of the insurance company before the mentioned cutoff date.

4.They should fill-up the proposal form and provide the details of their saving bank account & land identification number with all the necessary documents.

5.The farmers will need to submit this form along with the premium amount to the bank/ authorized channel partner of the insurance company.",[Reference:https://www.bajajallianz.com/blog/announcements/pradhan-mantri-fasal-bima-yojna-faqs.html]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Kisan SAMPADA Yojana,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME PARDHAN MANTRI KISAN SAMPADA YOJANA?,"In 2017, the Cabinet Committee on Economic Affairs (CCEA) approved the central sector scheme SAMPADA (Scheme for Agro-Marine Processing and Development of Agro-Processing Clusters). Later, the Government renamed this scheme into ""Pradhan Mantri Kisan Sampada Yojana (PMKSY)"", which is implemented by the Ministry of Food Processing Industries (MoFPI). This piece talks about every important detail regarding the Pradhan Mantri Kisan Sampada Yojana. Read along!",[Reference:https://pmksy.gov.in/pdfLinks/FAQ.pdf]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Kisan SAMPADA Yojana,Government Schemes,"INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SCHEME IMPLEMENTED UNDER 
PARDHAN MANTRI KISAN SAMPADA YOJANA?","Schemes implemented under PMKSY:
1.Mega Food Parks
2.Integrated Cold Chain and Value Addition Infrastructure
3.Creation/ Expansion of Food Processing/ Preservation Capacities (Unit Scheme)
4.Infrastructure for Agro-processing Clusters
5.Creation of Backward and Forward Linkages
6.Food Safety and Quality Assurance Infrastructure
7.Human Resources and Institutions",[Reference:https://www.solutionbuggy.com/blog/pm-kisan-sampada-yojana-scheme-details-and-its-benefits/]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Kisan SAMPADA Yojana,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME PARDHAN MANTRI KISAN SAMPADA YOJANA BENEFITS?,"1.Formulated to expand cultivable area under assured irrigation, to reduce water wastage and to improve water use efficiency in agriculture.
2.Creating protective irrigation by harnessing rain water at micro level through Jal Sanchay and Jal Sinchan.
3.Implemented with an outlay of Rs. 50,000 crore in five years (2015 to 2020).
4.All the States and Union Territories including North Eastern States are covered under the programme.
5.The overreaching vision of PMKSY is to ensure access to some means of protective irrigation to all agricultural farms in the country, to produce drop more crops thus bringing much desired rural prosperity.",[Reference: www.apnikheti.com]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Kisan SAMPADA Yojana,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME PARDHAN MANTRI KISAN SAMPADA YOJANA REQUIRED DOCUMENTS?,"1.Applicant Aadhar Card
2.identity card
3.Housing Certificate
4.Farm papers
5.Bank Account Passbook
6.mobile number
7.Passport Size Photo",[Reference:https://www.squareyards.com/blog/pradhan-mantri-krishi-sinchai-yojana-pmksy-yojart]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Kisan SAMPADA Yojana,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME HOW TO APPLY PARDHAN MANTRI KISAN SAMPADA YOJANA?,"Step 1: Visit the official PMKSY portal.
Step 2: Click on the Login option on the homepage.
Step 3: In the next window, enter the credentials (username, password, and captcha code) that you use to log in to your account.
Step 4: After filling in all the credentials, click on login to access your account and apply.",[Reference:https://www.squareyards.com/blog/pradhan-mantri-krishi-sinchai-yojana-pmksy-yojart]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Kisan SAMPADA Yojana,Government Schemes,"INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME AS PER THE MODIFIED GUIDELINES NEW UNITS WILL BE ALLOCATED IN MEGA FOOD PARKS ASSISTED BY THE MINISTRY, WHETHER THE NEW UNITS TO BE SET UP IN AGRO FOOD PARKS, AGRO CLUSTERS OR AGRO INDUSTRIAL AREAS OF THE STATES ALSO WILL BE CONSIDERED ON THE SAME LINE UNDER THE SCHEME?","The new units from the proposals to be received against the EoI will be approved in the Mega Food Parks assisted by MoFPI; only, except for the States that do not have Mega Food Parks.",[Reference:https://www.mofpi.gov.in/sites/default/files/faqs_cefppc_1_0_0.pdf]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Kisan SAMPADA Yojana,Government Schemes,"INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME MY COMPANY IS TAKING A LAND ON LEASE FOR SETTING UP A FOOD PROCESSING UNIT, WHAT SHOULD BE THE MINIMUM LEASE PERIOD ACCEPTABLE TO AVAIL THE GRANT UNDER CEFPPC SCHEME?",Minimum lease of 15 years is required and registered lease deed on the name of applicant company need to be submitted with application.,[Reference:https://www.mofpi.gov.in/sites/default/files/faqs_cefppc_1_0_1.pdf]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Kisan SAMPADA Yojana,Government Schemes,"INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME THE LAND TAKEN FOR THE PROJECT HAS OWNERSHIP ON THE NAME OF ONE OF THE DIRECTOR/ PARTNER OF THE COMPANY, IS IT REQUIRED TO BE TRANSFERRED ON THE NAME OF APPLICANT COMPANY?","Yes, if the land is owned by one of the Director or partner of the company, then such a land need to be leased out on the name of the applicant firm for minimum of 15 years.",[Reference:https://www.mofpi.gov.in/sites/default/files/faqs_cefppc_1_0_2.pdf]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Kisan SAMPADA Yojana,Government Schemes,"INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME THE MEGA FOOD PARK PROMOTER HAS GIVEN ME THE PROVISIONAL ALLOTMENT LETTER FOR THE PLOT WHERE I INTEND TO SET UP MY FOOD PROCESSING UNIT, WHETHER I WILL BE ELIGIBLE FOR AVAILING PREFERENCE FOR MY PROJECT?","To avail preference for the project to be set up in Mega Food Park, Possession letter of the respective plot need to be submitted at time of application under the CEFPPC scheme.
",[Reference:https://www.mofpi.gov.in/sites/default/files/faqs_cefppc_1_0_3.pdf]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Kisan SAMPADA Yojana,Government Schemes,"INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SINCE THERE IS NO 100% SURETY FOR SANCTION OF GRANT TO OUR PROJECTS BECAUSE GRANT WILL BE SANCTIONED AS PER THE MERIT OF THE MARKINGS AND ALSO PREFERENCE WILL BE GIVEN TO UNITS IN MEGA FOOD PARKS, IN SUCH A SITUATION, WHETHER THE GRANT COMPONENT TO BE INDICATED IN
MEANS OF FINANCES OR SAME CAN BE SHOWN IN TERM LOAN?",The grant component required to be shown in the means of finances. Which can be shown as Unsecured loan in lieu of MoFPI grant or Bridge loan from bank in lieu of MoFPI Grant or Bank should clearly indicate in TL sanction order about Term loan component and Loan approved in lieu of MoFPI grant if sanctioned.,[Reference:https://www.mofpi.gov.in/sites/default/files/faqs_cefppc_1_0_4.pdf]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Kisan SAMPADA Yojana,Government Schemes,"INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME AS PER GUIDELINES IT IS MANDATORY TO BRING 20% PROMOTERS EQUITY IN CASE OF GENERAL AREAS AND 10% PROMOTER EQUITY IN CASE OF NER & DIFFICULT AREAS, WHETHER THE COST OF LAND WILL BE CONSIDERED UNDER THE PROMOTERS EQUITY?","No, the 20% or 10% promoter equity as the case may be required to be brought in the project excluding the land cost .",[Reference:https://www.mofpi.gov.in/sites/default/files/faqs_cefppc_1_0_5.pdf]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Kisan SAMPADA Yojana,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME DO I HAVE TO SUBMIT TECHNO ECONOMIC VIABILITY (TEV) REPORT ALONGWITH BANK APPRAISAL REPORT?,"If the Bank appraisal report has not indicated the financial benchmarks (i.e. IRR, DSCR,BEP, DER etc), SWOT analysis etc. in the Bank appraisal report then TEV report need to besubmitted duly authenticated by the respective bank.",[Reference:https://www.mofpi.gov.in/sites/default/files/faqs_cefppc_1_0_6.pdf]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Kisan SAMPADA Yojana,Government Schemes,"INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME AS SANCTION OF PROPOSALS TAKES TIME FROM BANK, MINISTRY MAY CONSIDER IN-PRINCIPLE SANCTION IN PLACE OF FINAL TERM LOAN SANCTION ORDER.?",As per the scheme guidelines applicant require to submit final term loan sanction order.,[Reference:https://www.mofpi.gov.in/sites/default/files/faqs_cefppc_1_0_7.pdf]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Kisan SAMPADA Yojana,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WHETHER THE TERM LOAN CAN BE AVAILED FROM COOPERATIVE BANKS?,"Term loan can be availed from any scheduled bank or financial institutions having core banking facilities. If the term loan sanctioning Bank/FI does not have core banking facility, in such a case an Escrow account need to be opened in the Bank having core banking facility and all the transactions for the applicant project need to be done through such Escrow account.",[Reference:https://www.mofpi.gov.in/sites/default/files/faqs_cefppc_1_0_8.pdf]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Kisan SAMPADA Yojana,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WHETHER THE 15% ALLOCATION FOR GRAIN MILLING SECTOR IS OUT OF STATE WISE QUOTA ALLOCATED TO THE RESPECTIVE STATE?,"The 15% allocation is nothing to do with the State wise projects allocated to respective States. For the grain milling sector, the 15% of the total allocated budget may be utilized each year for release of grant (Ref. para 2)",[Reference:https://www.mofpi.gov.in/sites/default/files/faqs_cefppc_1_0_9.pdf]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Kisan SAMPADA Yojana,Government Schemes,"INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME LOAN SANCTIONED TO THE FIRM AFTER EOI DATE BUT SOME OF THE EXPENDITURE ALREADY INCURRED ON THE PROJECT FROM THE PROMOTERS EQUITY, WHETHER SUCH EXPENDITURE WILL BE CONSIDERED UNDER ELIGIBLE PROJECT COST?","The expenditure incurred on the project before sanction of term loan will not be considered under the eligible project cost. However only, advances paid for plant and machinery and final billing/ invoices paid after sanction of the term loan then such total expenditure will be considered under eligible project cost.
",[Reference:https://www.mofpi.gov.in/sites/default/files/faqs_cefppc_1_0_10.pdf]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Kisan SAMPADA Yojana,Government Schemes,"INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WHETHER ELECTRICITY SUPPLY TRANSFORMER, SOLAR PANEL ETC. ARE THE ELIGIBLE COMPONENTS UNDER PROJECT COST?","The cost of transformer, solar panel etc. will be considered eligible component under utilities (para. 8.3 of guidelines).",[Reference:https://www.mofpi.gov.in/sites/default/files/faqs_cefppc_1_0_11.pdf]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Kisan SAMPADA Yojana,Government Schemes,"INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WHETHER THE TEMPERATURE CONTROLLED TRANSPORTS, COLD STORAGES FOR STORAGE OF RAW MATERIAL OR FINISHED PRODUCTS STORAGE ARE ALLOWED UNDER THE SCHEME? ","The cold storages required for the storage of raw material or finished products of the core processing unit are eligible under the scheme but standalone cold storages/ ware houses are not eligible under the CEFPPC scheme. Further the expenditure proposed for cold storages or
temperature controlled transports for existing units also will be considered eligible viz-a-viz processing capacity of the existing unit.
",[Reference:https://www.mofpi.gov.in/sites/default/files/faqs_cefppc_1_0_12.pdf]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Kisan SAMPADA Yojana,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WHETHER THE STAND ALONE IRRADIATION PROJECTS ARE ALLOWED UNDER THE SCHEME FOR PRESERVATION OF PRODUCTS?,"The stand alone irradiation projects will not be eligible. Standalone irradiation facility is covered under the Scheme of Cold Chain, Value Addition and Preservation Infrastructure.",[Reference:https://www.mofpi.gov.in/sites/default/files/faqs_cefppc_1_0_13.pdf]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Kisan SAMPADA Yojana,Government Schemes,"INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WHETHER THE INTEGRATED PROJECTS OF MUSHROOM, HONEY ARE ELIGIBLE UNDER THE SCHEME?","Under the integrated projects, only processing infrastructure will be considered under the scheme. For example, infrastructure facility required for Mushroom canning, mushroom powder etc. will be considered under the scheme but infrastructure for mushroom cultivation, mushroom pawn culture etc will not be considered under the scheme. Honey processing
facilities including packaging etc will be considered under the scheme but facilities created for bee keeping etc. will not be considered under the CEFPPC scheme.",[Reference:https://www.mofpi.gov.in/sites/default/files/faqs_cefppc_1_0_14.pdf]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Kisan SAMPADA Yojana,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WHETHER DOVETAILING OF ASSISTANCE IS ALLOWED UNDER THE CEFPPC SCHEME?,"Applicant firm may dovetail assistance available under various other schemes of other Central / State Governments, which would improve the viability of the project. While dovetailing such assistance, it will be ensured that there is no duplication of assistance for the same component/activity of the project.",[Reference:https://www.mofpi.gov.in/sites/default/files/faqs_cefppc_1_0_15.pdf]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Kisan SAMPADA Yojana,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME AS PER GUIDELINES MINIMUM PROJECT COST OF RS. 3 CRORE IS SUFFICIENT FOR ELIGIBILITY OF THE PROJECT?,"It is not the minimum project cost of Rs. 3 Crore. For eligibility of the project under the scheme, minimum eligible project cost (ref. para. 8.3 of guidelines) required to be of Rs. 3 Crore. (which includes cost of Plant & machinery, technical civil work and 25% cost of Utilities).",[Reference:https://www.mofpi.gov.in/sites/default/files/faqs_cefppc_1_0_16.pdf]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Kisan SAMPADA Yojana,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME HOW MUCH MONEY DID THE GOVERNMENT ALLOT FOR PRADHAN MANTRI KISAN SAMPADA YOJANA?,The Government allotted 6000 crores for Pradhan Mantri Kisan Sampada Yojana.,[Reference: https://www.godigit.com/guides/government-schemes/pm-kisan-sampada-yojana]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri Kisan SAMPADA Yojana,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME WHAT IS THE DURATION OF PRADHAN MANTRI KISAN SAMPADA YOJANA?,The duration of Pradhan Mantri Kisan Sampada Yojana is 2016-20 coterminous with the 14th Finance Commission cycle.,[Reference:https://www.godigit.com/guides/government-schemes/pm-kisan-sampada-yojana]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri KISAN Samman Nidhi Yojana,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME PRADHAN MANTRI KISAN SAMMAN NIDHI YOJANA?,"Pradhan Mantri Kisan Samman Nidhi (PM-KISAN) is a new Central Sector Scheme to provide income support to all landholding farmers' families in the country to supplement their financial needs for procuring various inputs related to agriculture and allied activities as well as domestic needs.

1.Under this scheme, an income support of Rs.6000/- per year in three equal instalments will be provided to small and marginal farmer families having combined land holding/ownership of upto 2 hectares
2.Definition of family for the scheme is husband, wife and minor children.
3.State Government and UT Administration will identify the farmer families which are eligible for support as per scheme guidelines.
4.The funds will be directly transferred to the bank accounts of the beneficiaries.
5.The revised Scheme is expected to cover around 2 crore more farmers, increasing the coverage of PM-KISAN to around 14.5 crore beneficiaries, with an estimated expenditure of Rs. 87,217.50 crores by Central Government for year 2019-20.
6.There are various Exclusion Categories for the scheme.",[Reference:https://pmkisan.gov.in/Documents/FAQPMKISAN.pdf]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri KISAN Samman Nidhi Yojana,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME PRADHAN MANTRI KISAN SAMMAN NIDHI YOJANA ELIGIBILITY?,"Eligibility:
All land holding eligible farmer families (subject to the prevalent exclusion criteria) are to avail of the benefits under this scheme.

The following categories of beneficiaries of higher economic status shall not be eligible for benefit under the scheme.

1.All Institutional Land holders.
2.Farmer families in which one or more of its members belong to following categories
 ->Farmer and present holders of constitutional posts
 ->Farmer and present Ministers/ State Ministers and former/present Members of LokSabha/ RajyaSabha/ State Legislative Assemblies/ State Legislative Councils,former and present Mayors of Municipal Corporations, former and present Chairpersons of District Panchayats.
 ->All serving or retired officers and employees of Central/ State Government Ministries /Offices/Departments and its field units Central or State PSEs and Attached offices /Autonomous Institutions under Government as well as regular employees of the Local Bodies (Excluding Multi Tasking Staff /Class IV/Group D employees)
 -> All superannuated/retired pensioners whose monthly pension is Rs.10,000/-or more (Excluding Multi Tasking Staff / Class IV/Group D employees) of above category
 -> All Persons who paid Income Tax in last assessment year
 -> Professionals like Doctors, Engineers, Lawyers, Chartered Accountants, and Architects registered with Professional bodies and carrying out profession by undertaking practices.
",[Reference:https://static.pib.gov.in/WriteReadData/specificdocs/documents/2021/nov/doc2021112361.pdf]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri KISAN Samman Nidhi Yojana,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME PRADHAN MANTRI KISAN SAMMAN NIDHI YOJANA BENEFITS?,"Benefits:
Under the PM-KISAN scheme, all landholding farmers' families shall be provided the financial benefit of Rs. 6000 per annum per family payable in three equal installments of Rs. 2000 each, every four months.

",[Reference:https://static.pib.gov.in/WriteReadData/specificdocs/documents/2021/nov/doc2021112362.pdf]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri KISAN Samman Nidhi Yojana,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME "HOW TO APPLY PRADHAN MANTRI KISAN SAMMAN NIDHI YOJANA"?,"How to apply:
1.Go to the official PM-Kisan website.
2.Scroll down to farmers Corner,and then click the new Farmer Registration button.
3.The page Farmer Registration Form will appear.
4.Enter the Aadhar number, mobile number, select the state and Captcha.
5.One time password OTP will be sent to your registered mobile number which is linked with your aadhar card.
6.Enter the Aadhar registered mobile OTP and then click the verify Aadhar OTP button.
7.A new registration page will open. Some of the details are automatically filled up from your aadhar card.
8.Enter your details like address, bank account details, land details and ration card number.
9.At the end upload the three documents land registration, aadhar card and bank passbook.
10.After that you have to make a payment, and after that you will get famer id.
11.So after the your pm kisan new registration is successfully completed.",[Reference:https://udyamregistrationform.com/pm-kisan/]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri KISAN Samman Nidhi Yojana,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME THAT THE INSTALLMENTS OF PRADHAN MANTRI KISAN SAMMAN NIDHI YOJANA AFTER RECEIVING FEW INSTALLMENTS?,"The GOI has started this scheme and the main purpose of which is to help the farmers only. Under this scheme, farmers are given Rs 6000 every year and this amount is given every year in 3 installments.",[Reference:https://www.sssamiti.org/pm-kisan-12th-installment-status-2022/]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri KISAN Samman Nidhi Yojana,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME THE SOLUTION IF THE REGISTRATION OF PRADHAN MANTRI KISAN SAMMAN NIDHI YOJANA IS REJECTED AT DISTRICT/ STATE LEVEL?,"If your Pradhan Mantri Kisan Samman Nidhi Yojana registration has been rejected at district or state level, contact your district nodal officer to know the reason and solution and at this time your Aadhaar Card, PAN Card, Bank Take the photo copy of the passbook and the deposit of the land","[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri KISAN Samman Nidhi Yojana,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME HOW TO CHECK THE STATUS OF PRADHAN MANTRI KISAN SAMMAN NIDHI YOJANA STATUS IF YOU REGISTERED FOR THIS SCHEME AND NOT RECEIVED ANY INSTALLMENT YET?,"If you have registered for Pradhan Mantri Kisan Samman Nidhi Yojana and have not received any installment yet, you can check your registration status with the help of Aadhaar card number by visiting https://pmkisan.gov.in/FarmerStatus.aspx. Here you will get to know whether your registration is done or not, if the registration is done then the installments can start coming after approval at the district and state level.","[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri KISAN Samman Nidhi Yojana,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL MEHOW TO REGISTERED FOR  PRADHAN MANTRI KISAN SAMMN NIDHI YOJANA?,For registration in Pradhan Mantri Kisan Samman Nidhi Yojana go to https://pmkisan.gov.in/ link or contact nodal officer.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri KISAN Samman Nidhi Yojana,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME THE HELPLINE NUMBER FOR PRADHAN MANTRI KISAN SAMMAN NIDHI YOJANA?,"For more information about Pradhan Mantri Kisan Samman Nidhi Yojana, contact its helpline number 011-24300606","[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri KISAN Samman Nidhi Yojana,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME THE IF BENEFICIARY IS INACTIVE DUE TO INELEGIBILITY OF PRADHAN MANTRI KISAN SAMMAN NIDHI YOJANA?,"Contact your nodal officer with attach copy of PAN card, Aadhaar card and bank passbook.","[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri KISAN Samman Nidhi Yojana,Government Schemes,"INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME HOW TO CHECK THE STATUS OF PRADHAN MANTRI KISAN SAMMN NIDHI YOJANA ACCOUNT
?",You can check your registration status with the help of Aadhaar card number by visiting https://pmkisan.gov.in/FarmerStatus.aspx,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri KISAN Samman Nidhi Yojana,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME THE INACTIVE STATUS OF PRADHAN MANTRI KISAN SAMMAN NIDHI YOJANA?,"If your status is showing Inactive in Pradhan Mantri Kisan Samman Nidhi Yojana then there are many reasons like death of beneficiary, transfer of land not in the name of beneficiary, not attaching land deposit at the time of registration, family Registration of 2 or more than 2 spouses, Beneficiary having a job or retired from a government job and receiving pension or paying income tax etc.","[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri KISAN Samman Nidhi Yojana,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME THE CORRECTION IN BANK ACCOUNT NUMBER FOR PRADHAN MANTRI KISAN SAMMAN NIDHI YOJANA?,"If the bank account number under Pradhan Mantri Kisan Samman Nidhi Yojana is wrong then contact your nodal officer and attach the copy of PAN card, Aadhaar card and bank passbook.","[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri KISAN Samman Nidhi Yojana,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME NECESSARY DOCUMENTS FOR THE PRADHAN MANTRI KISAN SAMMAN NIDHI YOJANA?,"When applying as a beneficiary for this scheme, individuals would need to submit the following documents:
1.Aadhaar Card
2.Proof of citizenship
3.Documents substantiating ownership of land
4.Details of bank account
**Individuals will need to provide scanned copies of such documents if they are registering online.",[Reference:https://groww.in/p/savings-schemes/pm-kisan-samman-nidhi-yojana]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri KISAN Samman Nidhi Yojana,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME HOW TO CHECK THE BENEFICIARY STATUS OF PM KISAN SCHEME.?,"GOI disburses the minimum income support amount of Rs.6000 a year in three instalments. In case an enlisted farmer did not receive the amount as per schedule, they can check such PM Kisan Samman Nidhi Yojana status online. 

Here are the steps to do so 
Step 1 -Visit PMKSNY official website.
Step 2 -Click on beneficiary Status under Farmers Corner.
Step 3 -Enter the Aadhaar number, registered mobile number, or account number.
Upon providing any of those aforementioned numbers, individuals can view the status of their receipt.
Individuals can also check whether they are included in their villages Beneficiary List for this scheme online, as well, via its portal. For that, one needs to follow these steps:

Step 1 - Click on the tab marked list of beneficiaries under Farmers Corner.

Step 2 -Select State, District and Sub-district, Block and Village, and click on Get Report.

One can then view the Pradhan Mantri Kisan Samman Nidhi Yojana list for a particular village. These are all that one needs to know about the schemes status. Individuals who have not yet enlisted can do so to receive the next instalment of Rs. 2000.",[Reference:https://groww.in/p/savings-schemes/pm-kisan-samman-nidhi-yojana]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri KISAN Samman Nidhi Yojana,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME FEATURES OF PM KISAN SAMMAN NIDHI YOJANA?,"1.Income Support
The primary feature of this Yojana is the minimum income support it provides to farmers. Each eligible farmer family is entitled to receive Rs.6000 per annum across India. However, the amount is not disbursed at once. Instead, it divided into three equal instalments and meted out four months apart. Each farmer, thus, receives Rs.2000 every 4 months. Beneficiaries can use this amount for numerous purposes. Pradhan Mantri Kisan Samman Nidhi Yojana guidelines do not categorically define any usage restriction. 

2.Funding
PMKSNY is an Indian government-sponsored farmer support scheme. Therefore, the entirety of its funding comes from the Government of India. Initially, it announced a reserve of Rs.75000 crore a year to be spent on this initiative. It disbursed Rs.17,000 crore in the latest instalment on 9th August 2020 to the scheme beneficiaries bank accounts via Direct Benefit Transfer or DBT. 

3.Identification Responsibility
While the responsibility of funding lies with GOI, the identification of beneficiaries is not under its purview. Instead, it the responsibility of the State and Union Territory governments. These governments shall identify which farmer families will benefit from the scheme. Here, it is crucial to note that per PM Kisan Samman Nidhi Yojana definition, a farmer's family shall comprise a husband, wife, and minor child or children.",[Reference:https://groww.in/p/savings-schemes/pm-kisan-samman-nidhi-yojana]
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri KISAN Samman Nidhi Yojana,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME HOW TO LINK AADHAAR CARD WITH PM KISAN SAMMAN NIDHI SCHEME?,"

1.Visit PM Kisan website.
2.Click on Farmers Corner.
3.Select New Farmer Registration.
4.Enter Aadhaar number
5.Enter details of the farmer like state, district, block, village, farmer type, account no.,mobile no., date of birth, ownership etc. in the specified fields. Ensure that all the details are correct.
","[Reference:https://www.tesz.in/ask/how-to-link-aadhaar-card-with-pm-kisan-samman-nidhi-scheme-nc1544](
Raju:
Answered on October 10,2019)"
Schemes,Pradhan Mantri KISAN Samman Nidhi Yojana,Government Schemes,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CHECK THE STATUS OF THE BENEFICIARY IN PM KISAN SAMMAN NIDHI YOJANA?,"1.Visit PM Kisan website.
