Oilseeds,Sesame,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME VARIETIES OF SESAME CROP?,"Varieties of Sesame Crop - Flowers Sesame No.1, Tapi, Padma, J.L.T. 408 are here.","[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Oilseeds,Sesame,Varieties,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SESAME?,"Sesame can be grown in all types of well-drained soil. Since sesame seeds are fine, the soil should be well prepared. For this, the waste should be removed and spread vertically and horizontally, the plateau should be rotated and flattened. Mix well rotted cow dung while preparing the soil. Seed For summer season four kg of seed per hectare should be used. Seed treatment Before sowing the seed should be treated with three grams of Carbendazim and four grams of Trichoderma per kg. This prevents soil borne diseases and improves seed germination. Sowing Sowing of summer sesame crop should be done in the first fortnight of February. If sowing is delayed, there is a fear that the crop will be caught in the pre-monsoon rains at harvest time. As the seeds are very fine, equal proportions of sand/sifted dung/ash/soil should be mixed. Tiffani should be sown at 30 cm.","[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Oilseeds,Sesame,Seeds,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME SESAME VARIETIES?,"Sesame varieties Phule Teel No.1, Tapi (JLT7), Padma (JLT26), JLT. 408","[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
