Fiber Crops,Cotton,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME CATERPILLAR ATTACK ON COTTON?,To manage the bollworm on cotton = Chlorpyrifos 30 ml / 15 liters of water should be sprayed.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Fiber Crops,Cotton,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME HARVESTING OF COTTON?,"The first harvest should be done when approximately 30 to 35 percent of the pods in the field have emerged, followed by 2 to 3 harvests generally at 15 to 20 day intervals. It is better to pick the cotton in the morning, because the moisture in the air separates the scum, bolls and worms and the husked cotton. Each type of cotton should be stored separately, after picking the cotton should be dried in the sun for 3-4 days and stored in a clean and dry place.","[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Fiber Crops,Cotton,Cultural Practices,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME RATOON OF COTTON CROP?,"Long-growing hybrid varieties of cotton are cultivated. More generations of pink bollworm are completed on these hybrids. As a result, the prevalence of this worm is found to be high. Due to the cultivation of different hybrid varieties of cotton, their flowering and boll time varies. Pink bollworms grow in numbers due to continuous food supply and intermingling of life cycles. Raw cotton is stored in ginning and commercial complexes for long periods of time. This creates a fertile environment for pink bollworms to emerge in the coming season. In pre-season planted (April-May) cotton, early pink bollworm infestation occurs as the flowering period occurs in June-July. Also, the life cycle of bollworm on cotton from the previous season is accompanied simultaneously. Alternatively, pink bollworm infestation is found in large numbers. Their immunity is also increasing.","[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
Fiber Crops,Cotton,Plant Protection,INFORMATION REGARDING/DETAILS ABOUT/TELL ME LARVAE CONTROL INFORMATION OF COTTON?,Spray Emamectin Benzoate 5% SC 7-8 g/pump for control of bollworms in cotton crop.,"[Reference: www.data.gov.in, Kisan Calling Center]"
